{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","prNumber":80,"prUrl":"https://github.com/BbrSofiane/email-os/pull/80","prRepository":"BbrSofiane/email-os","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:51:08.940Z"}
{"parentUuid":"11e8cf79-1a0e-4546-9df3-bc47c507a795","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011Ch7M5HhrpRs19Wh3kKP6Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The row's content is transparent, so the red underlay shows through behind the text and \"Mark done\" collides with the row's label. The tint also covers the whole row, and the children slide one by one instead of a solid panel moving, which is why the mid-swipe state looks broken.\n\nI'm checking the mid-swipe screenshot and noticing the sender text has slid far off while the other children are still overlapping. Subject and preview don't seem to move at all, which I suspect is because the snippet span uses `display: contents`, so its transform never applies. That would mean the swipe was already visually broken before, and I never caught it since I only looked at the final state.\n\nI'm weighing a CSS-only fix: move the row itself with the swipe offset and counter-translate the underlay, but the underlay sits inside the row's stacking context and would still paint over the row's opaque background, so the text would overlap the tint again.\n\nI'm sketching a way to make the underlay sit just outside the row's right edge, so it only shows in the strip the row leaves behind as it slides left. That way the tint is confined to the revealed area and can't sit behind the row's text. I'd still need to right-align the label within that strip so it stays readable.\n\nStill working out how the underlay should be sized and aligned in the revealed strip, with a separate distance variable so the label can sit at the trailing edge.\n\nI'm settling on moving the whole row with a transform and giving the underlay a `left: 100%` offset, so it only shows in the strip the row leaves behind. Since it sits outside the row box, the tint can no longer land behind the text, and I'm adding a side class so the underlay knows which edge to attach to.\n\nI'm now adding a `--swipe-distance` variable alongside the existing offset, so the underlay can size itself to the revealed strip. I also want assertions that check the underlay sits outside the row's subject area and that the subject actually moves by the swipe amount, which would have caught the `display: contents` problem.\n\nI'm making the underlay's width match the swipe distance, and I'm setting the row's background to an opaque surface color so the tint stays hidden behind it. The focused state currently sets the background to transparent, so I need to change that rule too. I'll write this up as item 14 and push the change to the existing PR branch for the list thread.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8433,"cache_read_input_tokens":305357,"output_tokens":4227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4227,"cache_read_input_tokens":305357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":26415,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7M5HFaJyWvV5QSdWYWB","requestRef":"795ec4ab-ec6e-45af-ad50-6ed3e242969d","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e97c167d-d7e8-4220-a85f-5c19d17d2f7e","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:51:36.128Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"e97c167d-d7e8-4220-a85f-5c19d17d2f7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011Ch7M5HhrpRs19Wh3kKP6Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mid-swipe screenshots reveal a defect present since the first round: the row text doesn't move as one piece, so the action label overlaps it. I'm sending the list thread a fix that slides the whole row as one panel.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8433,"cache_read_input_tokens":305357,"output_tokens":4227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4227,"cache_read_input_tokens":305357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch7M5HFaJyWvV5QSdWYWB","requestRef":"795ec4ab-ec6e-45af-ad50-6ed3e242969d","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"65e0cca2-c8e0-48a3-a20a-1ecb7b917675","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:51:36.143Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"65e0cca2-c8e0-48a3-a20a-1ecb7b917675","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011Ch7M5HhrpRs19Wh3kKP6Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016pFmMSy7hV4x9ugTKwxx8p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review && cat >> p5-list/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n- [ ] 14. The swipe is visually broken (seen in `swipe-done.png`, `swipe-done-armed.png`, `swipe-remind-armed.png`). Today each direct child of the row is translated separately and the row has no opaque background, with the underlay filling the whole row behind them. Result: the subject and preview do not move at all (their wrapper `.row-subject-snippet` is `display: contents`, so a transform on it does nothing), the tint shows through the whole row, and the label \"Mark done\" / \"Remind\" is drawn on top of the row's own text. Required behaviour: the whole row slides sideways as one opaque panel, and the action (tint, glyph, label) is visible only in the strip the row has uncovered. Implement it like this:\n  - `InboxList.vue`: next to `--swipe-offset` set `--swipe-distance` (the absolute value of the offset, in px) in the row's inline style. Give `.row-swipe-underlay` a side class: `from-end` when the row is being dragged left (the strip opens at the row's right edge) and `from-start` when dragged right. Keep the action classes `done` / `remind` and `armed`.\n  - `list.css`, replacing the per-child transform rule: the row itself moves: `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"] .inbox-row { transform: translateX(var(--swipe-offset, 0px)); transition: transform 160ms ease; background: var(--surface); }`, with `transition: none` while it has the class `swiping` (and during the one-frame reset from item 8), and inside the reduced-motion block. Remove the rule that transforms `.inbox-row > :not(.row-swipe-underlay)`. The rule `.inbox-row.focused:not(:focus-visible)` must set `background: var(--surface)` instead of `transparent`; the selected rule from item 2 still wins for selected rows.\n  - The underlay sits outside the row's box, in the uncovered strip, and travels with the row's edge: `.row-swipe-underlay { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: var(--swipe-distance, 0px); overflow: hidden; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding-inline: 16px; white-space: nowrap; z-index: auto; }`; `.row-swipe-underlay.from-end { left: 100%; justify-content: flex-end; }`; `.row-swipe-underlay.from-start { right: 100%; justify-content: flex-start; }`. Because its width is the uncovered distance, it exactly fills the strip between the row's edge and the list's edge. When the strip is narrower than the glyph plus label, the content is clipped (that is fine); set `padding-inline: 0` and `justify-content: center` while `--swipe-distance` is under 56px if you can express that simply, otherwise leave it clipped.\n  - The list scroller must clip horizontally so nothing causes a horizontal scrollbar while a row is offset (it already has `overflow-x: hidden`; verify with the no-horizontal-overflow assertion during a drag).\n  - Keep the colours and the armed state from item 7, and the exit from item 8 (at the end of the exit the row is fully out and the underlay fills the row's whole width).\n  Rendered assertions in `tests/layout/mobile-list.rendered.test.ts` at 412×915 and 360×800, with CDP touch input held mid-gesture: after an 80px left drag on the first row: the row's `.row-sender`, `.row-subject` and `.row-preview` have each moved 80px left (±1) from their resting x; the underlay's rectangle is `[row resting right − 80, row resting right]` (±1) and does not intersect the rectangle of `.row-subject` or `.row-preview`; the underlay's label is fully inside the underlay's rectangle once the drag reaches 60% of the width; `document.scrollingElement.scrollWidth` equals the viewport width. The same, mirrored, for an 80px right drag. After release below the threshold the row returns to its resting x. Update the item 7 assertion that read the row content's `transition-duration` to read the row's. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/browsing tests/layout`, `mobile-list.rendered.test.ts` and `mobile-reduced-motion.rendered.test.ts` pass; run the screenshots (this rewrites the three `swipe-*.png` files); then rerun the full rendered suite and push to the same branch (the pull request updates itself).\nEOF\necho done","description":"Append the swipe rendering fix item to the list checklist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8433,"cache_read_input_tokens":305357,"output_tokens":4227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4227,"cache_read_input_tokens":305357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13797,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016pFmMSy7hV4x9ugTKwxx8p":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review && cat >> p5-list/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n- [ ] 14. The swipe is visually broken (seen in `swipe-done.png`, `swipe-done-armed.png`, `swipe-remind-armed.png`). Today each direct child of the row is translated separately and the row has no opaque background, with the underlay filling the whole row behind them. Result: the subject and preview do not move at all (their wrapper `.row-subject-snippet` is `display: contents`, so a transform on it does nothing), the tint shows through the whole row, and the label \"Mark done\" / \"Remind\" is drawn on top of the row's own text. Required behaviour: the whole row slides sideways as one opaque panel, and the action (tint, glyph, label) is visible only in the strip the row has uncovered. Implement it like this:\n  - `InboxList.vue`: next to `--swipe-offset` set `--swipe-distance` (the absolute value of the offset, in px) in the row's inline style. Give `.row-swipe-underlay` a side class: `from-end` when the row is being dragged left (the strip opens at the row's right edge) and `from-start` when dragged right. Keep the action classes `done` / `remind` and `armed`.\n  - `list.css`, replacing the per-child transform rule: the row itself moves: `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"] .inbox-row { transform: translateX(var(--swipe-offset, 0px)); transition: transform 160ms ease; background: var(--surface); }`, with `transition: none` while it has the class `swiping` (and during the one-frame reset from item 8), and inside the reduced-motion block. Remove the rule that transforms `.inbox-row > :not(.row-swipe-underlay)`. The rule `.inbox-row.focused:not(:focus-visible)` must set `background: var(--surface)` instead of `transparent`; the selected rule from item 2 still wins for selected rows.\n  - The underlay sits outside the row's box, in the uncovered strip, and travels with the row's edge: `.row-swipe-underlay { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: var(--swipe-distance, 0px); overflow: hidden; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding-inline: 16px; white-space: nowrap; z-index: auto; }`; `.row-swipe-underlay.from-end { left: 100%; justify-content: flex-end; }`; `.row-swipe-underlay.from-start { right: 100%; justify-content: flex-start; }`. Because its width is the uncovered distance, it exactly fills the strip between the row's edge and the list's edge. When the strip is narrower than the glyph plus label, the content is clipped (that is fine); set `padding-inline: 0` and `justify-content: center` while `--swipe-distance` is under 56px if you can express that simply, otherwise leave it clipped.\n  - The list scroller must clip horizontally so nothing causes a horizontal scrollbar while a row is offset (it already has `overflow-x: hidden`; verify with the no-horizontal-overflow assertion during a drag).\n  - Keep the colours and the armed state from item 7, and the exit from item 8 (at the end of the exit the row is fully out and the underlay fills the row's whole width).\n  Rendered assertions in `tests/layout/mobile-list.rendered.test.ts` at 412×915 and 360×800, with CDP touch input held mid-gesture: after an 80px left drag on the first row: the row's `.row-sender`, `.row-subject` and `.row-preview` have each moved 80px left (±1) from their resting x; the underlay's rectangle is `[row resting right − 80, row resting right]` (±1) and does not intersect the rectangle of `.row-subject` or `.row-preview`; the underlay's label is fully inside the underlay's rectangle once the drag reaches 60% of the width; `document.scrollingElement.scrollWidth` equals the viewport width. The same, mirrored, for an 80px right drag. After release below the threshold the row returns to its resting x. Update the item 7 assertion that read the row content's `transition-duration` to read the row's. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/browsing tests/layout`, `mobile-list.rendered.test.ts` and `mobile-reduced-motion.rendered.test.ts` pass; run the screenshots (this rewrites the three `swipe-*.png` files); then rerun the full rendered suite and push to the same branch (the pull request updates itself).\nEOF\necho done","description":"Append the swipe rendering fix item to the list checklist"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch7M5HFaJyWvV5QSdWYWB","requestRef":"795ec4ab-ec6e-45af-ad50-6ed3e242969d","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d8b554a-cd4b-4c2a-ab5b-b36c977b8a79","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:51:49.941Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"high