{"parentUuid":"d284a1c2-21ec-4190-bf16-644105ec3138","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d1c44379-5cb0-4517-88ea-7d92f01f81a4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mjg49SrWenb8a3yG7E9p9M","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"additions\":343,\"body\":\"## What changed\\n\\n- Updated both compact editors to use one protected header X as the close action, with identical 48px buttons and 24px glyphs. Removed the compact footer close action while preserving the regular editor behavior.\\n- Standardized draft status copy to “never sent” and added phone keyboard attributes plus Enter-to-next-field behavior that respects IME composition.\\n- Improved compact editor failure-state ordering and retry styling, and documented the current editor behavior.\\n- Added the copy, collapse, contact, and prompt glyphs, corrected their uses in compact reader and drawer actions, and improved disabled and primary reader action contrast.\\n- Regenerated the mobile review screenshots.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Drafts remain local and unsent; no send path, reply-all, or forward was added.\\n- To and Cc remain text inputs so recipient text is preserved exactly. Enter advances only when not composing and no modifier is held.\\n- Compact editors close through the protected header X. The regular layout retains its existing footer behavior.\\n- Failure-state rendered assertions use a component test because the browser preview does not expose a failed-save control.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `pnpm typecheck` passed.\\n- `pnpm test`: 120 files passed, 1,969 tests passed.\\n- `pnpm build` passed.\\n- Full rendered suite: 12 files passed, 76 tests passed.\\n- Mobile screenshots: 4 cases passed.\\n- Compact compose rendered geometry: 2 tests passed at 41","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2d3db43d-5b2a-4437-9a12-47985cee6bcc","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:52:05.780Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"additions\":343,\"body\":\"## What changed\\n\\n- Updated both compact editors to use one protected header X as the close action, with identical 48px buttons and 24px glyphs. Removed the compact footer close action while preserving the regular editor behavior.\\n- Standardized draft status copy to “never sent” and added phone keyboard attributes plus Enter-to-next-field behavior that respects IME composition.\\n- Improved compact editor failure-state ordering and retry styling, and documented the current editor behavior.\\n- Added the copy, collapse, contact, and prompt glyphs, corrected their uses in compact reader and drawer actions, and improved disabled and primary reader action contrast.\\n- Regenerated the mobile review screenshots.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Drafts remain local and unsent; no send path, reply-all, or forward was added.\\n- To and Cc remain text inputs so recipient text is preserved exactly. Enter advances only when not composing and no modifier is held.\\n- Compact editors close through the protected header X. The regular layout retains its existing footer behavior.\\n- Failure-state rendered assertions use a component test because the browser preview does not expose a failed-save control.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `pnpm typecheck` passed.\\n- `pnpm test`: 120 files passed, 1,969 tests passed.\\n- `pnpm build` passed.\\n- Full rendered suite: 12 files passed, 76 tests passed.\\n- Mobile screenshots: 4 cases passed.\\n- Compact compose rendered geometry: 2 tests passed at 41","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d284a1c2-21ec-4190-bf16-644105ec3138","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"9ef664cce99d25dc84d7dd957397e53d756ebe5ef00f3138113d933e576f9acd","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing whether to merge #82 into integration now, since the editor PR is already reviewed and has screenshots, and the merge itself is cheap even with two threads running their own tests. I'll hold the heavy unit tests until everything is in, and I'm checking whether `gh pr merge 82 --merge` is the right command to use.\n\nI'd already settled on merging #82 into integration, since the review and screenshots are done. Checking whether `gh pr merge 82 --merge` is the right command now. I'll skip the gates for this merge, since PR #80's CI will run on push and verify it.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mjg49SrWenb8a3yG7E9p9M","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os && gh pr view 82 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus,additions,deletions,body | head -c 1500; echo; gh pr merge 82 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --merge --subject \"Merge pull request #82: Mobile critique fixes: editor exit, keyboard, glyphs\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Merge the editor fixes pull request into the mobile integration branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
