{"parentUuid":"68e9cf84-9e38-457d-b6ef-b7009db4dc83","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2d2c373a-627a-45ee-bc41-64626405cdb3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Read, Skill, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__t3-code__device_list, mcp__t3-code__device_open, mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request, mcp__t3-code__orchestrator_capabilities, mcp__t3-code__t3_background_wait, mcp__t3-code__t3_thread_launch, mcp__t3-code__t3_thread_list, mcp__t3-code__t3_thread_read, mcp__t3-code__t3_thread_send, mcp__t3-code__t3_thread_wait</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Earlier phase (complete):**\n     - Planned and managed GPT-6 Luna (high) threads that built a phone layout for the Email OS Android app, modelled on the owner's reference screenshots.\n     - Delivered a working version: branch `mobile/integration`, with PR #80 to `main` open for the owner to merge.\n   - **New request from the user:** \"Use subagents (Sonnet 5.5) to run impeccable critique and key screens\". I ran `/impeccable critique` with four Sonnet 5.5 design reviewers (list, reader, editors, secondary pages) and one Sonnet 5.5 detector agent. The combined score was 25/40. I then asked targeted questions.\n   - **User's answers:**\n     - Fix first: \"Selection and swipes\".\n     - Scope: \"All five issues (Recommended)\".\n     - Editor intent: \"Remove the \"Save and Close\" button and only use the X button and a fixed senstence\". My reading: on the phone the X is the only exit, and the fixed phrase is \"never sent\".\n     - Who builds: \"GPT-6 Luna threads\".\n   - **The goal now:** implement all five priority issues through Luna threads, then validate, merge into `mobile/integration`, rebuild the APK, check it on the emulator, update PR #80, and report. Re-running the critique for a new score is a natural close.\n   - **Standing constraints (verbatim or near-verbatim):**\n     - User CLAUDE.md: \"You are running in an exe.dev VM… Only use documented exe.dev features (see https://exe.dev/docs.md). Undocumented local endpoints are internal infrastructure—unstable and unsupported.\"\n     - The reference screenshots in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-refs/` contain the owner's private mail. Never copy them into the repo, commit them, upload them, or quote their content. Do not name the reference product in the product.\n     - No third-party names, logos or brand colours.\n     - Treat user information as private.\n     - Threads run on provider `codex`, model `gpt-6-luna`, `reasoningEffort: high`. Never switch the model unasked.\n     - My merge authority (my interpretation): I merge phase PRs into `mobile/integration`. I never merge to `main`; PR #80 is for the owner.\n     - Out of scope:\n       - calendar, AI/voice, send\n       - HTML bodies, label chips, multiple splits\n       - trash/spam/move, reply-all, forward\n     - Drafts stay local; there is no send path.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Stack:** Email OS is a Tauri 2 shell with a Vue 3 + TypeScript frontend and a Rust `mail-core`.\n   - **Compact layout:**\n     - Switched on at viewport width ≤719px via `useLayoutMode`, which sets `data-layout=\"compact\"` on `.app`.\n     - Compact CSS lives only in `src/assets/mobile/*.css`, scoped under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, with no `!important`.\n     - The desktop layout must not change.\n   - **Mobile building blocks:**\n     - `MobileTopBar`\n     - `MobileBottomBar`, with `contextHost` and `actionsHost`\n     - `MobileDrawer`\n     - `MobileActionSheet`\n     - `useSwipeAction`\n     - `useLongPressSelection`\n     - Escape ladder\n     - Android back bridge\n   - **Impeccable critique method:**\n     - Assessment A (design review) and Assessment B (detector) run as isolated subagents.\n     - Nielsen's 10 heuristics, scored 0–4 each.\n     - Issue severity P0–P3.\n     - A snapshot is persisted with `critique-storage write`.\n     - The launcher is `/home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable`.\n     - The detector needs `IMPECCABLE_BROWSER` set to the Chrome path.\n   - **Luna management pattern:**\n     - Each track has a `PROGRESS.md` checklist outside the repo, made of small items each with its own check.\n     - Protocol per item: tick, commit, push.\n     - I queue identical nudges: \"Continue with …PROGRESS.md: take the first unticked item…\".\n     - Review fixes are appended as extra items.\n     - This round Luna is much faster (several items per turn).\n   - **Rendered tests:**\n     - Harness: `tests/rendered/chromium.ts` (CDP, PHONE_VIEWPORT 412×915).\n     - Query inside `.workspace-panel:not([inert]) .app`.\n     - Screenshots: `mise run screenshots:mobile` with `EMAIL_OS_RENDERED_LAYOUT_CHROME=/tmp/chrome-rendered/chrome/linux-156.0.8078.80/chrome-linux64/chrome` and `EMAIL_OS_SCREENSHOT_DIR`.\n   - **Android build from a worktree:**\n     - Use the shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os/target` with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`.\n     - Copy `src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/dev/exedev/emailos/androidfixture/generated/*` from the root checkout first.\n     - Build command: `mise run android:build`.\n     - Emulator: device host `local`, id `emulator-5554`, package `dev.exedev.emailos.androidfixture`. Use the T3 device tools.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Critique outputs**\n     - The snapshot was written to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/.impeccable/critique/2026-11-16T07-24-15Z__src-assets-mobile.md`. It is not committed. Its metadata: score 25/40, p0 0, p1 3. It is the first run for slug `src-assets-mobile`.\n     - The detector found:\n       - Source scan: clean, except an advisory for an 8px radius in `FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115`.\n       - Rendered scans: `tight-leading` on `.row-preview` (1.25); `flat-type-hierarchy` in Settings; `text-occlusion` hits, mostly false positives.\n   - **Checklists (all under `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/`)**\n     - `p5-list/PROGRESS.md` (branch `mobile/p5-list`). Items:\n       1. branch\n       2. selected-row fill (`.inbox-row.selected, .inbox-row.selected.focused:not(:focus-visible){background: var(--focus-fill); box-shadow:none}`)\n       3. SelectionBar `compact` two-row structure\n       4. selection bar style\n       5. swipe `dragging` ref plus `swiping` class, `transition:none`\n       6. `armed` ref at 35% width\n       7. underlay colours (done = `color-mix(--focus-accent 38%, --surface)`; armed = `--focus-accent` with `--surface` text; remind = `--focus-fill`; armed remind = `color-mix(--text-secondary 45%, --surface)`)\n       8. row exits to the swipe side, with `exitsOnCommit` and a 160ms delayed commit\n       9. reduced-motion `@media` blocks plus a contract test plus `mobile-reduced-motion.rendered.test.ts`\n       10. swipe screenshots\n       11. docs\n       12. final and PR\n       13. hide `.selection-loaded-scope` in compact (review fix)\n       14. whole row slides as one opaque panel, with the underlay in the uncovered strip (review fix)\n       - All 14 are ticked.\n       - PR: https://github.com/BbrSofiane/email-os/pull/83\n     - `p5-editor/PROGRESS.md` (branch `mobile/p5-editor`). Items:\n       1. branch\n       2. \"· never sent\" phrase\n       3. To and Cc inputs get `inputmode=\"email\" autocapitalize=\"none\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" enterkeyhint=\"next\"`, plus Enter moves to the next field\n       4. compact editor: X is the only exit, the footer has no `close-composer`, and the header slot passes `closeDisabled`\n       5. failure state: retry above the fields, bordered\n       6. glyphs `copy`, `collapse`, `contact`, `prompt` in `HeaderGlyph.vue`\n       7. glyph uses: Collapse→collapse, Copy text→copy, Contact details→contact, Commands→prompt (compact only)\n       8. done button gets the `--focus-accent` colour; disabled buttons get `opacity:1; color: var(--icon-muted)`\n       9. screenshots\n       10. docs\n       11. final\n       12. both X buttons 48px with a 24px glyph (review fix)\n       - All are ticked. PR #82 is MERGED into `mobile/integration` at 6d03b3a.\n       - PR #82 reported 1,969 unit tests in 120 files and 76 rendered tests.\n     - `p5-pages/PROGRESS.md` (branch `mobile/p5-pages`):\n       - Rule: destinations show the menu button; pushed pages (Settings, Activity, Account, Provider mail, Contact) show Back. No X or \"Close\" in page headers.\n       - Items:\n         1. branch\n         2. Back header markup (`mobile-round-button page-back`, `data-test=\"drawer-close\"` / `contact-disclosure-close`)\n         3. Back header aligned with the top bar\n         4. Settings hierarchy and grouping\n         5. ReminderSettings `compact`: immediate save, no Save/Cancel, note in `<details>`\n         6. Search page: context slot empty, Search tab current\n         7. search results on one left edge\n         8. search syntax in `<details>`\n         9. Reminders status first, zero tab counts hidden, Activity explanation line\n         10. screenshots\n         11. docs\n         12. final and PR\n       - Items 1–3 were ticked at the last check; 5 nudges are queued.\n       - Item 3 decision: \"anchored pushed pages below the 24px phone status inset so the shared header button aligns with the destination top bar.\"\n   - **Scratchpad helper:** `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad/p5.sh`. It prints ticks, the branch, commits ahead, dirty state, and the decision lines for the list, editor and pages tracks. It maps the tracks to worktrees `mobile-p2-list-*`, `mobile-p2-reader-*` and `mobile-p3-pages-*`.\n   - **Merged swipe CSS** in `src/assets/mobile/list.css`, as seen after the local merge:\n     ```css\n     .app[data-layout=\"compact\"] .row-swipe-underlay { position:absolute; z-index:auto; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; padding-inline:16px; top:0; bottom:0; width:var(--swipe-distance,0px); overflow:hidden; white-space:nowrap; color:var(--text-primary); transition: background-color 120ms ease-out, color 120ms ease-out, transform 120ms ease-out; }\n     .row-swipe-underlay.from-end { left:100%; justify-content:flex-end; }\n     .row-swipe-underlay.from-start { right:100%; justify-content:flex-start; }\n     .remind {background: var(--focus-fill)} .done {background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--focus-accent) 38%, var(--surface))}\n     .done.armed {background: var(--focus-accent); color: var(--surface)} .remind.armed {background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-secondary) 45%, var(--surface))}\n     .row-swipe-icon {40x40, transparent} svg 24px; armed svg scale(1.15); armed label weight 600\n     @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .inbox-row, .row-swipe-underlay, .row-swipe-icon svg { transition: none } }\n     ```\n     `InboxList.vue` sets `from-end` when `revealed === 'left'` and `from-start` when `revealed === 'right'`.\n   - **Memory:** `/home/exedev/.claude/projects/-home-exedev-email-os/memory/mobile-layout-programme.md`. I appended a \"Round 2, started 2026-11-16 ~21:30 UTC (critique fixes)\" block with:\n     - the owner's answers\n     - the three tracks and their threads and branches\n     - the plan after the tracks\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Critique reviewer claims checked against code and screenshots:**\n     - The \"two stacked sheets\" in `reader-more-sheet.png` turned out to be a screenshot-script artifact, now fixed in editor item 9.\n     - `06-reply-keyboard.png` is my accidental capture of Android Settings; it is not in the repo.\n     - I corrected my earlier hand-over: the reply-unavailable case also shows \"Save not confirmed\" and several exits.\n   - **Detector couldn't find a browser:** fixed by setting `IMPECCABLE_BROWSER`. Headless Chrome then gave a 500px viewport, which was still compact.\n   - **First swipe screenshots were broken:**\n     - Symptom: subject and preview did not move (they sit in a `display: contents` wrapper) and the label overlapped the row text.\n     - Fix: added list item 14 (the whole row translates with an opaque `var(--surface)` background, and the underlay sits in the uncovered strip using `--swipe-distance`).\n     - The new screenshots are verified correct.\n   - **Selection scope truncated** (\"1 selected · 18 lo…\"): list item 13 hides `.selection-loaded-scope` in compact.\n   - **Mismatched X sizes:** the reply X glyph was 16px against 24px in compose. Editor item 12 fixed it.\n   - **Tool use:** `gh pr checks` needs `-R BbrSofiane/email-os`. CI on 645d731 (PR #80) is green.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Done:**\n     - Critique delivered and the snapshot persisted.\n     - Editor/glyph fixes merged (PR #82).\n     - List fixes complete and screenshots verified (PR #83 open).\n   - **Verified screenshots:**\n     - `selection.png`: selected row fill, two-row pill with X, \"1 selected\", filled \"Mark 1 done\", and \"Mark read / Mark unread / Select all (18)\".\n     - `compose.png` and `reply.png`: X only, footer shows \"Discard…\", status \"… · never sent\".\n     - Reader pill: accent on the done glyph.\n     - Glyphs: copy, collapse, person, prompt.\n     - `reader-more-sheet.png`: a single sheet.\n     - Swipe screenshots after item 14: correct.\n   - **Remaining:**\n     - The pages track.\n     - Integration gates, the Android build and emulator check.\n     - Update PR #80.\n     - Re-run the critique.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Use subagents (Sonnet 5.5) to run impeccable critique and key screens\"\n   - Answers to my questions:\n     - \"Selection and swipes\"\n     - \"All five issues (Recommended)\"\n     - \"Remove the \"Save and Close\" button and only use the X button and a fixed senstence\"\n     - \"GPT-6 Luna threads\"\n   - \"Continue\"\n   - Earlier phase, for context:\n     - the Tailwind question\n     - \"Wouldn't tailwind give us a more robust UI system across the board?\"\n     - \"Ok sounds good, let's focus on the work for mobile… plan the work required to implement these\"\n     - \"OK, I've pulled the latest main locally. 1. Yes, the calendar and AI functionality are out of scope… 2. Yep sounds good, levave them out 3. Good call - let's leave it empty for now I want you to go ahead and manage threads (GPT-6-LUNA high) to implement against the plan you have. Make sure to validate with screenshots where applicable and continue until you have a working version for me test out\"\n     - \"Continue where you left off.\" (several times)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Merge PR #83 into `mobile/integration`.\n   - Drive the pages track (thread `mcp:launch:8aabfbb166f97f301710f04e10311dff2916e8927a63357130ed5c98b354c9f3`, branch `mobile/p5-pages`) to completion:\n     - Review its screenshots in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages/`.\n     - Add review-fix items if needed.\n     - Merge its PR into `mobile/integration` and link it with `link_pull_request`.\n   - On the merged integration branch, in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate`:\n     - Run `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite and the screenshots.\n     - Build the Android APK and check it on the emulator (selection, swipes, editor X, pages).\n   - Update PR #80's description with the round-2 changes and check CI.\n   - Optionally re-run the critique for a new score.\n   - Report to the user. The report should note that the save-state words stay truthful (for example \"Saved in preview memory (non-durable) · never sent\" in the browser build).\n   - Keep the memory file up to date.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Just before the summary, I updated my validation checkout and merged the list branch locally:\n     ```\n     cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q --ff-only origin/mobile/integration && git merge --no-ff origin/mobile/p5-list -m \"Merge pull request #83: Mobile critique fixes: selection and swipes\"\n     ```\n     - The fast-forward reached 6d03b3a (the PR #82 merge).\n     - The no-ff merge of p5-list succeeded locally (17 files, +781/−44) and is NOT pushed.\n   - I then read the merged swipe CSS and InboxList markup (shown above) to confirm item 14 landed correctly. It did.\n   - The pages track thread is running with 5 queued \"Continue with …p5-pages/PROGRESS.md\" nudges (clientRequestIds p5p-n1 to n5).\n   - PRs #82 and #83 are linked to this thread.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Merge PR #83 on GitHub rather than pushing the local merge: `gh pr merge 83 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --merge --subject \"Merge pull request #83: Mobile critique fixes: selection and swipes\"`. Then reset the validation checkout to `origin/mobile/integration` (`git fetch && git reset --hard origin/mobile/integration`, after confirming nothing else is local).\n   - Then wait on the pages thread with `t3_thread_wait` (timeout about 600000), check progress with the `p5.sh` helper, review its screenshots, and continue the plan:\n     - merge the pages PR\n     - full gates\n     - APK build and emulator check\n     - update PR #80\n     - report\n   - This follows the user's selections: \"All five issues (Recommended)\" with \"GPT-6 Luna threads\", and \"Selection and swipes\" first (now done).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/exedev/.claude/projects/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"c19612e3-6d3e-4a1b-ab2a-fb72700ead06","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:01:59.132Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":10},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
