{"parentUuid":"492e719a-f251-422c-9c79-abb8bffc9ee4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list/PROGRESS.md","displayPath":"../email-os-mobile-review/p5-list/PROGRESS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"943c8844-a69e-40dc-8172-3cf483de4182","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:01:59.353Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list/PROGRESS.md was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"943c8844-a69e-40dc-8172-3cf483de4182","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-editor/PROGRESS.md","displayPath":"../email-os-mobile-review/p5-editor/PROGRESS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6be7f312-9fad-492a-a1fe-85b6a1736da6","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:01:59.353Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-editor/PROGRESS.md was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"6be7f312-9fad-492a-a1fe-85b6a1736da6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/exedev/.claude/projects/-home-exedev-email-os/memory/mobile-layout-programme.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/exedev/.claude/projects/-home-exedev-email-os/memory/mobile-layout-programme.md","content":"---\nname: mobile-layout-programme\ndescription: \"Email OS phone layout (Android) that I coordinate via GPT-6 Luna (high) threads; scope decisions, branch scheme, phases, validation setup\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b\n  modified: 2026-11-16T21:17:32.469Z\n---\n\nStarted 2026-11-15. The owner asked me to plan and then \"manage threads (GPT-6-LUNA high)\" to implement a phone layout modelled on a reference mail app's screenshots, validate with screenshots, and \"continue until you have a working version for me to test out\". Follows on from [[maintenance-programme]] (closed).\n\n**Threads:** `t3_thread_launch`, provider/instance `codex`, model `gpt-6-luna`, option `reasoningEffort: high`, runtime full-access, worktree from `origin/mobile/integration`.\n\n**Owner decisions (2026-11-15):**\n- No Tailwind migration (my recommendation, accepted). Compact CSS goes in `src/assets/mobile/*.css` scoped under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`.\n- UI only over existing features. Out of scope: calendar, AI/voice, send, HTML bodies, label chips, multiple splits, trash/spam/move, reply-all, forward. Inbox zero = plain empty state, no photo.\n\n**Merge authority (my interpretation, not stated by the owner):** phase PRs target the branch `mobile/integration`; I review, gate and merge them into that branch. I do NOT merge to `main`; a PR `mobile/integration` → `main` is for the owner (and gives CI + the APK artifact, since CI only runs on PRs based on main).\n\n**Reference screenshots:** `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-refs/01..10-*.jpg`. They contain the owner's private mail: never commit or upload them.\n\n**Phases:** P1 foundations + shell frame (layout mode `useLayoutMode`, tokens, top bar/bottom bar, system bars, Back, rendered harness at 412×915) → then two parallel tracks: list (rows, split pill, drawer, swipes, long-press selection) and reader (bottom action bar, overflow sheet, message menu, undo toast, full-screen compose + keyboard) → remaining surfaces (search, reminders, drafts, account, activity, provider mail) + settings → my integrated emulator validation and APK for the owner.\n\n**Validation setup:** emulator device host `local`, id `emulator-5554` (t3-pixel, Android 15, 1080×2400), package `dev.exedev.emailos.androidfixture`; use T3 device tools. Chrome for rendered tests: `/tmp/chrome-rendered/chrome/linux-156.0.8078.80/chrome-linux64/chrome`. Machine: 4 cores, 15 GB, ~10 GB free disk; shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os/target`, `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`, one heavy command at a time, at most two threads.\n\n**State 2026-11-15 15:25 UTC:** `mobile/integration` pushed at f605bc1 (= main). P1 thread running: `mcp:launch:d2dfe6e91811e8a341ba49fc84e906bc3c3c0ea764a10fefbf3b39acd487c70d`, branch `mobile/p1-foundations`.\n\n**How GPT-6 Luna (high) behaves here (learned 2026-11-15, 15:25–16:15 UTC):** turns are short (seconds to ~4 min); it stops and reports \"not complete\" on a large step, stops right after `view_image`, tries the repo's `implement` skill (which wants a feature-engineer agent) and gives up at the first obstacle. Queued big steps burn as no-op turns. What works: a checklist file outside the repo (`/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p2-<track>/PROGRESS.md`, ~16–19 small items, each with its own check, \"tick, commit, push\") plus identical queued nudges (\"Continue with PROGRESS.md: first unticked item…\"), about one item per turn. Always tell it: no `implement` skill, no delegation, no `view_image`, no cargo/Android builds, code style (it writes minified one-liners unless told), retry pushes (remote pack errors are transient). I do the visual review (screenshots via `mise run screenshots:mobile`, test `tests/layout/mobile-screenshots.rendered.test.ts`, which I wrote) and all Android builds.\n\n**Android build from a worktree:** the shared cargo target does not regenerate Tauri's Kotlin sources in a new worktree; copy `src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/dev/exedev/emailos/androidfixture/generated/*` from the root checkout first (`cp -n`). My build checkout: `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate` (worktree, detached). Build ~35–90 s: `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os/target CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 mise run android:build`. The emulator's app was a CI-signed APK; I backed up its data to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/emulator-appdata-before-local-apk-2026-11-15.tar`, uninstalled it and installed the locally signed build. One hang at \"Checking the demo mailbox…\" on the first launch right after install (not reproduced after `pm clear`); retest before handing over.\n\n**State 2026-11-15 16:15 UTC:** P1 merged into `mobile/integration` (PR #75 + my fix commit + context-host prep; head 58ca5a9): layout mode, tokens, top bar, bottom bar with `backHost`/`actionsHost`/`contextHost`, dark system bars, Back via `window.__emailOsAndroidBack`, rendered tests 53/53, unit 1,909. Verified on the emulator: bars, compact frame, Back closes reader then backgrounds. Running: list track `mcp:launch:e4c090dc6cc0fc8fafd367a73aee4d879ff1b6b411e9c31b163528aa6b7a5491` (branch `mobile/p2-list`) and reader track `mcp:launch:817c514889e48621ca24bb86808f079e535512c3aaed7c31b2ee5b1be2475a7c` (branch `mobile/p2-reader`), both on checklists. After them: remaining surfaces (search, reminders, drafts, account/activity/provider mail pages, settings with swipe prefs), then integrated APK for the owner.\n\n**State 2026-11-15 20:45 UTC:** `mobile/integration` = a574927: P1 + list track (PR #77: stacked rows, split pill, navigation drawer `MobileDrawer.vue`, swipes `useSwipeAction.ts`, long-press selection) + reader track (PR #76: compact reader toolbar with star/more, `MobileActionSheet.vue`, reply bar, per-message menu, toast, compose sheet), merged by me with conflicts resolved (App.vue, main.ts, css-contract, HeaderGlyph, mise.toml, DESIGN.md). Merged tree: unit 1,947 in 116 files, rendered 67/67, build OK. Emulator check of a574927 (local APK): rows, swipe-left done + Undo, swipe-right reminder picker, reader, Back all work with real touch; real keyboard (Gboard) resizes the WebView correctly. Running: fix round in the old reader thread `mcp:launch:817c5148…` on branch `mobile/p2-fixes` (checklist `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p2-fixes/PROGRESS.md`, 12 items: reply/compose sheets must cover the app, focused-row date, selection checkboxes and bar, nav pill background, keyboard-height case) and pages track `mcp:launch:8aabfbb166f97f301710f04e10311dff2916e8927a63357130ed5c98b354c9f3` on `mobile/p3-pages` (checklist `…/p3-pages/PROGRESS.md`, 15 items: drafts, reminders, picker sheet, search, utility pages, palette, contact, swipe preferences, settings). After both: merge into integration, full gates, APK, emulator pass, open PR `mobile/integration` → `main` for the owner, hand over the APK path.\n- Emulator IME: I switched the default input method from the device tool's hidden helper (`com.callstack.agentdevice.imehelper/.TestInputMethodService`) to Gboard with `adb shell ime set` to see the real keyboard. Restore the helper when validation is finished.\n- `agent-device` tips: `gesture pan <x> <y> <dx> <dy> <ms>` in device pixels does a real swipe; `press <x> <y>` taps; a programmatic focus does not raise the keyboard, a tap does.\n\n**State 2026-11-16 01:35 UTC: FIRST WORKING VERSION DELIVERED.** `mobile/integration` = 645d731 (P1 #75, list #77, reader #76, fixes #78, pages #79, polish #81, plus my merges, a typecheck fix and a docs commit with emulator screenshots in `docs/validation/mobile/`). PR #80 `mobile/integration` → `main` is open and ready for review; the owner merges it (I do not). Unit 1,959 in 118 files, rendered 76/76, build OK, CI `check` + `android-apk` green on b7b2637 (645d731 is docs-only on top). Emulator has the locally built APK of b7b2637 installed (fresh install, fixture data, one draft); IME restored to the device tool's helper; airplane mode, which a stray tap of mine had turned on, is off again. No threads running.\n- Open items reported to the owner, not fixed: first launch right after a fresh install can ANR (pre-existing since #63; relaunch is fine); Contact page header still says \"Close\" as text; \"Contact details\" row uses the menu glyph; no physical-device test; I reviewed by tests, screenshots and device, and spot-read the code, not every line.\n- Lesson: before coordinate taps or `back` on the emulator, confirm the app is in the foreground (snapshot shows the webview title). `back` at the app root backgrounds it and the next taps land on whatever is behind (they landed in Android Settings).\n**Round 2, started 2026-11-16 ~21:30 UTC (critique fixes).** The owner asked for an Impeccable critique of the key phone screens run by Sonnet 5.5 subagents; result 25/40 (snapshot in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/.impeccable/critique/2026-11-16T07-24-15Z__src-assets-mobile.md`, not committed). Owner's answers: fix selection and swipes first; scope = all five priority issues, not the minor ones; editor = \"Remove the Save and Close button and only use the X button and a fixed sentence\" (my reading: X is the only exit on the phone, \"never sent\" is the fixed phrase, save-state words stay truthful); builders = GPT-6 Luna threads again. CI on 645d731 is green.\n- Three tracks reuse the old Luna threads and worktrees on new branches from `origin/mobile/integration`, with checklists in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-{list,editor,pages}/PROGRESS.md`: list thread (`mcp:launch:e4c090dc…`) → `mobile/p5-list` (selected-row fill, two-row selection bar, swipe tracking/armed state/row exit, reduced motion); reader thread (`mcp:launch:817c5148…`) → `mobile/p5-editor` (\"never sent\", phone keyboard attributes, X-only exit, failure state, new glyphs copy/collapse/contact/prompt, accent on done); pages thread (`mcp:launch:8aabfbb1…`) → `mobile/p5-pages` (Back header on pushed pages, Settings hierarchy and immediate save, search insets, syntax disclosure), started only after one of the first two finishes (two-thread limit).\n- After the tracks: I review screenshots (`p5-*/` dirs), merge PRs into `mobile/integration`, run gates, rebuild the APK, check on the emulator, update PR #80, re-run the critique for the score. Progress helper: `scratchpad/p5.sh` of session 415cd333.\n- Review directories: `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/` (`final/` browser screenshots, `final-android/` emulator screenshots, per-track `PROGRESS.md` checklists).\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"displayPath":"../.claude/projects/-home-exedev-email-os/memory/mobile-layout-programme.md","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"65918ca8-767d-4881-abcf-3e73c425a0d2","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:01:59.354Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/home/exedev/.claude/projects/-home-exedev-email-os/memory/mobile-layout-programme.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tname: mobile-layout-programme\n3\tdescription: \"Email OS phone layout (Android) that I coordinate via GPT-6 Luna (high) threads; scope decisions, branch scheme, phases, validation setup\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-16T21:17:32.469Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tStarted 2026-11-15. The owner asked me to plan and then \"manage threads (GPT-6-LUNA high)\" to implement a phone layout modelled on a reference mail app's screenshots