e, selection checkboxes and bar, nav pill background, keyboard-height case) and pages track `mcp:launch:8aabfbb166f97f301710f04e10311dff2916e8927a63357130ed5c98b354c9f3` on `mobile/p3-pages` (checklist `…/p3-pages/PROGRESS.md`, 15 items: drafts, reminders, picker sheet, search, utility pages, palette, contact, swipe preferences, settings). After both: merge into integration, full gates, APK, emulator pass, open PR `mobile/integration` → `main` for the owner, hand over the APK path.\n36\t- Emulator IME: I switched the default input method from the device tool's hidden helper (`com.callstack.agentdevice.imehelper/.TestInputMethodService`) to Gboard with `adb shell ime set` to see the real keyboard. Restore the helper when validation is finished.\n37\t- `agent-device` tips: `gesture pan <x> <y> <dx> <dy> <ms>` in device pixels does a real swipe; `press <x> <y>` taps; a programmatic focus does not raise the keyboard, a tap does.\n38\t\n39\t**State 2026-11-16 01:35 UTC: FIRST WORKING VERSION DELIVERED.** `mobile/integration` = 645d731 (P1 #75, list #77, reader #76, fixes #78, pages #79, polish #81, plus my merges, a typecheck fix and a docs commit with emulator screenshots in `docs/validation/mobile/`). PR #80 `mobile/integration` → `main` is open and ready for review; the owner merges it (I do not). Unit 1,959 in 118 files, rendered 76/76, build OK, CI `check` + `android-apk` green on b7b2637 (645d731 is docs-only on top). Emulator has the locally built APK of b7b2637 installed (fresh install, fixture data, one draft); IME restored to the device tool's helper; airplane mode, which a stray tap of mine had turned on, is off again. No threads running.\n40\t- Open items reported to the owner, not fixed: first launch right after a fresh install can ANR (pre-existing since #63; relaunch is fine); Contact page header still says \"Close\" as text; \"Contact details\" row uses the menu glyph; no physical-device test; I reviewed by tests, screenshots and device, and spot-read the code, not every line.\n41\t- Lesson: before coordinate taps or `back` on the emulator, confirm the app is in the foreground (snapshot shows the webview title). `back` at the app root backgrounds it and the next taps land on whatever is behind (they landed in Android Settings).\n42\t**Round 2, started 2026-11-16 ~21:30 UTC (critique fixes).** The owner asked for an Impeccable critique of the key phone screens run by Sonnet 5.5 subagents; result 25/40 (snapshot in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/.impeccable/critique/2026-11-16T07-24-15Z__src-assets-mobile.md`, not committed). Owner's answers: fix selection and swipes first; scope = all five priority issues, not the minor ones; editor = \"Remove the Save and Close button and only use the X button and a fixed sentence\" (my reading: X is the only exit on the phone, \"never sent\" is the fixed phrase, save-state words stay truthful); builders = GPT-6 Luna threads again. CI on 645d731 is green.\n43\t- Three tracks reuse the old Luna threads and worktrees on new branches from `origin/mobile/integration`, with checklists in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-{list,editor,pages}/PROGRESS.md`: list thread (`mcp:launch:e4c090dc…`) → `mobile/p5-list` (selected-row fill, two-row selection bar, swipe tracking/armed state/row exit, reduced motion); reader thread (`mcp:launch:817c5148…`) → `mobile/p5-editor` (\"never sent\", phone keyboard attributes, X-only exit, failure state, new glyphs copy/collapse/contact/prompt, accent on done); pages thread (`mcp:launch:8aabfbb1…`) → `mobile/p5-pages` (Back header on pushed pages, Settings hierarchy and immediate save, search insets, syntax disclosure), started only after one of the first two finishes (two-thread limit).\n44\t- After the tracks: I review screenshots (`p5-*/` dirs), merge PRs into `mobile/integration`, run gates, rebuild the APK, check on the emulator, update PR #80, re-run the critique for the score. Progress helper: `scratchpad/p5.sh` of session 415cd333.\n45\t- Review directories: `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/` (`final/` browser screenshots, `final-android/` emulator screenshots, per-track `PROGRESS.md` checklists).\n46\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
