{"parentUuid":"bba973ba-3677-4d31-ac0e-b0fa12c502af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e22c7f1c-f691-48a9-98f7-fb97a3ff056f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DQPLhC62mk4LEkSWji888h","type":"tool_result","content":"92b98c4 Merge pull request #83: Mobile critique fixes: selection and swipes\n  Decision: hide the empty swipe-settings live region with `:empty` while keeping it mounted.\n\n- [x] 5. Settings: one save model. The swipe options save at once; the reminder time has Save and Cancel, and Save closes the page. On the phone both must save at once. `src/components/ReminderSettings.vue` gets a `compact?: boolean` prop (passed from `App.vue` as `layoutMode === 'compact'`). When `compact` is true: there are no Save and Cancel buttons; changing the Hour or the Minute select saves immediately through the same function the form submit uses, emits `saved` as today, and does NOT emit `close`; a `role=\"status\"` line under the selects shows \"Saved\" after a confirmed save and the existing error text (`role=\"alert\"`) after a failed one, in which case the selects show the last confirmed value again. While a save is in flight the selects are disabled. The long second paragraph (\"Changing defaults does not move existing reminders…\") moves into a `<details class=\"settings-note\"><summary>About changing the default</summary>…</details>` in compact mode; the first sentence stays visible. When `compact` is false the component renders and behaves exactly as today. Style in `pages.css`: the `summary` is at least 48px high, colour `var(--text-secondary)`, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`. Unit tests in `tests/` next to the existing ReminderSettings tests (find them with `grep -rln \"ReminderSettings\" tests`): compact change saves once and does not emit `close`; failure restores the value and shows the alert; non-compact keeps Save and Cancel and closes on Save. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <those files> tests/layout`.\n  Decision: persist failures are surfaced as an alert and restore the last confirmed time; compact saves stay on the Settings page.\n\n- [x] 6. Search page: context pill and current tab. On the Search page the bottom pill still shows the Inbox split tab (\"Inbox 18\") and the Inbox icon is marked current. Fix in `src/App.vue` / `MobileBottomBar.vue`: the split tabs are teleported into the context slot only when the context is inbox, a saved split or reminders (so the slot is empty, and hidden, on Search, Drafts and every other context); `MobileBottomBar` gets a `search: boolean` prop: the Search button has `aria-current=\"page\"` when the context is search and the reader is closed, and the Inbox button has it only when `inboxOrSaved` is true. Give the current state of `.mobile-nav-item` one style for both buttons (it exists for Inbox; make sure it is not selector-bound to the first button). App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts`: on Search the context slot has no children, Search is current and Inbox is not; back on Inbox the split tab is in the slot again. Rendered assertion: on the search page `.mobile-context-slot` has zero height. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout tests/saved-split` and the rendered file that covers search pass.\n  Decision: split navigation is limited to Inbox, saved splits and Reminders; Search owns its current state in the bottom bar.\n\n- [x] 7. Search results: one left edge (`pages.css`). On the results page the query heading, the coverage notice and the list start at three different insets, and the heading is larger than anything else on the page. Target: `.search-results-header` has `padding-inline: var(--mobile-page-inset-start) var(--mobile-page-inset-end)` and no other horizontal margin or padding on its children; the query button (`.search-results-query`) is `font-size: var(--mobile-type-list)`, weight 600, left-aligned, at least 48px high, one line with ellipsis; the clear control next to it is a 48×48 button showing `<HeaderGlyph name=\"x\" />` at 24px (if it is a text \"×\" today, change the template in compact mode only and keep its `data-test` and accessible name); the coverage notice and the correspondent line (\"Ada Fixture (15)\") start at the same inset, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, colour `var(--text-secondary)`. Rendered assertions at 412×915 and 360×800 after searching `from:ada`: the left edges of the query text, the coverage notice, the correspondent line and the first row's sender are within 1px of each other; the clear control is at least 48×48 and inside the viewport; nothing overflows horizontally. Check: the rendered file passes.\n  Decision: use the shared page inset on the results header, coverage notice, and sender group captions; retain the existing accessible glyph clear button.\n\n- [x] 8. Search form: help behind a disclosure. In compact mode the six-line syntax list (`#search-help`) and the \"Not supported\" line sit inside `<details class=\"search-syntax\"><summary>Search syntax</summary>…</details>`, closed by default; the input keeps `aria-describedby=\"search-help\"` (the list keeps its id). In the regular layout the markup is unchanged. `summary`: at least 48px high, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, colour `var(--text-secondary)`. Unit test: compact renders the details closed with the list inside; regular renders the list as today. Rendered assertion: with the search form open at 412×915 the syntax list is not visible until the summary is activated. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout` and the rendered file pass.\n  Decision: a compact closed-details rule keeps existing search-help display styling from exposing the hidden content.\n\n- [x] 9. Reminders and Activity: status first. Reminders page (`RemindersList.vue` and `pages.css`): in compact mode the order is: the status or empty line (\"No pending reminders.\") first, then the explanation, then \"Refresh reminders\" as a quiet text button (no border, `var(--text-secondary)`, at least 48px high, left-aligned at the page inset). If the order needs a template change, make it for compact only (a `compact` prop, or CSS `order` if the parent is a flex or grid column). Tab counts of zero are not shown in compact mode (\"Pending\", not \"Pending 0\"); counts above zero are shown as today. Activity page (`ActivityPanel.vue`): under \"No operations yet.\" add the line \"Mail actions and their results appear here.\" in `var(--text-secondary)`, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, in both layouts' markup but only if the regular layout's tests and look are not disturbed; if they would be, render it in compact mode only. Unit tests for the tab labels and the Activity line. Rendered assertions at 412×915: on Reminders the empty line's top is above the Refresh button's top, and the Refresh button's right edge is at most the page width minus 16px. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout <the reminders and activity test files>` and the rendered file pass.\n  Decision: move compact loading and empty lines before the reminder explanation, while preserving the regular layout order; the Activity detail appears only in the empty state.\n\n- [x] 10. Screenshots. In `tests/layout/mobile-screenshots.rendered.test.ts` make sure these exist and are current: `settings.png`, `activity.png`, `contact.png`, `search.png` (form open, syntax closed), `search-results.png`, `reminders.png`; add `settings-note-open.png` (the details opened). Run the screenshots. Check: the files in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages/` were rewritten.\n  Decision: added `settings-note-open.png` immediately after the default Settings capture to show the expanded default-change note.\n\n- [x] 11. Documents. In `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" and `docs/ux-14-mobile-shell.md`: the destinations-versus-pushed-pages rule and the Back header values, the Settings hierarchy and the immediate-save model, the search results insets and the syntax disclosure, the Reminders order. State values, not history. Check: `pnpm vitest run tests/layout/design-typography.test.ts`.\n  Decision: documented the current compact states and measured values as contracts, with no change history.\n\n- [x] 12. Final. `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Then open a pull request from `mobile/p5-pages` against `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), title \"Mobile critique fixes: secondary pages\", body: what changed per item, the test counts you observed, anything left unticked. Write the pull request URL under this item.\n  Pull request: https://github.com/BbrSofiane/email-os/pull/84\nPROGRESS.md\nactivity.png\ncompose-keyboard.png\ncompose.png\ncontact.png\ndesktop-inbox.png\ndesktop-reader.png\ndrafts.png\ndrawer.png\ninbox-scrolled-end.png\ninbox-undo-toast.png\ninbox.png\npalette.png\nreader-message-sheet.png\nreader-more-sheet.png\nreader-scrolled-end.png\nreader-undo-toast.png\nreader.png\nreminder-picker.png\nreminders.png\nreply.png\nsearch-results.png\nsearch.png\nselection.png\nsettings-note-open.png\nsettings.png\nShell cwd was reset to /home/exedev/email-os","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c28818ed-4c6f-47c6-9808-473fbc1922ae","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:02:11.419Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"92b98c4 Merge pull request #83: Mobile critique fixes: selection and swipes\n  Decision: hide the empty swipe-settings live region with `:empty` while keeping it mounted.\n\n- [x] 5. Settings: one save model. The swipe options save at once; the reminder time has Save and Cancel, and Save closes the page. On the phone both must save at once. `src/components/ReminderSettings.vue` gets a `compact?: boolean` prop (passed from `App.vue` as `layoutMode === 'compact'`). When `compact` is true: there are no Save and Cancel buttons; changing the Hour or the Minute select saves immediately through the same function the form submit uses, emits `saved` as today, and does NOT emit `close`; a `role=\"status\"` line under the selects shows \"Saved\" after a confirmed save and the existing error text (`role=\"alert\"`) after a failed one, in which case the selects show the last confirmed value again. While a save is in flight the selects are disabled. The long second paragraph (\"Changing defaults does not move existing reminders…\") moves into a `<details class=\"settings-note\"><summary>About changing the default</summary>…</details>` in compact mode; the first sentence stays visible. When `compact` is false the component renders and behaves exactly as today. Style in `pages.css`: the `summary` is at least 48px high, colour `var(--text-secondary)`, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`. Unit tests in `tests/` next to the existing ReminderSettings tests (find them with `grep -rln \"ReminderSettings\" tests`): compact change saves once and does not emit `close`; failure restores the value and shows the alert; non-compact keeps Save and Cancel and closes on Save. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <those files> tests/layout`.\n  Decision: persist failures are surfaced as an alert and restore the last confirmed time; compact saves stay on the Settings page.\n\n- [x] 6. Search page: context pill and current tab. On the Search page the bottom pill still shows the Inbox split tab (\"Inbox 18\") and the Inbox icon is marked current. Fix in `src/App.vue` / `MobileBottomBar.vue`: the split tabs are teleported into the context slot only when the context is inbox, a saved split or reminders (so the slot is empty, and hidden, on Search, Drafts and every other context); `MobileBottomBar` gets a `search: boolean` prop: the Search button has `aria-current=\"page\"` when the context is search and the reader is closed, and the Inbox button has it only when `inboxOrSaved` is true. Give the current state of `.mobile-nav-item` one style for both buttons (it exists for Inbox; make sure it is not selector-bound to the first button). App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts`: on Search the context slot has no children, Search is current and Inbox is not; back on Inbox the split tab is in the slot again. Rendered assertion: on the search page `.mobile-context-slot` has zero height. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout tests/saved-split` and the rendered file that covers search pass.\n  Decision: split navigation is limited to Inbox, saved splits and Reminders; Search owns its current state in the bottom bar.\n\n- [x] 7. Search results: one left edge (`pages.css`). On the results page the query heading, the coverage notice and the list start at three different insets, and the heading is larger than anything else on the page. Target: `.search-results-header` has `padding-inline: var(--mobile-page-inset-start) var(--mobile-page-inset-end)` and no other horizontal margin or padding on its children; the query button (`.search-results-query`) is `font-size: var(--mobile-type-list)`, weight 600, left-aligned, at least 48px high, one line with ellipsis; the clear control next to it is a 48×48 button showing `<HeaderGlyph name=\"x\" />` at 24px (if it is a text \"×\" today, change the template in compact mode only and keep its `data-test` and accessible name); the coverage notice and the correspondent line (\"Ada Fixture (15)\") start at the same inset, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, colour `var(--text-secondary)`. Rendered assertions at 412×915 and 360×800 after searching `from:ada`: the left edges of the query text, the coverage notice, the correspondent line and the first row's sender are within 1px of each other; the clear control is at least 48×48 and inside the viewport; nothing overflows horizontally. Check: the rendered file passes.\n  Decision: use the shared page inset on the results header, coverage notice, and sender group captions; retain the existing accessible glyph clear button.\n\n- [x] 8. Search form: help behind a disclosure. In compact mode the six-line syntax list (`#search-help`) and the \"Not supported\" line sit inside `<details class=\"search-syntax\"><summary>Search syntax</summary>…</details>`, closed by default; the input keeps `aria-describedby=\"search-help\"` (the list keeps its id). In the regular layout the markup is unchanged. `summary`: at least 48px high, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, colour `var(--text-secondary)`. Unit test: compact renders the details closed with the list inside; regular renders the list as today. Rendered assertion: with the search form open at 412×915 the syntax list is not visible until the summary is activated. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout` and the rendered file pass.\n  Decision: a compact closed-details rule keeps existing search-help display styling from exposing the hidden content.\n\n- [x] 9. Reminders and Activity: status first. Reminders page (`RemindersList.vue` and `pages.css`): in compact mode the order is: the status or empty line (\"No pending reminders.\") first, then the explanation, then \"Refresh reminders\" as a quiet text button (no border, `var(--text-secondary)`, at least 48px high, left-aligned at the page inset). If the order needs a template change, make it for compact only (a `compact` prop, or CSS `order` if the parent is a flex or grid column). Tab counts of zero are not shown in compact mode (\"Pending\", not \"Pending 0\"); counts above zero are shown as today. Activity page (`ActivityPanel.vue`): under \"No operations yet.\" add the line \"Mail actions and their results appear here.\" in `var(--text-secondary)`, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, in both layouts' markup but only if the regular layout's tests and look are not disturbed; if they would be, render it in compact mode only. Unit tests for the tab labels and the Activity line. Rendered assertions at 412×915: on Reminders the empty line's top is above the Refresh button's top, and the Refresh button's right edge is at most the page width minus 16px. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout <the reminders and activity test files>` and the rendered file pass.\n  Decision: move compact loading and empty lines before the reminder explanation, while preserving the regular layout order; the Activity detail appears only in the empty state.\n\n- [x] 10. Screenshots. In `tests/layout/mobile-screenshots.rendered.test.ts` make sure these exist and are current: `settings.png`, `activity.png`, `contact.png`, `search.png` (form open, syntax closed), `search-results.png`, `reminders.png`; add `settings-note-open.png` (the details opened). Run the screenshots. Check: the files in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages/` were rewritten.\n  Decision: added `settings-note-open.png` immediately after the default Settings capture to show the expanded default-change note.\n\n- [x] 11. Documents. In `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" and `docs/ux-14-mobile-shell.md`: the destinations-versus-pushed-pages rule and the Back header values, the Settings hierarchy and the immediate-save model, the search results insets and the syntax disclosure, the Reminders order. State values, not history. Check: `pnpm vitest run tests/layout/design-typography.test.ts`.\n  Decision: documented the current compact states and measured values as contracts, with no change history.\n\n- [x] 12. Final. `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Then open a pull request from `mobile/p5-pages` against `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), title \"Mobile critique fixes: secondary pages\", body: what changed per item, the test counts you observed, anything left unticked. Write the pull request URL under this item.\n  Pull request: https://github.com/BbrSofiane/email-os/pull/84\nPROGRESS.md\nactivity.png\ncompose-keyboard.png\ncompose.png\ncontact.png\ndesktop-inbox.png\ndesktop-reader.png\ndrafts.png\ndrawer.png\ninbox-scro