{"parentUuid":"08410504-e218-4791-83ce-eed10ca34322","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch922fP4YSWyhstQwwv2p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XQ9a7CXsGjQRqYJXEFixHu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Review fixes (added by the reviewer after looking at the screenshots)\n\n- [ ] 13. Search form open = Search page. In `search.png` the search form is open (`searchVisible` true, context still inbox) but the bottom pill still shows the \"Inbox 18\" split tab, the Inbox button is current and the top bar has no title. In compact mode, while `searchVisible` is true and the reader is closed, treat it like the Search page: pass `search` to `MobileBottomBar` as `mailbox.context.value === 'search' || searchVisible.value` (so Search has `aria-current=\"page\"` and Inbox does not), keep the context slot empty (same rule as item 6: split tabs only when the context is inbox, a saved split or reminders AND the search form is not open), and the top bar title reads \"Search\". Closing the form (Escape or Back) without searching restores Inbox as current and the split tab in the slot. Regular layout unchanged. App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts` for open → Search current, slot empty, title \"Search\"; close → Inbox current, split tab back. Rendered assertion at 412×915 with the form open: `.mobile-context-slot` has zero height. Re-run the screenshots (`search.png` must show no \"Inbox 18\" pill). Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout tests/search` and the rendered file pass.\n\n- [ ] 14. One disclosure style. The two compact disclosures look different: \"Search syntax\" shows the native ▶ marker and its text sits at the top of its 48px box; \"About changing the default\" has no marker at all, so it reads as plain text, not a control. Give both summaries (`.search-syntax > summary` and `.settings-note summary`, compact only, `pages.css`) one shared style: `display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; min-height: 48px; list-style: none; cursor: pointer`, hide the native marker (`::-webkit-details-marker { display: none }` and `list-style: none`), and add a leading chevron drawn in CSS (a `::before` 8×8 box with a 2px right and bottom border in `currentColor`, rotated -45deg when closed and 45deg when the parent `details` is `[open]`, `transition: transform 120ms ease-out`, `transition: none` inside `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`). Colour `var(--text-secondary)`, `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`. Rendered assertions at 412×915: both summaries are at least 48px high, their text is vertically centred (text box centre within 2px of the summary centre), and their left edges match the page inset. Re-run the screenshots. Check: the rendered file passes, `search.png`, `settings.png` and `settings-note-open.png` rewritten.\n\n- [ ] 15. Final again: `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots; push; add a comment to PR #84 listing items 13 and 14 and the test counts.\nEOF","description":"Append review-fix items to pages checklist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1341,"cache_read_input_tokens":77610,"output_tokens":1328,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1341,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1328,"cache_read_input_tokens":77610,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1341},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"con