{"parentUuid":"945cc379-428e-46a8-94c6-3d5cc0fcc36c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch93VNonTPNfzCEAPtMv4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm settling on a fix for the compact list layout: hide the split nav while items are selected, and put the notice above the selection bar so the bar sits closest to the nav. I'm also writing a short checklist for the list thread on branch mobile/p5-list-2, starting with the branch name and the split-nav hiding.\n\nI'm going through the remaining checklist items for the list thread: the split-nav hiding with tests, a rendered check that the notice sits above the selection bar without overlap, and rerunning the selection screenshot. After that I'll finish up with a final pass and the PR.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1316,"cache_read_input_tokens":135942,"output_tokens":1874,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1316,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1874,"cache_read_input_tokens":135942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1316,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1316},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4155,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch93VLXs4smjZkCUFaMFP","requestRef":"6658efac-04cb-4012-a905-a64f41f690ec","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8b235b7a-683d-4c3b-baee-422dbdde4def","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:21:48.936Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"8b235b7a-683d-4c3b-baee-422dbdde4def","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch93VNonTPNfzCEAPtMv4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A1po7ZXwdxGUHB67bqU1WU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list2 && cat > /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list2/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# Mobile p5 list follow-up: selection mode stacking\n\nFound on the emulator: in selection mode the bottom of the phone screen carries four floating layers, top to bottom: the selection bar, the action notice (toast), the \"Inbox 14\" split pill, the nav pill. Together they cover almost half the screen and the toast separates the selection bar from the nav. Target: while one or more conversations are selected (compact only), the split pill is hidden (the selection bar replaces it), and the selection bar sits directly above the nav pill with the action notice above it.\n\nRules (unchanged): no `implement` skill, no delegation, no `view_image`, no cargo or Android builds. Readable multi-line code. Compact CSS only in `src/assets/mobile/*.css` under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, no `!important`; the regular layout must not change. Protocol per item: do it, run its check, tick it with a one-line `Decision:`, commit, push (retry on transient remote errors).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch. In your worktree: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p5-list-2 origin/mobile/integration`, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `git log -1 --oneline` shows `0388d56` (or later) and `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Hide the split pill while selecting. In `src/App.vue`, `inboxSplitsShown` also requires `!(layoutMode.value === 'compact' && selectedCount.value > 0)` (use whatever the selected count is called where `<SelectionBar v-if=... selectedCount > 0>` reads it). Clearing the selection (X, Escape, Back, or acting on it) brings the split pill back. App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts`: compact + one row selected → the context slot has no children; clear → the split tab is back; regular layout with a selection keeps its split nav. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 3. Dock order. In compact only (`list.css`), the `.list-dock` children are ordered so the action notice (`ActionNotice` root) and `.command-error` sit above `.selection-bar`, and the selection bar is the last, nearest the nav pill (use `display: flex; flex-direction: column` on the dock and `order` on the children if it is not already a flex column; do not change the template order, which the regular layout depends on). Rendered assertion at 412×915 in `tests/layout/mobile-list.rendered.test.ts` (or the rendered file that covers selection): select one row, then mark a different row done with a swipe or the `e` command so a notice shows, then select a row again: the notice's bottom ≤ the selection bar's top, the selection bar's bottom ≤ the nav pill's top, `.mobile-context-slot` has zero height, nothing overlaps horizontally out of the viewport. Check: that rendered file passes.\n\n- [ ] 4. Screenshots. In `tests/layout/mobile-screenshots.rendered.test.ts` keep `selection.png` current and add `selection-with-notice.png` (the state of item 3: a notice showing and one row selected). Run with `EMAIL_OS_SCREENSHOT_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list2`. Check: both files exist in that directory and were rewritten.\n\n- [ ] 5. Final. `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" selection paragraph in one or two sentences (state, not history). Open a pull request from `mobile/p5-list-2` against `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), title \"Mobile: selection mode replaces the split pill\", body with what changed and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\nbash /tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad/p5.sh 2>&1 | grep -A1 \"== list\"","description":"Write list follow-up checklist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1316,"cache_read_input_tokens":135942,"output_tokens":1874,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1316,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1874,"cache_read_input_tokens":135942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1316,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1316},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13418,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01A1po7ZXwdxGUHB67bqU1WU":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list2 && cat > /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-list2/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# Mobile p5 list follow-up: selection mode stacking\n\nFound on the emulator: in selection mode the bottom of the phone screen carries four floating layers, top to bottom: the selection bar, the action notice (toast), the \"Inbox 14\" split pill, the nav pill. Together they cover almost half the screen and the toast separates the selection bar from the nav. Target: while one or more conversations are selected (compact only), the split pill is hidden (the selection bar replaces it), and the selection bar sits directly above the nav pill with the action notice above it.\n\nRules (unchanged): no `implement` skill, no delegation, no `view_image`, no cargo or Android builds. Readable multi-line code. Compact CSS only in `src/assets/mobile/*.css` under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, no `!important`; the regular