{"parentUuid":"8200a7be-3bc2-42bc-b38e-639cbaa02dcb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch93c85Cr3JGrNVLh8t28","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lc4j1pAG2P6ZhGjq58H3FZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages/PROGRESS-2.md <<'EOF'\n# Mobile p5 pages follow-up: pushed pages must cover the app, not sit 24px down\n\nFound on the Android emulator: Settings (and the other pushed pages) start 24px below the top of the app, so the top bar's menu and compose buttons show through above the page, cut off, and the Back header sits lower than the top bar it replaces. Cause: `src/assets/mobile/pages.css` positions `.utility-drawer` with `position: fixed; inset: 24px 0 0` and gives `.contact-disclosure-panel` `padding-top: 24px`. The 24px equals the height of the browser preview's account tab strip (`.fixture-workspaces`), which does not exist in the Android app. `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]` is already `position: relative; overflow: hidden` (shell.css line 1).\n\nRules (unchanged): no `implement` skill, no delegation, no `view_image`, no cargo or Android builds. Readable multi-line code. Compact CSS only in `src/assets/mobile/*.css` under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, no `!important`; the regular layout must not change. Protocol per item: do it, run its check, tick it with a one-line `Decision:`, commit, push (retry on transient remote errors).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch. In your worktree: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p5-pages-2 origin/mobile/integration`. Check: `git log -1 --oneline` shows `0388d56` or later and `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Cover the app box. Pushed pages (`.utility-drawer`, which includes Settings, Activity, Account, Provider mail, and the Contact panel) cover exactly the `.app` box: `position: absolute; inset: 0` (the `.app` is the containing block), with no literal 24px top offset or top padding anywhere for this purpose. If something between `.app` and the page is a nearer positioned or clipping ancestor that makes `absolute` wrong, use the nearest correct approach and say which in the Decision; do not reintroduce a constant matching the preview tab strip. The Back header then sits exactly where the top bar sits (same top, same height). Add a contract test in `tests/layout/` that `src/assets/mobile/pages.css` has no `inset: 24px` and no `padding-top: 24px` on `.utility-drawer` or `.contact-disclosure-panel`. Rendered assertions at 412×915 for Settings, Activity and Contact: the page's top equals the `.app` top within 1px; the page's Back button's top and centre equal the destination top bar menu button's top and centre (measure the menu button before opening the page) within 1px; at the page's top-left and top-right corners (3px inside), `document.elementFromPoint` returns an element inside the page, not the top bar. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout` and the rendered files that cover pages pass.\n\n- [ ] 3. Screenshots and final. Re-run the screenshots with `EMAIL_OS_SCREENSHOT_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages-2`; `settings.png`, `activity.png`, `contact.png` must exist there. Then `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite. Open a pull request from `mobile/p5-pages-2` against `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), title \"Mobile: pushed pages cover the app on Android\", body with the cause, the change and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\nmkdir -p /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages-2","description":"Write pages follow-up checklist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":150508,"output_tokens":1380,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1925,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1380,"cache_read_input_tokens":150508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1925},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10959,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Lc4j1pAG2P6ZhGjq58H3FZ":{"command":"cat > /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages/PROGRESS-2.md <<'EOF'\n# Mobile p5 pages follow-up: pushed pages must cover the app, not sit 24px down\n\nFound on the Android emulator: Settings (and the other pushed pages) start 24px below the top of the app, so the top bar's menu and compose buttons show through above the page, cut off, and the Back header sits lower than the top bar it replaces. Cause: `src/assets/mobile/pages.css` positions `.utility-drawer` with `position: fixed; inset: 24px 0 0` and gives `.contact-disclosure-panel` `padding-top: 24px`. The 24px equals the height of the browser preview's account tab strip (`.fixture-workspaces`), which does not exist in the Android app. `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]` is already `position: relative; overflow: hidden` (shell.css line 1).\n\nRules (unchanged): no `implement` skill, no delegation, no `view_image`, no cargo or Android builds. Readable multi-line code. Compact CSS only in `src/assets/mobile/*.css` under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, no `!important`; the regular layout must not change. Protocol per item: do it, run its check, tick it with a one-line `Decision:`, commit, push (retry on transient remote errors).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch. In your worktree: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p5-pages-2 origin/mobile/integration`. Check: `git log -1 --oneline` shows `0388d56` or later and `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Cover the app box. Pushed pages (`.utility-drawer`, which includes Settings, Activity, Account, Provider mail, and the Contact panel) cover exactly the `.app` box: `position: absolute; inset: 0` (the `.app` is the containing block), with no literal 24px top offset or top padding anywhere for this purpose. If something between `.app` and the page is a nearer positioned or clipping ancestor that makes `absolute` wrong, use the nearest correct approach and say which in the Decision; do not reintroduce a constant matching the preview tab strip. The Back header then sits exactly where the top bar sits (same top, same height). Add a contract test in `tests/layout/` that `src/assets/mobile/pages.css` has no `inset: 24px` and no `padding-top: 24px` on `.utility-drawer` or `.contact-disclosure-panel`. Rendered assertions at 412×915 for Settings, Activity and Contact: the page's top equals the `.app` top within 1px; the page's Back button's top and centre equal the destination top bar menu button's top and centre (measure the menu button before opening the page) within 1px; at the page's top-left and top-right corners (3px inside), `document.elementFromPoint` returns an element inside the page, not the top bar. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout` and the rendered files that cover pages pass.\n\n- [ ] 3. Screenshots and final. Re-run the screenshots with `EMAIL_OS_SCREENSHOT_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages-2`; `settings.png`, `activity.png`, `contact.png` must exist there. Then `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite. Open a pull request from `mobile/p5-pages-2` against `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), title \"Mobile: pushed pages cover the app on Android\", body with the cause, the change and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\nmkdir -p /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages-2","description":"Write pages follow-up checklist"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch93c5Vg5puzxehjyezai","requestRef":"854fd722-64b2-4246-89ef-22b99418f9e9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"628cf199-4a8a-46fe-82db-84ee30d50c8b","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:23:27.350Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
