{"parentUuid":"e0fdc841-eae6-4334-a1bc-30696bb9c601","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch93ibEW8zjuXm9t6j1f1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The window-level Escape ladder skips the search form, which only closes on Escape when its own input has focus, so Android Back's synthetic Escape misses it. I'm adding that fix and a check of every phone surface against the Back bridge to the pages follow-up.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_read_input_tokens":162858,"output_tokens":1414,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":508},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":162858,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch93iXgwSKZwvNmreEh9S","requestRef":"9eb99d6d-28e0-4ea1-a8e3-6c1c253409f3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d3097a4-0ef1-4281-8b5d-5ba92b4e18f0","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:24:51.474Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"6d3097a4-0ef1-4281-8b5d-5ba92b4e18f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch93ibEW8zjuXm9t6j1f1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MutntNxHypEQ4jSaSWmSfb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PROGRESS-2.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"- [ ] 3. Screenshots and final.\",\"\"\"- [ ] 3. Android Back closes the search form. Found on the emulator: with the compact search form open (`searchVisible` true) and focus not in the search input, Android Back backgrounds the app and the form is still open on return. Cause: `installAndroidBackBridge` in `src/App.vue` (around line 781) dispatches a synthetic `Escape` keydown on `window` and returns `defaultPrevented`; the search form only handles Escape in the input's own keydown handler (`useSearchSurface.ts`), and the window ladder has no step for it. Fix, compact layout only (the regular layout's keyboard behaviour must not change): the window-level Escape handling closes a visible search form (same effect as the input's Escape: close suggestions first if open, else `searchVisible = false` and focus the focused row) and calls `preventDefault`, ordered after the modal surfaces, sheets, compose and reply, and before the step that leaves the search context. Then audit the bridge: add a test file `tests/layout/mobile-android-back.test.ts` that mounts the compact app with the Android bridge installed (see `src/lib/android-back.test.ts` for how it is set up) and, for each phone surface, opens it, calls `window.__emailOsAndroidBack()`, and asserts it returns `true` and closes exactly that surface: search form (focus on body, and focus on a row), selection mode, navigation drawer, a pushed page (Settings), Contact, the reader, the reader's more sheet, the per-message sheet, the reminder picker sheet, compose, reply. At the Inbox root with nothing open it returns `false`. Fix any other surface the audit finds that does not close (compact only), and note each in the Decision. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout src/lib`.\n\n- [ ] 4. Screenshots and final.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^- \\[\" PROGRESS-2.md","description":"Insert Android Back item into pages follow-up"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_read_input_tokens":162858,"output_tokens":1414,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":508},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":162858,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":6546,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MutntNxHypEQ4jSaSWmSfb":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PROGRESS-2.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"- [ ] 3. Screenshots and final.\",\"\"\"- [ ] 3. Android Back closes the search form. Found on the emulator: with the compact search form open (`searchVisible` true) and focus not in the search input, Android Back backgrounds the app and the form is still open on return. Cause: `installAndroidBackBridge` in `src/App.vue` (around line 781) dispatches a synthetic `Escape` keydown on `window` and returns `defaultPrevented`; the search form only handles Escape in the input's own keydown handler (`useSearchSurface.ts`), and the window ladder has no step for it. Fix, compact layout only (the regular layout's keyboard behaviour must not change): the window-level Escape handling closes a visible search form (same effect as the input's Escape: close suggestions first if open, else `searchVisible = false` and focus the focused row) and calls `preventDefault`, ordered after the modal surfaces, sheets, compose and reply, and before the step that leaves the search context. Then audit the bridge: add a test file `tests/layout/mobile-android-back.test.ts` that mounts the compact app with the Android bridge installed (see `src/lib/android-back.test.ts` for how it is set up) and, for each phone surface, opens it, calls `window.__emailOsAndroidBack()`, and asserts it returns `true` and closes exactly that surface: search form (focus on body, and focus on a row), selection mode, navigation drawer, a pushed page (Settings), Contact, the reader, the reader's more sheet, the per-message sheet, the reminder picker sheet, compose, reply. At the Inbox root with nothing open it returns `false`. Fix any other surface the audit finds that does not close (compact only), and note each in the Decision. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout src/lib`.\n\n- [ ] 4. Screenshots and final.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^- \\[\" PROGRESS-2.md","description":"Insert Android Back item into pages follow-up"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch93iXgwSKZwvNmreEh9S","requestRef":"9eb99d6d-28e0-4ea1-a8e3-6c1c253409f3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"11af4054-5125-4a71-abaa-e644791a705d","timestamp":"2026-11-17T19:24:58.022Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
