m is still open on return. Cause: `installAndroidBackBridge` in `src/App.vue` (around line 781) dispatches a synthetic `Escape` keydown on `window` and returns `defaultPrevented`; the search form only handles Escape in the input's own keydown handler (`useSearchSurface.ts`), and the window ladder has no step for it. Fix, compact layout only (the regular layout's keyboard behaviour must not change): the window-level Escape handling closes a visible search form (same effect as the input's Escape: close suggestions first if open, else `searchVisible = false` and focus the focused row) and calls `preventDefault`, ordered after the modal surfaces, sheets, compose and reply, and before the step that leaves the search context. Then audit the bridge: add a test file `tests/layout/mobile-android-back.test.ts` that mounts the compact app with the Android bridge installed (see `src/lib/android-back.test.ts` for how it is set up) and, for each phone surface, opens it, calls `window.__emailOsAndroidBack()`, and asserts it returns `true` and closes exactly that surface: search form (focus on body, and focus on a row), selection mode, navigation drawer, a pushed page (Settings), Contact, the reader, the reader's more sheet, the per-message sheet, the reminder picker sheet, compose, reply. At the Inbox root with nothing open it returns `false`. Fix any other surface the audit finds that does not close (compact only), and note each in the Decision. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout src/lib`.\n14:- [ ] 4. Screenshots and final. Re-run the screenshots with `EMAIL_OS_SCREENSHOT_DIR=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p5-pages-2`; `settings.png`, `activity.png`, `contact.png` must exist there. Then `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite. Open a pull request from `mobile/p5-pages-2` against `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), title \"Mobile: pushed pages cover the app on Android\",