{"parentUuid":"3eeb0590-cfdb-498e-b7ef-36a25916d686","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch96WYfyaFt88dWjH9qz5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Back clears the selection too. Now I'm updating PR #80's description with the round-2 work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":210349,"output_tokens":1723,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1453,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":210349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1453},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch96WUcfKq6JsNKtf4hgD","requestRef":"a4e61c02-aacd-419e-8c43-d99185cb6295","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"94aabda8-9c4d-47dd-9c8c-8b68e7472635","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:01:23.263Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"94aabda8-9c4d-47dd-9c8c-8b68e7472635","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch96WYfyaFt88dWjH9qz5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0159PMDKwqpQRbEz2fy7GTn2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"B=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad/pr80-body.md; gh pr view 80 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --json body -q .body > $B.orig; python3 - \"$B\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p+'.orig').read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"## Not included\"\"\",\"\"\"## Round 2: design critique fixes\n\nA design critique of the key phone screens scored 25/40 and named five priority issues; all five are addressed:\n\n- **Selection and swipes (#83, #85):** selected rows use the focus fill with a checked box; the selection bar is a two-row pill (clear, count, \"Mark N done\"; then Mark read, Mark unread, Select all) and replaces the split pill while anything is selected, with notices above it. Swipes track the finger, the whole row slides as one panel, the action arms at 35% of the row width (stronger colour, larger glyph), and a committed done swipe moves the row out before the action runs. Reduced motion removes these transitions.\n- **Editors (#82):** on the phone the X is the only way out of a new message or reply; the status line always ends in \"never sent\" (for example \"Saved locally · never sent\"). To and Cc use the email keyboard without autocorrect, and Enter moves to the next field. The failure state puts Retry above the fields. New glyphs for copy, collapse, contact and commands; the done action uses the accent colour.\n- **Secondary pages (#84, #86):** pushed pages (Settings, Activity, Account, Provider mail, Contact) have a Back button in the top bar's place and cover the whole app; destinations keep the menu button. Settings is grouped, saves the reminder time at once (no Save/Cancel) and puts the long note behind a disclosure. Search marks itself current, drops the Inbox pill, lines results up on one edge and hides the syntax help behind a disclosure. Reminders shows its status first and hides zero counts; Activity explains its empty state.\n- **Android Back (#86):** Back now closes the search form and the reminder picker; a test checks that Back closes each phone surface in turn and returns false at the Inbox root.\n\n## Not included\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Frontend unit tests: 1,959 in 118 files (1,897 in 105 on `main`); typecheck and production build pass.\n- Rendered tests in Chromium: 76 of 76 (49 on `main`), including phone geometry at 412×915 and 360×800 and real touch input for swipes and long press.\"\"\",\"\"\"- Frontend unit tests: 2,004 in 122 files (1,897 in 105 on `main`); typecheck and production build pass.\n- Rendered tests in Chromium: 82 passed, 6 skipped (the screenshot capture and opt-in files), including phone geometry at 412×915 and 360×800 and real touch input for swipes and long press. One run in five had a single failure that did not reproduce in four reruns; I did not identify the test.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Screenshots are in `docs/validation/mobile/`.\"\"\",\"\"\"Screenshots are in `docs/validation/mobile/` (from the first round). Round 2 was re-checked on the emulator with a local APK of f08fd85: swipe to mark done, long-press selection (bar above the nav, no split pill), Back clearing the selection, compose with only the X, Settings with Back aligned to the menu button, the search form, and Android Back closing Settings, the search form and the reader without leaving the app.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- The Contact page header still shows the word \"Close\" in its round button; the other pages use the glyph.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- After an action's Undo window ends, its notice stays on screen (\"Undo expired — Mark not done restores…\") over the list and reader until the next action. This behaviour predates this PR and was not changed.\n\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Implemented in sub-PRs #75, #76, #77, #78, #79 and #81\"\"\",\"\"\"Implemented in sub-PRs #75, #76, #77, #78, #79, #81 and, for round 2, #82, #83, #84, #85 and #86\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ndiff <(cat $B.orig) $B | head -5; gh pr edit 80 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --body-file $B >/dev/null && echo updated; gh pr checks 80 -R BbrSofiane/email-os 2>&1 | head","description":"Update PR 80 description and check CI"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":210349,"output_tokens":1723,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1453,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":210349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1453},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13464,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0159PMDKwqpQRbEz2fy7GTn2":{"command":"B=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad/pr80-body.md; gh pr view 80 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --json body -q .body > $B.orig; python3 - \"$B\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p+'.orig').read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"## Not included\"\"\",\"\"\"## Round 2: design critique fixes\n\nA design critique of the key phone screens scored 25/40 and named five priority issues; all five are addressed:\n\n- **Selection and swipes (#83, #85):** selected rows use the focus fill with a checked box; the selection bar is a two-row pill (clear, count, \"Mark N done\"; then Mark read, Mark unread, Select all) and replaces the split pill while anything is selected, with notices above it. Swipes track the finger, the whole row slides as one panel, the action arms at 35% of the row width (stronger colour, larger glyph), and a committed done swipe moves the row out before the action runs. Reduced motion removes these transitions.\n- **Editors (#82):** on the phone the X is the only way out of a new message or reply; the status line always ends in \"never sent\" (for example \"Saved locally · never sent\"). To and Cc use the email keyboard without autocorrect, and Enter moves to the next field. The failure state puts Retry above the fields. New glyphs for copy, collapse, contact and commands; the done action uses the accent colour.\n- **Secondary pages (#84, #86):** pushed pages (Settings, Activity, Account, Provider mail, Contact) have a Back button in the top bar's place and cover the whole app; destinations keep the menu button. Settings is grouped, saves the reminder time at once (no Save/Cancel) and puts the long note behind a disclosure. Search marks itself current, drops the Inbox pill, lines results up on one edge and hides the syntax help behind a disclosure. Reminders shows its status first and hides zero counts; Activity explains its empty state.\n- **Android Back (#86):** Back now closes the search form and the reminder picker; a test checks that Back closes each phone surface in turn and returns false at the Inbox root.\n\n## Not included\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Frontend unit tests: 1,959 in 118 files (1,897 in 105 on `main`); typecheck and production build pass.\n- Rendered tests in Chromium: 76 of 76 (49 on `main`), including phone geometry at 412×915 and 360×800 and real touch input for swipes and long press.\"\"\",\"\"\"- Frontend unit tests: 2,004 in 122 files (1,897 in 105 on `main`); typecheck and production build pass.\n- Rendered tests in Chromium: 82 passed, 6 skipped (the screenshot capture and opt-in files), including phone geometry at 412×915 and 360×800 and real touch input for swipes and long press. One run in five had a single failure that did not reproduce in four reruns; I did not identify the test.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Screenshots are in `docs/validation/mobile/`.\"\"\",\"\"\"Screenshots are in `docs/validation/mobile/` (from the first round). Round 2 was re-checked on the emulator with a local APK of f08fd85: swipe to mark done, long-press selection (bar above the nav, no split pill), Back clearing the selection, compose with only the X, Settings with Back aligned to the menu button, the search form, and Android Back closing Settings, the search form and the reader without leaving the app.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- The Contact page header still shows the word \"Close\" in its round button; the other pages use the glyph.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- After an action's Undo window ends, its notice stays on screen (\"Undo expired — Mark not done restores…\") over the list and reader until the next action. This behaviour predates this PR and was not changed.\n\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Implemented in sub-PRs #75, #76, #77, #78, #79 and #81\"\"\",\"\"\"Implemented in sub-PRs #75, #76, #77, #78, #79, #81 and, for round 2, #82, #83, #84, #85 and #86\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ndiff <(cat $B.orig) $B | head -5; gh pr edit 80 -R BbrSofiane/email-os --body-file $B >/dev/null && echo updated; gh pr checks 80 -R BbrSofiane/email-os 2>&1 | head","description":"Update PR 80 description and check CI"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch96WUcfKq6JsNKtf4hgD","requestRef":"a4e61c02-aacd-419e-8c43-d99185cb6295","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"5704fbb9-41af-4a12-9737-5f4647cfd10a","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:01:36.727Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-m