{"parentUuid":"f494fe26-a7b0-4b38-a565-5df3244365c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch96YnpLzbErRDVdWFDU7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing whether to close the device panel, and my rule is to only close tabs I opened myself, so I'll leave that panel alone. Next I'll put together the final report.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":213881,"output_tokens":1188,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":30},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":213881,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6918,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch96YioEoTTKVHtUtK2XL","requestRef":"e42ee54a-f69c-473d-b0f1-f712835692e4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad34ae50-02ac-44ea-bb59-f8ec3625680e","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:01:58.835Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"ad34ae50-02ac-44ea-bb59-f8ec3625680e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch96YnpLzbErRDVdWFDU7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five priority issues from the critique are fixed and merged into `mobile/integration`. PR #80 (`mobile/integration` → `main`) is ready for you to review and merge; its description now has a section on this round. CI (`check` and `android-apk`) passes on the latest commit (f08fd85).\n\n**What changed, by the issues you picked:**\n- **Selection and swipes** (PRs #83, #85):\n  - **Selection:** selected rows get a fill and a checked box. The selection bar has two rows: X, \"1 selected\" and \"Mark 1 done\" on top, then Mark read, Mark unread and Select all. While anything is selected, it takes the place of the Inbox tab bar.\n  - **Swipes:** the whole row moves with your finger. At 35% of the row width the action \"arms\": the colour gets stronger and the icon grows. When you let go, the row slides off before it's marked done. All of this respects the reduced-motion setting.\n- **Editors** (#82):\n  - On the phone, the X is the only way to close a new message or a reply. There is no \"Save and close\" button.\n  - The status line always ends with the fixed phrase \"never sent\", e.g. \"Saved locally · never sent\". The first part stays truthful about where the draft is actually saved.\n  - To and Cc bring up the email keyboard with autocorrect off, and Enter moves to the next field.\n  - Also in this PR: new icons for copy, collapse, contact and commands, and the done button now uses the accent colour.\n- **Secondary pages** (#84, #86):\n  - Settings, Activity, Account, Provider mail and Contact have a Back arrow where the menu button normally sits. This also replaces the \"Close\" text on Contact.\n  - Settings now saves the reminder time as soon as you change it, with no Save/Cancel. The long note is tucked behind a disclosure.\n  - Search tidies its layout: the Search tab is shown as current, results line up on one edge, and the syntax help is folded away.\n  - Reminders shows its status first.\n\n**Bugs found on the emulator, now fixed** (the browser screenshots didn't show any of them):\n- Pages like Settings sat 24px too low on the phone, with the top bar's buttons showing through above them.\n- Android Back closed the whole app while the search form was open. Back now closes the search form and the reminder picker. A new test checks that Back closes each phone screen in turn.\n- In selection mode, four floating bars stacked up over half the screen.\n\n**Checks on the final branch:**\n- 2,004 unit tests pass; typecheck and build pass.\n- 82 browser layout tests pass and 6 are skipped. One run in five had a single failure that I couldn't reproduce in four reruns, so there's an unidentified flaky test.\n- On the emulator, with a locally built app of the final branch:\n  - Swipes, selection and the compose X work.\n  - Settings and search look right.\n  - Back closes Settings, search, the reader and a selection without leaving the app.\n\n**Still open:**\n- The first launch right after installing can show Android's \"isn't responding\" dialog; relaunching fixes it. This was already known.\n- After an action's Undo window ends, its \"Undo expired…\" message stays on screen until your next action. This was already the behaviour before this work, and it covers part of the list and reader on a phone.\n- Two sample conversations are marked done on the emulator from my swipe tests.\n\nI haven't re-run the critique for a new score. I can run it again with the same Sonnet 5.5 reviewers if you'd like one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":213881,"output_tokens":1188,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":30},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":213881,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch96YioEoTTKVHtUtK2XL","requestRef":"e42ee54a-f69c-473d-b0f1-f712835692e4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"da387384-c426-4b93-be23-56cc593d84f6","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:02:03.190Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
