{"parentUuid":"f208dc6e-9639-42d8-9201-676907eddaeb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch98Le39LkgjmYKfqERyf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'm writing the briefs for the reviewers, making sure they can't see each other and that nothing points to private references or the reference product's name. I'm also telling them to stay read-only: no repo edits, and their output goes to a file in the critique-r2 directory and gets returned in the final message. For the A reviewers' shared context, I'm noting the repo at the detached commit f08fd85, which must not be modified, committed, or switched, and I'm starting with the product brief.\n\nNext I'm pulling the design spec, the mobile shell doc, and the mobile CSS and components the reviewers need to read. I'm also setting the browser screenshots and the Android emulator captures as the visual references, and noting that the browser strip and \"Preview\" label are harness chrome. Last, I'm planning the detector run with `impeccable detect --json` on the markup directories and starting the dev server for the browser check.\n\nI'm setting the detector up to scan rendered pages, so I'm working out how to serve the built app: I'll run a preview server from the existing build in the background on a fixed port, point the detector at Chrome through the browser path variable, and shut the server down afterward. There's no live browser available here for overlay injection, so I'll note that and fall back to the reported results. Reviewers will run on high effort in async mode, and I'll write their outputs to A1.md, A2.md, and B.md in the critique-r2 directory.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":244194,"output_tokens":1831,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":782},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1831,"cache_read_input_tokens":244194,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9629,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch98LaoBEpvJaae877niW","requestRef":"3e0f217b-4176-4c6a-80c3-a53dc363208d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"impeccable","type":"assistant","uuid":"5701ac88-7e47-4fa9-a74b-3b850afe5eef","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:25:30.236Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"5701ac88-7e47-4fa9-a74b-3b850afe5eef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch98Le39LkgjmYKfqERyf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015hbjgcQEog7BgnCBWuMM8Y","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/COMMON.md <<'EOF'\n# Shared context for this design critique (read fully before starting)\n\nProduct: Email OS, a keyboard-first email client (Tauri 2 + Vue 3). This critique covers its **phone (compact) layout** used by the Android build, switched on at viewport width ≤719px (`.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`).\n\nRepository (read-only for you): `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate`, detached at commit f08fd85. Do NOT edit, commit, switch branches, install packages or delete anything in it. Write only inside `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/`.\n\nRead for context:\n- `PRODUCT.md` (users, brand personality \"focused, precise, trustworthy\", anti-references, design principles)\n- `DESIGN.md`, section \"Compact layout (phone)\" and anything it references (the file is long; read that section and the token tables)\n- `docs/ux-14-mobile-shell.md`, `docs/adr/0003-mobile-layout.md`\n- Compact CSS: `src/assets/mobile/*.css`; components: `src/components/mobile/*`, `src/components/InboxList.vue`, `src/components/SelectionBar.vue`, `src/components/ActionNotice.vue`, compose/reply components, `src/App.vue` (large; search it, don't read it whole)\n\nScreenshots of the current state:\n- `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/browser/*.png`: headless Chromium at 412×915 CSS px (device pixel ratio about 2.6), fixture data. The thin strip at the very top with account tabs (\"you@fixture.emailos · Inbox — 18 loaded\") and the yellow \"Preview\" label are **browser-preview harness chrome only**; they do not exist in the Android app. Do not critique them as part of the phone design. `desktop-*.png` show the desktop layout for comparison only.\n- `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/android/*.png`: the real Android 15 emulator (1080×2400), local debug build of f08fd85. Two of them show an \"Undo expired …\" notice that stays on screen after an action's Undo window ends (behaviour from before the phone work).\n\nScope: UI over features the app already has. These are deliberately OUT of scope and must not be counted as missing: send, HTML bodies, label chips, multiple splits, trash/spam/move, reply-all, forward, calendar, AI and voice. Drafts are local-only by design. No third-party brand names in the product.\n\nDo not open any directory named `email-os-mobile-refs` (private material). Do not read `.impeccable/critique/` (earlier critique runs; this review must be independent).\n\nViewing images: use your image-viewing tool on the PNG files above.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write shared critique context file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":244194,"output_tokens":1831,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":782},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1831,"cache_read_input_tokens":244194,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7921,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015hbjgcQEog7BgnCBWuMM8Y":{"command":"cat > /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/COMMON.md <<'EOF'\n# Shared context for this design critique (read fully before starting)\n\nProduct: Email OS, a keyboard-first email client (Tauri 2 + Vue 3). This critique covers its **phone (compact) layout** used by the Android build, switched on at viewport width ≤719px (`.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`).\n\nRepository (read-only for you): `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate`, detached at commit f08fd85. Do NOT edit, commit, switch branches, install packages or delete anything in it. Write only inside `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/`.\n\nRead for context:\n- `PRODUCT.md` (users, brand personality \"focused, precise, trustworthy\", anti-references, design principles)\n- `DESIGN.md`, section \"Compact layout (phone)\" and anything it references (the file is long; read that section and the token tables)\n- `docs/ux-14-mobile-shell.md`, `docs/adr/0003-mobile-layout.md`\n- Compact CSS: `src/assets/mobile/*.css`; components: `src/components/mobile/*`, `src/components/InboxList.vue`, `src/components/SelectionBar.vue`, `src/components/ActionNotice.vue`, compose/reply components, `src/App.vue` (large; search it, don't read it whole)\n\nScreenshots of the current state:\n- `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/browser/*.png`: headless Chromium at 412×915 CSS px (device pixel ratio about 2.6), fixture data. The thin strip at the very top with account tabs (\"you@fixture.emailos · Inbox — 18 loaded\") and the yellow \"Preview\" label are **browser-preview harness chrome only**; they do not exist in the Android app. Do not critique them as part of the phone design. `desktop-*.png` show the desktop layout for comparison only.\n- `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/android/*.png`: the real Android 15 emulator (1080×2400), local debug build of f08fd85. Two of them show an \"Undo expired …\" notice that stays on screen after an action's Undo window ends (behaviour from before the phone work).\n\nScope: UI over features the app already has. These are deliberately OUT of scope and must not be counted as missing: send, HTML bodies, label chips, multiple splits, trash/spam/move, reply-all, forward, calendar, AI and voice. Drafts are local-only by design. No third-party brand names in the product.\n\nDo not open any directory named `email-os-mobile-refs` (private material). Do not read `.impeccable/critique/` (earlier critique runs; this review must be independent).\n\nViewing images: use your image-viewing tool on the PNG files above.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write shared critique context file"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch98LaoBEpvJaae877niW","requestRef":"3e0f217b-4176-4c6a-80c3-a53dc363208d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"impeccable","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c5cb7fd-e42c-484b-9b6a-8a4e6cde3545","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:25:38.159Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
