{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"b86cd279ad8732a83f17c40f0a50b3923860e0187534446ab3aeeb3b72232175","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018gtiHhyS3WRAWoWeevgroC","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"Critique A1: list, selection, swipes, nav","role":"review","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"clientRequestId":"crit-r2-a1","task":"You are a senior product design director doing an independent design review (Assessment A of an \"Impeccable critique\") of a phone UI. Read `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/COMMON.md` first and follow it exactly (read-only repo, where to write, what to ignore).\n\nYour screens: the **mail list surfaces**: inbox list and rows (`inbox.png`, `inbox-scrolled-end.png`), the navigation drawer (`drawer.png`), swipe actions (`swipe-done.png`, `swipe-done-armed.png`, `swipe-remind-armed.png`), long-press selection (`selection.png`, `selection-with-notice.png`), the undo notice (`inbox-undo-toast.png`), the bottom navigation and split pill, the reminder picker sheet (`reminder-picker.png`), the command palette (`palette.png`), drafts list (`drafts.png`), plus the Android screenshots `android/inbox.png` and `android/selection.png`. Look at every one of these images with your image tool; read the matching CSS (`src/assets/mobile/list.css`, `shell.css`, `tokens.css`) and components.\n\nEvaluate as a design director: design specificity (authored for this product vs category-interchangeable), hierarchy, IA, composition, typography, colour, states, copy, edge cases, thumb reach and touch targets, motion. Then:\n1. Design-specificity verdict (one paragraph).\n2. Nielsen's 10 heuristics, each scored 0–4 with a one-line key issue (4 = genuinely excellent; most real interfaces total 20–32). Score only for your screens.\n3. Cognitive load: run this 8-item checklist (single focus; chunking ≤4 per group; grouping; visual hierarchy; one thing at a time; ≤4 visible options per decision; working memory; progressive disclosure), report failures and any decision point with more than 4 visible options.\n4. Emotional journey: peak-end, valleys, reassurance at high-stakes moments (bulk mark done, swipe commit, undo expiry).\n5. 2–3 specific strengths.\n6. 3–5 priority issues, each tagged P0 (blocks task) / P1 (major) / P2 (minor) / P3 (polish), with What, Why it matters, a concrete Fix (selectors, values, copy), and the evidence (screenshot name and/or file:line).\n7. Persona red flags for \"Alex\" (impatient power user), \"Casey\" (one-handed distracted phone user) and \"Sam\" (screen reader / low vision): name the exact elements that fail them.\n8. Minor observations (bullets) and 2–3 provocative questions.\n\nBe direct and specific; no \"consider exploring\". Verify claims against the code before stating them; if a screenshot artifact might be the harness rather than the product, say so instead of counting it.\n\nWrite the full review to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/A1-list.md` and also return it as your final message. Do not delegate, do not edit the repository."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0142sz71ZBHwVokHq3EXXKAk","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"Critique A2: reader, editors, pages","role":"review","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"clientRequestId":"crit-r2-a2","task":"You are a senior product design director doing an independent design review (Assessment A of an \"Impeccable critique\") of a phone UI. Read `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/COMMON.md` first and follow it exactly (read-only repo, where to write, what to ignore).\n\nYour screens: the **reader, editors and secondary pages**: reader (`reader.png`, `reader-scrolled-end.png`, `reader-more-sheet.png`, `reader-message-sheet.png`, `reader-undo-toast.png`), new message and reply (`compose.png`, `compose-keyboard.png`, `reply.png`), search (`search.png`, `search-results.png`), reminders (`reminders.png`), settings (`settings.png`, `settings-note-open.png`), activity (`activity.png`), contact (`contact.png`), plus the Android screenshots `android/reader-with-expired-notice.png`, `android/compose.png`, `android/settings.png`, `android/search-form-with-expired-notice.png`. Look at every one of these images with your image tool; read the matching CSS (`src/assets/mobile/reader.css`, `pages.css`, `shell.css`, `tokens.css`, and any compose CSS) and components.\n\nEvaluate as a design director: design specificity (authored for this product vs category-interchangeable), hierarchy, IA, composition, typography, colour, states, copy (the product voice is terse and factual and must never overstate what happened; drafts are local and never sent), edge cases, thumb reach and touch targets, keyboard-up behaviour. Then:\n1. Design-specificity verdict (one paragraph).\n2. Nielsen's 10 heuristics, each scored 0–4 with a one-line key issue (4 = genuinely excellent; most real interfaces total 20–32). Score only for your screens.\n3. Cognitive load: run this 8-item checklist (single focus; chunking ≤4 per group; grouping; visual hierarchy; one thing at a time; ≤4 visible options per decision; working memory; progressive disclosure), report failures and any decision point with more than 4 visible options.\n4. Emotional journey: peak-end, valleys, reassurance at high-stakes moments (leaving a draft, a failed save, mark done from the reader, changing a setting).\n5. 2–3 specific strengths.\n6. 3–5 priority issues, each tagged P0 (blocks task) / P1 (major) / P2 (minor) / P3 (polish), with What, Why it matters, a concrete Fix (selectors, values, copy), and the evidence (screenshot name and/or file:line).\n7. Persona red flags for \"Jordan\" (first-timer), \"Casey\" (one-handed distracted phone user) and \"Riley\" (stress tester: long subjects, failures, interruptions): name the exact elements that fail them.\n8. Minor observations (bullets) and 2–3 provocative questions.\n\nBe direct and specific; no \"consider exploring\". Verify claims against the code before stating them; if a screenshot artifact might be the harness rather than the product, say so instead of counting it.\n\nWrite the full review to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/A2-reader-pages.md` and also return it as your final message. Do not delegate, do not edit the repository."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D73YgJJPPDunRvrmseBvzY","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"Critique B: detector and browser evidence","role":"review","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"clientRequestId":"crit-r2-b","task":"You run Assessment B (deterministic detector + browser evidence) of an \"Impeccable critique\" of a phone UI. Read `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/COMMON.md` first and follow it (read-only repo, where to write). You do not do a subjective design review; you collect and triage detector evidence.\n\nTool: the Impeccable launcher at `/home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable` (self-contained binary). Run it with cwd `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate`. It needs a browser for rendered scans: set `IMPECCABLE_BROWSER=/tmp/chrome-rendered/chrome/linux-156.0.8078.80/chrome-linux64/chrome`. Run `.../impeccable detect --help` first to learn the exact flags (viewport options especially).\n\nSteps:\n1. Source scan: `impeccable detect --json src/components src/App.vue` (markup only; do not pass CSS-only files). Exit 0 = clean, 2 = findings. Record counts per rule and file:line locations.\n2. Rendered scan of the phone layout. Serve the existing production build: if `dist/` is missing or older than `src/`, run `pnpm build` (this writes only `dist/`, which is allowed). Start `npx vite preview --port 4873 --strictPort` in the background, record its PID, and scan `http://localhost:4873/` with the detector at a phone viewport (412 wide by 915 high if the detector supports a viewport flag; otherwise report the viewport it used and whether it was ≤719px wide, the compact breakpoint). Scan 3–5 representative states if the detector can reach them by URL; if it can only scan the landing state (the inbox), say so. Stop the preview server before you finish (kill the PID) and confirm it is gone.\n3. Do not attempt a live overlay or script injection into a human browser; there is no human browser tab here. Report \"overlay not available: headless environment\".\n4. Triage every finding: true issue, false positive (with reason, e.g. off-screen/inert desktop-only markup, harness chrome such as the top account-tab strip and yellow \"Preview\" label which exist only in the browser preview), or advisory. Check each against the CSS in `src/assets/mobile/` and the screenshots in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/browser/` before calling it.\n\nReturn: the CLI findings (counts, rule names, file locations), the rendered findings (counts, rules, selectors, viewport used), the triage table, and any skipped or failed steps with the concrete reason and command output. Write it to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/B-detector.md` and also return it as your final message. Do not delegate, do not edit the repository."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
