{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:29:23.196Z","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3Aff073a25-60a1-40e6-9d21-12438e4be376%3Adelegate-task%3Acrit-r2-b (Critique B: detector and browser evidence) [completed]:\nSaved to [B-detector.md](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/B-detector.md). Repository unchanged; preview server stopped and confirmed gone.\n\nAssessment B only, independent of Assessment A. Evidence was checked against the compact CSS and supplied inbox screenshots.\n\n| Pass | Exit | Primary findings | Advisories | Rules |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Source | 0 | 0 | 1 | `design-system-radius` ×1 |\n| Rendered inbox | 2 | 22 warnings | 0 | `tight-leading` ×18; `text-occlusion` ×4 |\n\n**Triage:** 18 instances of one shared line-height issue, four false positives, and one source consistency advisory.\n\nCommands ran from `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate`:\n\n```bash\n/home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable detect --help\n/home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable detect --json src/components src/App.vue\nIMPECCABLE_BROWSER=/tmp/chrome-rendered/chrome/linux-156.0.8078.80/chrome-linux64/chrome /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable detect --json --viewport 412x915 http://localhost:4873/\n```\n\nThe rendered scan used **412×915 CSS px**, within the ≤719px compact breakpoint. Existing `dist/` was newer than `src/`, so no build was needed.\n\nOnly the landing inbox was detector-scanned. The CLI supports URL navigation but has no interaction/state setup flags; no URL-based state selection was found in the application source. Other supplied screenshots do not count as additional detector passes.\n\nThe source finding was `design-system-radius` (“Radius outside DESIGN.md”), reported at [FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/src/components/FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115). Its snippet was `border-radius: 8px is outside the DESIGN.md rounded scale`. The declaration itself is at line 122.\n\nFor the rendered selectors below, `P` expands exactly to:\n\n```css\nsection.workspace-panel:nth-of-type(1) > div.app > main.app-main > section.central > ul.inbox-list.inbox-scroll\n```\n\nEvery rendered finding reports URL `http://localhost:4873/`, line `0`. `R#` denotes its position in [B-rendered.json](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/B-rendered.json); DOM indices include the date-group row.\n\n| ID | Rule | Selector after `P >` | Triage |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| S1 | `design-system-radius` | `src/components/FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115` | Advisory: undocumented 8px startup-card radius |\n| R1 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.focused > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: inherited 1.25× multiline leading |\n| R2 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(3) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R3 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(4) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R4 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(5) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R5 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(6) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R6 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(7) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R7 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(8) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R8 | `text-occlusion` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(8) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | False positive: 63% beneath floating navigation |\n| R9 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(9) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R10 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(10) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R11 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(11) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R12 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(12) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R13 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(13) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R14 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(14) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R15 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(15) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R16 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(16) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R17 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(17) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R18 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(18) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R19 | `tight-leading` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(19) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-preview` | True issue: same CSS |\n| R20 | `text-occlusion` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(8) > span.row-subject-snippet > span.row-subject` | False positive: 90% beneath context pill/split label |\n| R21 | `text-occlusion` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(9) > span.row-sender` | False positive: 100% beneath floating navigation |\n| R22 | `text-occlusion` | `li.inbox-row.read-disclosed:nth-of-type(9) > span.row-meta > span.row-trailing > time.row-time` | False positive: 100% beneath floating navigation |\n\nThe line-height findings are supported by [list.css:79](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/src/assets/mobile/list.css:79): rows set `line-height: 1.25`, inherited by the 14px, two-line previews at [list.css:229](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/src/assets/mobile/list.css:229). The detector reports `1.25x (need >=1.3)`. Both [inbox.png](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/browser/inbox.png) and [inbox-scrolled-end.png](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/browser/inbox-scrolled-end.png) show this multiline treatment. This is one shared minor readability issue; some instances are below the initial viewport. Any leading adjustment should also adjust the `2.5em` height cap.\n\nThe four overlaps are real at the sampled position but expected beneath floating controls. [shell.css:111](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/src/assets/mobile/shell.css:111) provides end padding and scroll padding; [tokens.css:25](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/src/assets/mobile/tokens.css:25) increases clearance to 122px plus safe area when the context pill is present. The end screenshot shows the final row fully above the controls. These findings do not establish persistently inaccessible text. The overlapping controls belong to the app, not the preview harness.\n\nThe radius finding remains an advisory. DESIGN.md’s machine-readable scale is `0/4/6/10/full`; compact [pages.css:617](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate/src/assets/mobile/pages.css:617) leaves the 8px radius intact. This conditional native startup gate is absent from the inbox screenshots and browser-fixture entry path. There is no screenshot evidence of a phone usability defect, and it should not be dismissed as desktop-only.\n\nFailures, skips, and cleanup:\n\n- Initial background launch recorded PID **4115858** but did not survive its command session. Its log was empty. The first rendered attempt exited **1**, producing `Error: net::ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED at http://localhost:4873/` and JSON `[]`.\n- Relaunched `npx vite preview --port 4873 --strictPort` as a background job with its parent shell kept alive by `wait`. PID **4116153** served successfully. Startup output included `➜ Local: http://localhost:4873/`. The retry exited **2** with no stderr.\n- Sent SIGTERM to PID **4116153** and descendants **4116165, 4116166, 4116179**. All were confirmed gone, as was initial PID 4115858. Port check returned `connect_ex=111 (connection refused)`. Evidence: [B-cleanup.log](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/B-cleanup.log).\n- **overlay not available: headless environment**. No human-browser injection or live overlay attempted.\n- Additional states were not URL-addressable through the available detector workflow. Android runtime behavior was not scanned.\n- No prior critique storage or private reference directories were read. All output was written inside the permitted review directory.\n- Raw source findings: [B-source.json](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/B-source.json). Full rendered findings and unshortened selectors: [B-rendered.json](/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r2/B-rendered.json).\n\nQuestions skipped: evidence-only sub-agent brief is explicit and complete."}
