x-height: 4.5em`). The X/save path with a real keyboard and a failure is untested on a device.\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]},"uuid":"50c9531f-2a1e-44cf-85b0-48645cc59e75","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:32:15.971Z","toolUseResult":"{\"sentMessage\":\"**[P1] Contact never got the phone treatment.**\\n- Recent-mail rows are 24px tall.\\n- The copy buttons for name and address are 24px and invisible until hover, so they never show on touch.\\n- The big name is secretly a \\\"search this sender\\\" button.\\n- *Fix:* 48px rows, visible 48px copy buttons, and an explicit \\\"Find mail from sender\\\" control.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable adapt`\\n\\n**[P2] Swipe cue and swipe action follow different rules.**\\n- A fast fling commits at 64px, well before the 35% point where the row shows it's armed.\\n- Real bug: the icon follows the swipe direction, not the action set in Settings. With swipe right set to \\\"Mark done\\\", you get a clock icon labelled \\\"Mark done\\\".\\n- A narrow reveal cuts off the label.\\n- *Fix:* show the armed state whenever a release would commit; pick the icon from the action; show the label only once the strip is wide enough.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n## Persona red flags\\n- **Alex (power user):** quick flings act with no cue. \\\"Select all\\\" hides \\\"loaded\\\". Reminder presets read like paragraphs. The empty command list shows the whole catalogue.\\n- **Casey (one-handed):** the menu and compose buttons sit in opposite top corners. Long-press has no visible cue. The bulk button is the smallest target. The notice and selection bar stack over the mail.\\n- **Sam (screen reader):** row checkboxes are `display:none` until selection mode, so there's no per-row route in.\\n- **Jordan (first-timer):** the reader tick and arrows don't say what they do. The search-results heading is secretly an edit button.\\n- **Riley (stress tester):** subjects longer than three lines are silently cut off in the reader (`max-height: 4.5em`). The X/save path with a real keyboard and a failure is untested on a device.\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"T3 Code","version":"0.1.10"}},"structuredContent":{"sentMessage":"**[P1] Contact never got the phone treatment.**\n- Recent-mail rows are 24px tall.\n- The copy buttons for name and address are 24px and invisible until hover, so they never show on touch.\n- The big name is secretly a \"search this sender\" button.\n- *Fix:* 48px rows, visible 48px copy buttons, and an explicit \"Find mail from sender\" control.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable adapt`\n\n**[P2] Swipe cue and swipe action follow different rules.**\n- A fast fling commits at 64px, well before the 35% point where the row shows it's armed.\n- Real bug: the icon follows the swipe direction, not the action set in Settings. With swipe right set to \"Mark done\", you get a clock icon labelled \"Mark done\".\n- A narrow reveal cuts off the label.\n- *Fix:* show the armed state whenever a release would commit; pick the icon from the action; show the label only once the strip is wide enough.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n## Persona red flags\n- **Alex (power user):** quick flings act with no cue. \"Select all\" hides \"loaded\". Reminder presets read like paragraphs. The empty command list shows the whole catalogue.\n- **Casey (one-handed):** the menu and compose buttons sit in opposite top corners. Long-press has no visible cue. The bulk button is the smallest target. The notice and selection bar stack over the mail.\n- **Sam (screen reader):** row checkboxes are `display:none` until selection mode, so there's no per-row route in.\n- **Jordan (first-timer):** the reader tick and arrows don't say what they do. The search-results heading is secretly an edit button.\n- **Riley (stress tester):** subjects longer than three lines are silently cut off in the reader (`max-height: 4.5em`). The X/save path with a real keyboard and a failure is untested on a device.","message":"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c6d6539-6f0e-4946-aac4-d2d195eb69c6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"50c9531f-2a1e-44cf-85b0-48645cc59e75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch98rms2ScYRT3hvW3cKT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01THeZtY9nXPhu5ENu9dA3Ht","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\" and say \"Times in UTC\" once.\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \"New draft\" button.\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\n- \"No operations yet\" → \"No actions yet\".\n\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\nA2 recommends a visible \"Save and close\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \"dismiss\" rather than \"save\". You chose X-only with the fixed \"never sent\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \"Saved locally\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \"keep\" more clearly.\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If \"done\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":278327,"output_tokens":1320,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1710,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":278327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1710},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":5553,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01THeZtY9nXPhu5ENu9dA3Ht":{"message":"## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\" and say \"Times in UTC\" once.\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \"New draft\" button.\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\n- \"No operations yet\" → \"No actions yet\".\n\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\nA2 recommends a visible \"Save and close\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \"dismiss\" rather than \"save\". You chose X-only with the fixed \"never sent\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \"Saved locally\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \"keep\" more clearly.\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If \"done\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch98ri36XpqcyR9AJww9i","requestRef":"fef99a82-627c-4532-84ae-aa90475fdf71","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"t3-code","attributionMcpTool":"send_to_user","type":"assistant","uuid":"b03efda4-b522-47ce-a6a2-edea651d5947","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:32:21.496Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"b03efda4-b522-47ce-a6a2-edea651d5947","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9f6f758c-81e7-4f81-8936-fdb94b5d7a51","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THeZtY9nXPhu5ENu9dA3Ht","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## Minor observations\\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \\\"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\\\" and say \\\"Times in UTC\\\" once.\\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \\\"New draft\\\" button.\\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\\n- \\\"No operations yet\\\" → \\\"No actions yet\\\".\\n\\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\\nA2 recommends a visible \\\"Save and close\\\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \\\"dismiss\\\" rather than \\\"save\\\". You chose X-only with the fixed \\\"never sent\\\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \\\"Saved locally\\\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \\\"keep\\\" more clearly.\\n\\n## Questions to consider\\n- If \\\"done\\\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]},"uuid":"3b3d0e2d-6e70-4ba5-a0de-ef749c3fdf5a","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:32:21.539Z","toolUseResult":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## Minor observations\\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \\\"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\\\" and say \\\"Times in UTC\\\" once.\\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \\\"New draft\\\" button.\\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\\n- \\\"No operations yet\\\" → \\\"No actions yet\\\".\\n\\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\\nA2 recommends a visible \\\"Save and close\\\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \\\"dismiss\\\" rather than \\\"save\\\". You chose X-only with the fixed \\\"never sent\\\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \\\"Saved locally\\\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \\\"keep\\\" more clearly.\\n\\n## Questions to consider\\n- If \\\"done\\\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"T3 Code","version":"0.1.10"}},"structuredContent":{"sentMessage":"## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\" and say \"Times in UTC\" once.\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \"New draft\" button.\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\n- \"No operations yet\" → \"No actions yet\".\n\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\nA2 recommends a visible \"Save and close\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \"dismiss\" rather than \"save\". You chose X-only with the fixed \"never sent\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \"Saved locally\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \"keep\" more clearly.\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If \"done\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?","message":"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b03efda4-b522-47ce-a6a2-edea651d5947","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"cfb83949ea447f5799b09dcce3e16967d66719105ff8344b06b310be91c0f270","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FkXP8Th9nA82qXPCyDRPih","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"**[P1] Contact never got the phone treatment.**\n- Recent-mail rows are 24px tall.\n- The copy buttons for name and address are 24px and invisible until hover, so they never show on touch.\n- The big name is secretly a \"search this sender\" button.\n- *Fix:* 48px rows, visible 48px copy buttons, and an explicit \"Find mail from sender\" control.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable adapt`\n\n**[P2] Swipe cue and swipe action follow different rules.**\n- A fast fling commits at 64px, well before the 35% point where the row shows it's armed.\n- Real bug: the icon follows the swipe direction, not the action set in Settings. With swipe right set to \"Mark done\", you get a clock icon labelled \"Mark done\".\n- A narrow reveal cuts off the label.\n- *Fix:* show the armed state whenever a release would commit; pick the icon from the action; show the label only once the strip is wide enough.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n## Persona red flags\n- **Alex (power user):** quick flings act with no cue. \"Select all\" hides \"loaded\". Reminder presets read like paragraphs. The empty command list shows the whole catalogue.\n- **Casey (one-handed):** the menu and compose buttons sit in opposite top corners. Long-press has no visible cue. The bulk button is the smallest target. The notice and selection bar stack over the mail.\n- **Sam (screen reader):** row checkboxes are `display:none` until selection mode, so there's no per-row route in.\n- **Jordan (first-timer):** the reader tick and arrows don't say what they do. The search-results heading is secretly an edit button.\n- **Riley (stress tester):** subjects longer than three lines are silently cut off in the reader (`max-height: 4.5em`). The X/save path with a real keyboard and a failure is untested on a device."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01THeZtY9nXPhu5ENu9dA3Ht","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\" and say \"Times in UTC\" once.\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \"New draft\" button.\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\n- \"No operations yet\" → \"No actions yet\".\n\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\nA2 recommends a visible \"Save and close\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \"dismiss\" rather than \"save\". You chose X-only with the fixed \"never sent\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \"Saved locally\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \"keep\" more clearly.\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If \"done\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"4016dafaf3312c6f29335dcf6b5cf75a825a2ad781bfc2f79ef2549ea007df4f","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FkXP8Th9nA82qXPCyDRPih","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"**[P1] Contact never got the phone treatment.**\\n- Recent-mail rows are 24px tall.\\n- The copy buttons for name and address are 24px and invisible until hover, so they never show on touch.\\n- The big name is secretly a \\\"search this sender\\\" button.\\n- *Fix:* 48px rows, visible 48px copy buttons, and an explicit \\\"Find mail from sender\\\" control.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable adapt`\\n\\n**[P2] Swipe cue and swipe action follow different rules.**\\n- A fast fling commits at 64px, well before the 35% point where the row shows it's armed.\\n- Real bug: the icon follows the swipe direction, not the action set in Settings. With swipe right set to \\\"Mark done\\\", you get a clock icon labelled \\\"Mark done\\\".\\n- A narrow reveal cuts off the label.\\n- *Fix:* show the armed state whenever a release would commit; pick the icon from the action; show the label only once the strip is wide enough.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n## Persona red flags\\n- **Alex (power user):** quick flings act with no cue. \\\"Select all\\\" hides \\\"loaded\\\". Reminder presets read like paragraphs. The empty command list shows the whole catalogue.\\n- **Casey (one-handed):** the menu and compose buttons sit in opposite top corners. Long-press has no visible cue. The bulk button is the smallest target. The notice and selection bar stack over the mail.\\n- **Sam (screen reader):** row checkboxes are `display:none` until selection mode, so there's no per-row route in.\\n- **Jordan (first-timer):** the reader tick and arrows don't say what they do. The search-results heading is secretly an edit button.\\n- **Riley (stress tester):** subjects longer than three lines are silently cut off in the reader (`max-height: 4.5em`). The X/save path with a real keyboard and a failure is untested on a device.\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THeZtY9nXPhu5ENu9dA3Ht","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## Minor observations\\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector, 18 rows). Raise it to 1.35 and adjust the 2.5em height cap.\\n- The reminder picker repeats the timezone in every option. Use \\\"Wed 18 Nov · 8:00 AM\\\" and say \\\"Times in UTC\\\" once.\\n- The drawer divider is placed by position (`index === 8`), so it shifts when options are hidden. Group by meaning: Mail / Follow-up / Utilities.\\n- The command palette has no visible close button on the phone.\\n- The bottom of the list may not clear a tall selection-plus-notice stack, because the list's bottom padding doesn't count the dock. A1 inferred this from the CSS; it isn't in any screenshot yet.\\n- Settings radios are browser blue; `accent-color: var(--focus-accent)` would match the rest of the app.\\n- Drafts has both the top pencil and a full-width \\\"New draft\\\" button.\\n- In selection mode the text jumps 48px right.\\n- \\\"No operations yet\\\" → \\\"No actions yet\\\".\\n\\n## Disagreement with your earlier decision\\nA2 recommends a visible \\\"Save and close\\\" text button instead of the X, because the X looks like \\\"dismiss\\\" rather than \\\"save\\\". You chose X-only with the fixed \\\"never sent\\\" phrase last round, so I've left this out of the priorities. The status line already says \\\"Saved locally\\\". If you want a middle ground, a tick icon instead of the X would say \\\"keep\\\" more clearly.\\n\\n## Questions to consider\\n- If \\\"done\\\" is the core promise, why does its button need a hidden label to explain itself, and reuse the same tick for the opposite action?\\n- What do the two permanent bottom containers earn on an inbox with one tab and two icons?\\n- Should a successful session end on a note about the Undo you just lost?\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]}}
