{"parentUuid":"3b3d0e2d-6e70-4ba5-a0de-ef749c3fdf5a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch98sowa3UuLEaEqLUA28","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I'm saving the snapshot."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2741,"cache_read_input_tokens":280037,"output_tokens":2012,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2741,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2012,"cache_read_input_tokens":280037,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2741},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch98sjq2GT145XDj7p5LU","requestRef":"cc40f731-9431-44e4-8db5-549c928b1c60","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"t3-code","attributionMcpTool":"send_to_user","type":"assistant","uuid":"385ee5c4-2442-4683-9415-baaff22088a3","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:32:23.694Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"385ee5c4-2442-4683-9415-baaff22088a3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch98sowa3UuLEaEqLUA28","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011cMKS9VmWMpGBLGSD52njf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate && S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad; cat > $S/crit-body.md <<'EOF'\nMethod: three isolated GPT-6.1-SOL sub-agents, high effort (A1 list/selection/swipes/drawer · A2 reader/editors/pages · B detector). Commit f08fd85.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Exact outcome states; Undo has no visible deadline |\n| 2 | Match system / real world | 3 | Natural row order; \"Provider mail\", \"operations\" are product jargon |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back/Undo work everywhere; settled notice cannot be dismissed |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Contact keeps 24px desktop targets; bulk primary 40px vs 48px |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Fling commits at 64px before armed cue; \"loaded\" scope hidden |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Unlabelled reader dock glyphs; hidden long-press selection entry |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, long-press, bulk, commands |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet rows; stacked floating containers |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 2 | Draft failure recovery strong; expired-Undo text names a fix without routing |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; touch meanings in hidden labels |\nHalves: A1 25/40, A2 26/40. Not like-for-like with the previous run (different reviewers and split).\n\n## Design specificity\nIdentity lives in behaviour (truthful states, local-only drafts, coverage notices). Frame (two top rings, single-tab pill, two-icon nav pill) is category-interchangeable. Detector: source clean except design-system-radius advisory (FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115, 8px); rendered inbox 412x915: tight-leading x18 on .row-preview (line-height 1.25, list.css:79) true issue; text-occlusion x4 false positives (under floating bars at sampled scroll). No overlay (headless).\n\n## Priority issues\n1. [P1] Settled success notice persists after Undo expiry (amber, no dismiss, recovery wording binds a different conversation). Fix: collapse to neutral line + Dismiss + View in Done; keep pending/failed/unknown. ActionNotice.vue, useActionNotice.ts, notices.css. clarify + harden.\n2. [P1] Reader dock: six unlabelled equal glyphs; tick toggles done/not done; up/down = conversations. Fix: visible label on done; optionally move star/prev/next into More. ReaderView.vue:944-987. clarify + layout.\n3. [P1] Selection entry hidden (long-press only, .row-select display:none), \"Select all (N)\" hides loaded scope, primary 40px (list.css:405). Fix: visible Select control, \"Select N loaded\", 48px, optional bulk review sheet. adapt + clarify.\n4. [P1] Contact: 24px recent rows (style.css:1070), 24px hover-only copy buttons, name is hidden search action. Fix: 48px rows, visible copy, explicit \"Find mail from sender\". adapt.\n5. [P2] Swipe: fling commit (64px, >0.5px/ms) bypasses 35% armed cue (useSwipeAction.ts); glyph chosen by direction not configured action (InboxList.vue:736); label clipped at narrow reveal. harden.\n\n## Persona red flags\nAlex: fling without cue, hidden loaded scope, verbose picker, full palette. Casey: top-corner menu/compose, invisible long-press, smallest bulk target, stacked dock. Sam: no per-row checkbox route before selection mode. Jordan: unlabelled reader glyphs, search heading is an edit button. Riley: reader subject clipped at 3 lines (reader.css:10), IME+failure untested on device.\n\n## Minor observations\nPreview leading 1.25; picker repeats timezone; drawer separator index===8; palette no close button; dock height not in scroll clearance (inferred); radios not accent; Drafts duplicate create; 48px text jump in selection; \"No operations yet\" wording. A2 recommended visible \"Save and close\" text instead of X: conflicts with owner decision (X only), excluded.\n\n## Questions\nDone needs a hidden label and reuses its glyph for the opposite; what do the two permanent bottom containers earn; should a successful session end on lost Undo?\nEOF\nIMPECCABLE_CRITIQUE_META='{\"target\":\"phone layout key screens (src/assets/mobile)\",\"total_score\":25,\"max_score\":40,\"na_heuristics\":\"\",\"p0_count\":0,\"p1_count\":4}' /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable critique-storage write src/assets/mobile $S/crit-body.md 2>&1 | tail -1; rm -f $S/crit-body.md; /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable critique-storage trend src/assets/mobile 5 2>&1 | grep -oE '\"total_score\": ?[0-9]+|\"max_score\": ?[0-9]+' | tr '\\n' ' '","description":"Persist critique snapshot and read trend"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2741,"cache_read_input_tokens":280037,"output_tokens":2012,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2741,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2012,"cache_read_input_tokens":280037,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2741},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":16357,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011cMKS9VmWMpGBLGSD52njf":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate && S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad; cat > $S/crit-body.md <<'EOF'\nMethod: three isolated GPT-6.1-SOL sub-agents, high effort (A1 list/selection/swipes/drawer · A2 reader/editors/pages · B detector). Commit f08fd85.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Exact outcome states; Undo has no visible deadline |\n| 2 | Match system / real world | 3 | Natural row order; \"Provider mail\", \"operations\" are product jargon |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back/Undo work everywhere; settled notice cannot be dismissed |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Contact keeps 24px desktop targets; bulk primary 40px vs 48px |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Fling commits at 64px before armed cue; \"loaded\" scope hidden |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Unlabelled reader dock glyphs; hidden long-press selection entry |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, long-press, bulk, commands |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet rows; stacked floating containers |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 2 | Draft failure recovery strong; expired-Undo text names a fix without routing |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; touch meanings in hidden labels |\nHalves: A1 25/40, A2 26/40. Not like-for-like with the previous run (different reviewers and split).\n\n## Design specificity\nIdentity lives in behaviour (truthful states, local-only drafts, coverage notices). Frame (two top rings, single-tab pill, two-icon nav pill) is category-interchangeable. Detector: source clean except design-system-radius advisory (FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115, 8px); rendered inbox 412x915: tight-leading x18 on .row-preview (line-height 1.25, list.css:79) true issue; text-occlusion x4 false positives (under floating bars at sampled scroll). No overlay (headless).\n\n## Priority issues\n1. [P1] Settled success notice persists after Undo expiry (amber, no dismiss, recovery wording binds a different conversation). Fix: collapse to neutral line + Dismiss + View in Done; keep pending/failed/unknown. ActionNotice.vue, useActionNotice.ts, notices.css. clarify + harden.\n2. [P1] Reader dock: six unlabelled equal glyphs; tick toggles done/not done; up/down = conversations. Fix: visible label on done; optionally move star/prev/next into More. ReaderView.vue:944-987. clarify + layout.\n3. [P1] Selection entry hidden (long-press only, .row-select display:none), \"Select all (N)\" hides loaded scope, primary 40px (list.css:405). Fix: visible Select control, \"Select N loaded\", 48px, optional bulk review sheet. adapt + clarify.\n4. [P1] Contact: 24px recent rows (style.css:1070), 24px hover-only copy buttons, name is hidden search action. Fix: 48px rows, visible copy, explicit \"Find mail from sender\". adapt.\n5. [P2] Swipe: fling commit (64px, >0.5px/ms) bypasses 35% armed cue (useSwipeAction.ts); glyph chosen by direction not configured action (InboxList.vue:736); label clipped at narrow reveal. harden.\n\n## Persona red flags\nAlex: fling without cue, hidden loaded scope, verbose picker, full palette. Casey: top-corner menu/compose, invisible long-press, smallest bulk target, stacked dock. Sam: no per-row checkbox route before selection mode. Jordan: unlabelled reader glyphs, search heading is an edit button. Riley: reader subject clipped at 3 lines (reader.css:10), IME+failure untested on device.\n\n## Minor observations\nPreview leading 1.25; picker repeats timezone; drawer separator index===8; palette no close button; dock height not in scroll clearance (inferred); radios not accent; Drafts duplicate create; 48px text jump in selection; \"No operations yet\" wording. A2 recommended visible \"Save and close\" text instead of X: conflicts with owner decision (X only), excluded.\n\n## Questions\nDone needs a hidden label and reuses its glyph for the opposite; what do the two permanent bottom containers earn; should a successful session end on lost Undo?\nEOF\nIMPECCABLE_CRITIQUE_META='{\"target\":\"phone layout key screens (src/assets/mobile)\",\"total_score\":25,\"max_score\":40,\"na_heuristics\":\"\",\"p0_count\":0,\"p1_count\":4}' /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable critique-storage write src/assets/mobile $S/crit-body.md 2>&1 | tail -1; rm -f $S/crit-body.md; /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable critique-storage trend src/assets/mobile 5 2>&1 | grep -oE '\"total_score\": ?[0-9]+|\"max_score\": ?[0-9]+' | tr '\\n' ' '","description":"Persist critique snapshot and read trend"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch98sjq2GT145XDj7p5LU","requestRef":"cc40f731-9431-44e4-8db5-549c928b1c60","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"t3-code","attributionMcpTool":"send_to_user","type":"assistant","uuid":"82a2c41a-da1e-4738-84f9-ea133e2cc0aa","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:32:40.052Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
