{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","id":"c715d22f-5a12-46fa-84f4-6607156f78c0","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:34:59.768Z","version":"2.1.326","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"910f92d9bd9f283f9ce514220272f6b9ed1f306559080f25290301d617c09838","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"4db2d7e9-c5e9-4e23-9232-bf28d4c57b30","keep":362,"tail":["6f6a492f956d6bf96bb198210d628bee17842eabf7ffb6b6ae5ff90ecb3b2e73","b87b42852f335bc5c3efe5f61a641db1b6f18677c91cbe96a7e4354b60709839"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",362,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",363,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"4f78f76d93fe9485e4cd42a90c92fd5c06cf1e13edd37f7d18f484fec1630633"}
{"parentUuid":"767b168f-79c6-453f-858e-a61949365bb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch995TDyDf7ynrwsaeysd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The critique is done: 25/40, with four P1 issues and one P2. The full report, the scores and a note on the trend are in the messages above.\n\nThis 25 doesn't mean last round's fixes did nothing. The three GPT-6.1-SOL reviewers looked at parts of the app no earlier review had covered, and none of the five issues we fixed came back.\n\nThe reviewers agreed on the identity: it works because the app never overstates what it did. The weak spot is the screen frame, which still feels like a desktop layout squeezed onto a phone.\n\nOne reviewer suggested putting a \"Save and close\" text button back in place of the X. That goes against your X-only decision, so I left it out of the priorities.\n\nYour answers: all four P1s plus the swipe P2, the \"Undo expired\" notice first, and only a label on the Done button in the reader. In that order, the work is:\n\n1. **`/impeccable harden` + `/impeccable clarify` for the \"Undo expired\" notice.**\n   - Once a confirmed action's Undo window ends, the notice shrinks to a short neutral line with Dismiss and \"View in Done\".\n   - Its recovery always points at the notice's own conversation, never the one on screen.\n   - Pending, failed and unknown outcomes don't change.\n   - Main files: `ActionNotice.vue`, `useActionNotice.ts`, `src/assets/mobile/notices.css`.\n2. **`/impeccable clarify` for the reader's action bar.**\n   - The done button gets a visible \"Done\" / \"Not done\" label next to its icon, at least 48px tall.\n   - All six controls stay (`ReaderView.vue`, `reader.css`).\n3. **`/impeccable adapt` + `/impeccable clarify` for selection.**\n   - Add a visible 48px \"Select\" control in the list that starts selection mode without selecting anything.\n   - \"Select all (18)\" becomes \"Select 18 loaded\".\n   - The main button is at least 48px tall (`list.css:405`).\n   - The confirmation sheet before bulk done is optional. It fits the \"preview before acting\" principle but adds a tap; I'd hold it back unless you want it.\n4. **`/impeccable adapt` for the Contact page.**\n   - Recent-mail rows and copy buttons become 48px and always visible.\n   - A visible \"Find mail from sender\" control replaces the hidden search on the name.\n5. **`/impeccable harden` for swipes.**\n   - The row shows its armed state whenever releasing would commit, including fast flings.\n   - The icon follows the action you set in Settings, not the swipe direction. This is a confirmed bug.\n   - The label shows only once the revealed strip is wide enough.\n6. **`/impeccable polish`** as a last pass, then screenshots, the emulator check and an update to PR #80.\n\nYou can ask me to run these one at a time, all at once, or in any order you prefer. Last round they were built by GPT-6 Luna threads working through checklists, with me reviewing; I can set that up the same way.\n\nRe-run `/impeccable critique` after fixes to see your score improve."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_read_input_tokens":286243,"output_tokens":1018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1018,"cache_read_input_tokens":286243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch995PuHgPaQt6X2NQm8M","requestRef":"c715d22f-5a12-46fa-