{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","prNumber":84,"prUrl":"https://github.com/BbrSofiane/email-os/pull/84","prRepository":"BbrSofiane/email-os","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:45:25.444Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7d5ef1f0-f769-4804-a00f-2ed154a2ff68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch99saKPmaBBZLJSHF6z9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm keeping the fix to compact layouts so the desktop notice stays as it is, since its single-line slot is a deliberate design. In compact, once the notice has settled and the undo window is closed, I'll hide the expanded state.\n\nI'm working out how to make the compact notice end quietly once a settled success has run its course, auto-hiding it a few seconds after the undo window closes while failed or pending states stay visible. I'm also weighing whether a Dismiss button belongs alongside Undo in compact, and checking whether there's an existing function I can use to clear the last-action slot.\n\nI'm planning a dismiss path for the single-action notice, keyed on its operation ID so it can be hidden without touching mailbox state. Whether Dismiss should be allowed during the undo window is still open, since that would cut off Undo on a phone, so I'm leaning toward letting the notice auto-hide once the window closes for settled results while leaving pending and failed states visible.\n\nI'm sorting out the compact-only behaviour for the notice that sits in the single-action slot: a failed or unknown result will get an Activity button that opens the Activity page, and a pending result that settles after the undo window has closed will hide at that point. The same rule seems right for group notices, so I'll check how dismissGroupNotice is wired and handle groups in the same way.\n\nI'm noting that the dismiss-and-auto-hide rule should also cover group notices: once a settled group's undo window closes, it hides, while unsettled ones keep their Activity route. I'll also check the recovery wording, since \"Mark not done restores…\" would vanish on a phone for settled results, which seems acceptable. Desktop stays as it is, so the next step is looking at the reader label in ReaderView around lines 944–987.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4232,"cache_read_input_tokens":291318,"output_tokens":1443,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1284},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4232,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1443,"cache_read_input_tokens":291318,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4232},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14657,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch99sWxUUTFZyvezpFtjX","requestRef":"802cba53-2622-4f29-8c58-de89c24434a7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9bfb1db2-33fc-48f9-9ae3-dc406e24a8c9","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:45:41.682Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
