{"parentUuid":"d0d035f1-9da0-42f1-86ae-2d01e9c15c6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch99v5yemdgZgEYSRpQen","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VKdNWsWYCH4N4TEMR1aejY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review; mkdir -p $R/p6-notice-swipe $R/p6-reader-contact $R/p6-selection; cat > $R/P6-RULES.md <<'EOF'\n# Rules for every p6 checklist (read before the first item)\n\nRepository: Email OS (Tauri 2 + Vue 3 + TypeScript). You work in your own worktree on the branch named in item 1, created from `origin/mobile/integration`. Pull requests target `mobile/integration` (`gh pr create -R BbrSofiane/email-os --base mobile/integration`), never `main`.\n\nScope: the phone (compact) layout only: `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, `layoutMode === 'compact'`, or a `compact` prop. The regular (desktop) layout must render and behave exactly as today; its existing tests must keep passing unchanged unless an item says otherwise. Compact CSS lives only in `src/assets/mobile/*.css` under `.app[data-layout=\"compact\"]`, no `!important`. Do not touch `src/assets/style.css` except where an item says so.\n\nProduct voice: terse and factual; never claim more than the app knows (pending, confirmed, failed and unknown stay distinct). Out of scope features (do not add): send, HTML bodies, label chips, multiple splits, trash/spam/move, reply-all, forward, calendar, AI, voice. No third-party brand names. Do not open any directory named `email-os-mobile-refs`.\n\nWorking protocol: take the first unticked item in your checklist, do it, run its Check, then tick it (`- [x]`) and add one line under it starting `Decision:` (what you chose where the item left a choice), commit with a clear message, push (retry on transient remote errors). Then continue straight to the next item in the same turn; do not stop to report between items. Stop only when every item is ticked, or when you are blocked: then write `Blocked:` with the exact reason under the item and stop.\n\nCode: readable multi-line code that matches the surrounding style; no minified one-liners. No `implement` skill, no delegation or sub-agents, no cargo or Android builds (the reviewer does those). Tests: unit tests with Vitest next to the existing ones; rendered (real Chromium) tests run with `EMAIL_OS_RUN_RENDERED=1 EMAIL_OS_RENDERED_LAYOUT_CHROME=/tmp/chrome-rendered/chrome/linux-156.0.8078.80/chrome-linux64/chrome pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts <file>`; screenshots with `EMAIL_OS_RENDERED_LAYOUT_CHROME=<same path> EMAIL_OS_SCREENSHOT_DIR=<dir> mise run screenshots:mobile` (test file `tests/layout/mobile-screenshots.rendered.test.ts`). The machine has 4 cores and another thread may be running tests: run focused tests per item and the full suites only in the final item.\nEOF\ncat > $R/p6-notice-swipe/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p6 track A: finished actions end quietly; swipe cue matches the action\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first. Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p6-notice-swipe/`.\n\nBackground (design critique, 2026-11-17): on the phone, after a confirmed action's Undo window ends, the notice stays on every screen (list, reader, search, selection) with amber text \"Undo expired — Mark not done restores the whole conversation to Inbox\" and no way to dismiss it; its wording also reads as if it applied to the conversation now on screen. Separately, a fast swipe commits before the row shows its armed cue, and the swipe icon follows the swipe direction instead of the configured action.\n\nCode map: `src/components/ActionNotice.vue` (statusText/statusTone/undoVisible/undoExpired, template), `src/composables/useActionNotice.ts` (builds the notice from `mailbox.lastAction` / `mailbox.lastGroup`, `nowMs` timer), `src/assets/mobile/notices.css`, the `<ActionNotice …>` in `src/App.vue` (inside `.list-dock`), `src/composables/useSwipeAction.ts` (`armed`, `finish`, `shouldCommit`), the swipe underlay in `src/components/InboxList.vue` (around the `row-swipe-underlay` span, RowGlyph name chosen by `revealed`), `src/assets/mobile/list.css` (`.row-swipe-underlay`).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p6-notice-swipe origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Settled single-action notices leave quietly on the phone. Add a `compact?: boolean` prop to `ActionNotice` (App passes `layoutMode === 'compact'`). In compact mode only, for a single-action notice (not a group): when the status tone is `settled` (confirmed or cancelled, or an undo whose compensations all confirmed) AND the Undo window is closed (`undoVisible` false), the notice is not shown at all: render the empty state (`action-notice-empty`), so the dock collapses. It is never hidden while pending, failed or outcome unknown; those keep their current text. The amber \"Undo expired — …\" clause is therefore never shown for a settled single action on the phone; for a still-pending action whose window has passed, keep today's wording. If the notice becomes settled later (pending → confirmed after the window), it disappears then. Regular layout: unchanged (the expired clause still shows there). The polite live region (`role=\"status\"`) must stay mounted so announcements still work. Unit tests in the existing ActionNotice/useActionNotice test files (find them with `grep -rln \"ActionNotice\" tests src`): compact + confirmed + window open → shown with Undo; compact + confirmed + window closed → empty; compact + pending + window closed → shown with today's expired wording; compact + failed → shown; regular + confirmed + window closed → shows \"Undo expired — …\" as today. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <those files>`.\n\n- [ ] 3. Settled group notices behave the same. For a group notice in compact mode: when every member is confirmed (the group status tone is `settled`) and the group Undo window is closed, hide it the same way. Never hide while `acceptanceUnknown`, partial, failed, unknown or pending. Unit tests for the group cases (settled+closed hidden; partial/failed shown; acceptanceUnknown shown with Check acceptance). Check: `pnpm vitest run <the same files>`.\n\n- [ ] 4. Problems link to Activity on the phone. In compact mode, when a single-action or group notice's text says \"see Activity\" (failed, outcome unknown, restore failed/unknown) or \"recover individual members from Activity\", show a text button \"Activity\" (min 48px high, `var(--focus-accent)`, same style as the Undo button) in the notice's action slot that opens the Activity page through the same action the drawer uses (find it in `src/components/mobile/MobileDrawer.vue` / `App.vue`, e.g. an `executeAction('activity')`-style call; emit an event such as `openActivity` from ActionNotice and handle it in App). Do not show it for pending or settled notices. Regular layout unchanged. Unit tests: failed → Activity button present and emits; confirmed → absent; regular → absent. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <files> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 5. Rendered check and screenshot for the notice. In the rendered list test that covers the undo toast (find `inbox-undo-toast` in `tests/layout/mobile-screenshots.rendered.test.ts` and the matching rendered test), add an assertion at 412×915: after marking a row done and letting the Undo window pass (use the existing fixture/time controls; if the window cannot be advanced in the rendered harness, assert through the unit tests only and say so in the Decision), the `.list-dock .action-notice` has zero height. Add screenshot `inbox-after-undo-window.png` showing the list with no lingering notice (or skip with a Decision if the window cannot be advanced). Check: the rendered file passes.\n\n- [ ] 6. One commit rule for swipes. In `useSwipeAction.ts` a release commits when the drag reaches 35% of the row width OR when it moved at least 64px faster than 0.5px/ms. The armed cue only follows the 35% rule, so a fast fling acts with no cue. Make the cue and the release agree: compute velocity during `move` (distance over elapsed time since pointerdown, or over the last ~80ms of samples, whichever the code can do cleanly) and set `armed` true whenever a release at that moment would commit under the same predicate `finish` uses (extract one function `wouldCommit(dx, velocity)` used by both). Keep the 64px and 0.5px/ms values. Unit tests in the existing useSwipeAction tests: a slow 100px drag is not armed and does not commit; a fast 80px drag is armed before release and commits; a 40% slow drag is armed and commits. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <the useSwipeAction test file> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 7. The swipe icon follows the configured action. In `InboxList.vue` the underlay's RowGlyph is chosen by direction (`revealed === 'right'` → reminder) while its label follows the configured action (`props.swipeRight` / `props.swipeLeft`). Derive one resolved action per reveal (`remind` or `done`) and use it for both: `remind` → glyph `reminder`, label \"Remind\"; `done` → glyph `restore` with \"Mark not done\" in the Done context, otherwise glyph `archive` with \"Mark done\". Also use it for the underlay's colour class (the `.remind` / `.done` class must follow the action, not the side; check `list.css` selectors). Unit test: with swipeRight = 'done' and swipeLeft = 'remind', a right reveal shows the archive glyph, \"Mark done\" and the done class; a left reveal shows the reminder glyph, \"Remind\" and the remind class. Check: `pnpm vitest run <InboxList tests> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 8. The label never shows clipped. At narrow reveals the label is cut off (\"Mark do…\"). In compact CSS show only the 24px icon until the revealed strip is wide enough for icon plus label: hide the label text (keep it in the DOM for nothing; the underlay is `aria-hidden`) when `--swipe-distance` is below 128px. CSS cannot compare a custom property, so add a class from InboxList (e.g. `labelled` when `Math.abs(offset) >= 128`) and style `.row-swipe-underlay:not(.labelled) .row-swipe-label { display: none }` (wrap the label in a span with that class). Rendered assertion at 412×915 in the swipe rendered test: at a 100px reveal the label is not displayed and the icon is fully inside the underlay; at the armed distance the label is fully visible (its right edge ≤ the underlay's right edge and left edge ≥ its left edge). Re-run the swipe screenshots (`swipe-done.png`, `swipe-done-armed.png`, `swipe-remind-armed.png`) into this track's directory. Check: the rendered file passes and the three screenshots exist.\n\n- [ ] 9. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` into your branch if it moved (`git fetch origin && git merge origin/mobile/integration`). `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite (all `tests/**/*.rendered.test.ts`), the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" in two or three sentences: settled notices leave when Undo ends, problem notices link to Activity, the swipe cue/commit rule and label threshold (state, not history). Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: finished actions end quietly; swipe cue matches the action\", body with what changed per item and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write rules file and track A checklist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2684,"cache_read_input_tokens":301750,"output_tokens":4328,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":25},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2684,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4328,"cache