{"parentUuid":"44cc8a32-eb6b-4f23-a3a9-ac7ad0bda1bd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch99yAR8diVpTpETUraRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QktaKfjxLSWEL9nMJngv1L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review; cat > $R/p6-reader-contact/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p6 track B: the reader's Done says what it does; Contact gets phone targets\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first. Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p6-reader-contact/`.\n\nBackground (design critique, 2026-11-17): the phone reader's bottom bar has six equal, unlabelled icons (star, clock, tick, up, down, more); the tick means \"Mark done\" or \"Mark not done\" depending on context. The owner chose: keep all six controls and give the done button a visible label. Separately, the Contact page kept desktop density: recent-mail rows are 24px tall, the copy buttons are 24px and invisible until hover (so never visible on touch), and the large name is a hidden \"find mail from sender\" button.\n\nCode map: `src/components/ReaderView.vue` (the `.reader-actions` toolbar teleported into the phone's bottom bar; `data-test=\"reader-archive-toggle\"`, `props.compact`), `src/assets/mobile/shell.css` (`.mobile-reader-actions .reader-actions` and `> .header-glyph`), `src/assets/mobile/reader.css` (accent on the archive toggle), `src/components/ContactPane.vue`, `src/assets/style.css` (`.contact-recent button` 24px, `.contact-copy` size/opacity), `src/assets/mobile/pages.css` (compact pages including Contact).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p6-reader-contact origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Visible label on the reader's done button. When `props.compact` is true, the `reader-archive-toggle` button shows its glyph followed by a visible text label: \"Done\" when the conversation is in the Inbox, \"Not done\" when it is not (the action is Mark not done). Keep the existing visually hidden full name and title for assistive tech (the accessible name must stay \"Mark done (E)\" / \"Mark not done\" or an equivalent full phrase; do not let the short visible word replace it: use `aria-label` with the full phrase if needed). Regular layout: no visible label, unchanged. Unit test in the ReaderView tests: compact + in inbox → visible text \"Done\" and accessible name contains \"Mark done\"; compact + not in inbox → \"Not done\" and \"Mark not done\"; regular → no visible label element. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <ReaderView tests>`.\n\n- [ ] 3. Lay out the bar with the labelled button. In `shell.css`/`reader.css` (compact only): the labelled done button is an inline-flex pill: 24px glyph, 6px gap, label `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, weight 600, `padding-inline: 12px`, min-height 48px, the existing accent colour. The other buttons stay 48×48px with 24px glyphs. Distribute the controls with `justify-content: space-between` (or the existing rule) so nothing overflows. Rendered assertions in the reader rendered test at 412×915 and 360×800: all toolbar buttons are inside the bar and the viewport, none overlap each other, the done button is at least 48px high and its label is fully visible (no ellipsis, `scrollWidth <= clientWidth`), every other button is at least 48×48. Re-run `reader.png` and `reader-undo-toast.png` into this track's directory. Check: the rendered file passes.\n\n- [ ] 4. Contact rows and copy buttons. In compact mode (`pages.css`, under the Contact page selectors already used there): `.contact-recent button` gets `min-height: 48px; height: auto; padding-block: 12px; white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; text-align: left` with a 1px `var(--rule)` separator between rows; `.contact-copy` is 48×48px, `opacity: 1`, always visible, glyph 20–24px, `color: var(--text-secondary)`. The name line and the mailbox line keep the copy button at their end without overlapping text (the text takes `flex: 1; min-width: 0` and wraps). Rendered assertions at 412×915 and 360×800 on the Contact page: each recent button ≥ 48px high; each copy button 48×48 and computed opacity 1; no horizontal overflow; copy buttons do not overlap the name/address text boxes. Check: the rendered file covering Contact passes.\n\n- [ ] 5. Make \"find mail from sender\" visible. In compact mode the name stays a heading-like line but is no longer the only way to search: add a visible text button \"Find mail from sender\" (48px high, left-aligned at the page inset, `var(--focus-accent)` text, weight 600) below the identity lines and above \"Recent cached mail\", emitting the same `searchSender` event with the mailbox. In compact mode the name itself becomes plain text (not a button) so there is one obvious control; in the regular layout the name button stays exactly as today. Unit tests in the ContactPane tests: compact → the new button exists and emits `searchSender` with the mailbox, the name is not a button; regular → unchanged. Re-run `contact.png` into this track's directory. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <ContactPane tests> tests/layout` and the Contact rendered test pass.\n\n- [ ] 6. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` into your branch if it moved (`git fetch origin && git merge origin/mobile/integration`). `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" in two sentences (the labelled done button; Contact rows, copy buttons and the find-mail control), state not history. Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: labelled Done in the reader; phone-sized Contact\", body with what changed per item and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\ncat > $R/p6-selection/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p6 track C: selection can be found and says its scope\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first. Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p6-selection/`.\n\nBackground (design critique, 2026-11-17): on the phone the only way into selection is a 500ms long-press on a row (the row checkboxes are `display: none` until selection mode, so screen-reader users have no per-row route in); \"Select all (18)\" hides that it means the 18 *loaded* rows; the \"Mark 1 done\" button is 40px high while its neighbours are 48px.\n\nCode map: `src/components/SelectionBar.vue` (compact template), `src/assets/mobile/list.css` (`.selection-bar`, `.selection-row-primary`, `.row-select`, around line 248 and 405), `src/components/InboxList.vue` (row checkbox `.row-select`, row tap/long-press handling), `src/composables/useLongPressSelection.ts`, `src/App.vue` (`selectedCount`, `<SelectionBar v-if=…>`, `inboxSplitsShown`), `src/components/mobile/MobileTopBar.vue`, `src/components/HeaderGlyph.vue`, the mailbox selection API (find `selectAllLoaded`, `toggleSelected` or similar in `src/composables/`).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p6-selection origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Selection mode can exist with nothing selected. Add an explicit compact selection mode flag (e.g. `selectionMode` ref in App or the selection composable): true while any row is selected, and also after the new Select control (item 3) is pressed with nothing selected yet. While it is true in compact mode: row checkboxes are visible, tapping a row toggles its selection instead of opening it (reuse what already happens when `selectedCount > 0`), the split pill is hidden (extend the existing `selectedCount > 0` condition in `inboxSplitsShown`), and the SelectionBar shows. Leaving it: the bar's X, Escape/Android Back (the escape ladder already clears selection; make it also clear the empty mode), changing context, opening the reader, or acting on the selection (after a bulk action the mode ends as today). Regular layout unchanged. App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts`: enter mode with 0 selected → checkboxes visible, bar visible, split pill hidden, row tap selects not opens; X → mode ends; Android Back (`window.__emailOsAndroidBack()` as in `tests/layout/mobile-android-back.test.ts`) → mode ends and returns true. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 3. A visible Select control. In compact mode, when the context is a list that supports selection (inbox, saved split, done, starred, search results; not reader, drafts, reminders or pushed pages) and no selection mode is active, the top bar shows a 48×48 round button (same style as the compose button, placed immediately left of it) with a new `select` glyph in `HeaderGlyph.vue` (a 24px rounded square with a tick, 2px stroke, `currentColor`, matching the other glyphs' style), `aria-label=\"Select conversations\"`, `data-test=\"mobile-select\"`. Pressing it enters the empty selection mode. While selection mode is active the button is not shown (the bar's X exits). The long-press stays. Unit test for the glyph name; app tests: visible on Inbox, absent on Drafts and in the reader, enters the mode. Rendered assertion at 412×915 and 360×800: the button is 48×48, inside the top bar, does not overlap the title or the compose button. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout` and the rendered top-bar/list file pass.\n\n- [ ] 4. The bar with nothing selected, and its scope words. SelectionBar compact template: when `count` is 0, the primary row shows the X, the text \"Select conversations\" (in place of \"0 selected\"), and no primary action button (do not render a disabled \"Mark 0 done\"); the secondary row shows only the select-all button. When `count` > 0: the count text reads \"{count} of {loadedCount} loaded\" (keep the `data-test=\"selection-count\"` element containing the count, and keep the hidden scope caveat); the select-all button label reads \"Select {loadedCount} loaded\" (accessible name \"Select all {loadedCount} loaded conversations\"); when every loaded row is already selected the button is disabled. Remove the compact-only rule that hides `.selection-loaded-scope` if it now duplicates text, so scope is stated once. Regular layout unchanged. Unit tests in the SelectionBar tests for count 0, count 1 of 18, all selected. Check: `pnpm vitest run <SelectionBar tests> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 5. Targets. In `list.css` (compact): the primary action button (`[data-test=\"selection-archive\"]`, `[data-test=\"selection-unarchive\"]`) has `min-height: 48px` (it is 40px today, around line 405); the secondary buttons stay ≥ 48px; the secondary row may wrap to two lines rather than overflow when the text is long (\"Select 18 loaded\" plus Mark read / Mark unread) — no horizontal overflow at 360px. Rendered assertions in the selection rendered test at 412×915 and 360×800: every button in the bar ≥ 48px high; the bar is inside the viewport; no element of the bar overflows horizontally; the bar's bottom ≤ the nav pill's top. Re-run `selection.png` and `selection-with-notice.png`, and add `selection-empty.png` (mode entered with the Select button, nothing selected) into this track's directory. Check: the rendered file passes and the three screenshots exist.\n\n- [ ] 6. Per-row route for assistive tech. With no selection mode active, the row checkbox is `display: none` in compact mode, so it is unreachable. Keep it visually hidden but reachable instead: in compact mode outside selection mode, style `.row-select` as visually hidden (the standard 1px clip pattern used elsewhere in the repo; find `.visually-hidden`) rather than `display: none`, so a screen reader can find \"Select <subject>\" on each row; checking it enters selection mode with that row selected. Pointer users see no change. Unit/app test: outside selection mode, the row checkbox is in the accessibility tree (not `display: none`) and checking it selects the row and enters the mode. Check: `pnpm vitest run tests/layout <InboxList tests>`.\n\n- [ ] 7. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` into your branch (`git fetch origin && git merge origin/mobile/integration`; another track may have changed `list.css`, `InboxList.vue` and `App.vue`; keep both sides' behaviour and tests). `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" selection paragraph (Select control, empty mode, scope words, 48px targets), state not history. Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: visible Select and loaded-scope wording\", body with what changed per item and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write track B and C checklists"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4335,"cache_read_input_tokens":304434,"output_tokens":4793,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":45},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4793,"cache_read_input_tokens":304434,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":40531,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QktaKfjxLSWEL9nMJngv1L":{"command":"R=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review; cat > $R/p6-reader-contact/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p6 track B: the reader's Done says what it does; Contact gets phone targets\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first. Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p6-reader-contact/`.\n\nBackground (design critique, 2026-11-17): the phone reader's bottom bar has six equal, unlabelled icons (star, clock, tick, up, down, more); the tick means \"Mark done\" or \"Mark not done\" depending on context. The owner chose: keep all six controls and give the done button a visible label. Separately, the Contact page kept desktop density: recent-mail rows are 24px tall, the copy buttons are 24px and invisible until hover (so never visible on touch), and the large name is a hidden \"find mail from sender\" button.\n\nCode map: `src/components/ReaderView.vue` (the `.reader-actions` toolbar teleported into the phone's bottom bar; `data-test=\"reader-archive-toggle\"`, `props.compact`), `src/assets/mobile/shell.css` (`.mobile-reader-actions .reader-actions` and `> .header-glyph`), `src/assets/mobile/reader.css` (accent on the archive toggle), `src/components/ContactPane.vue`, `src/assets/style.css` (`.contact-recent button` 24px, `.contact-copy` size/opacity), `src/assets/mobile/pages.css` (compact pages including Contact).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p6-reader-contact origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Visible label on the reader's done button. When `props.compact` is true, the `reader-archive-toggle` button shows its glyph followed by a visible text label: \"Done\" when the conversation is in the Inbox, \"Not done\" when it is not (the action is Mark not done). Keep the existing visually hidden full name and title for assistive tech (the accessible name must stay \"Mark done (E)\" / \"Mark not done\" or an equivalent full phrase; do not let the short visible word replace it: use `aria-label` with the full phrase if needed). Regular layout: no visible label, unchanged. Unit test in the ReaderView tests: compact + in inbox → visible text \"Done\" and accessible name contains \"Mark done\"; compact + not in inbox → \"Not done\" and \"Mark not done\"; regular → no visible label element. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <ReaderView tests>`.\n\n- [ ] 3. Lay out the bar with the labelled button. In `shell.css`/`reader.css` (compact only): the labelled done button is an inline-flex pill: 24px glyph, 6px gap, label `font-size: var(--mobile-type-meta)`, weight 600, `padding-inline: 12px`, min-height 48px, the existing accent colour. The other buttons stay 48×48px with 24px glyphs. Distribute the controls with `justify-content: space-between` (or the existing rule) so nothing overflows. Rendered assertions in the reader rendered test at 412×915 and 360×800: all toolbar buttons are inside the bar and the viewport, none overlap each other, the done button is at least 48px high and its label is fully visible (no ellipsis, `scrollWidth <= clientWidth`), every other button is at least 48×48. Re-run `reader.png` and `reader-undo-toast.png` into this track's directory. Check: the rendered file passes.\n\n- [ ] 4. Contact rows and copy buttons. In compact mode (`pages.css`, under the Contact page selectors already used there): `.contact-recent button` gets `min-height: 48px; height: auto; padding-block: 12px; white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; text-align: left` with a 1px `var(--rule)` separator between rows; `.contact-copy` is 48×48px, `opacity: 1`, always visible, glyph 20–24px, `color: var(--text-secondary)`. The name line and the mailbox line keep the copy button at their end without overlapping text (the text takes `flex: 1; min-width: 0` and wraps). Rendered assertions at 412×915 and 360×800 on the Contact page: each recent button ≥ 48px high; each copy button 48×48 and computed opacity 1; no horizontal overflow; copy buttons do not overlap the name/address text boxes. Check: the rendered file covering Contact passes.\n\n- [ ] 5. Make \"find mail from sender\" visible. In compact mode the name stays a heading-like line but is no longer the only way to search: add a visible text button \"Find mail from sender\" (48px high, left-aligned at the page inset, `var(--focus-accent)` text, weight 600) below the identity lines and above \"Recent cached mail\", emitting the same `searchSender` event with the mailbox. In compact mode the name itself becomes plain text (not a button) so there is one obvious control; in the regular layout the name button stays exactly as today. Unit tests in the ContactPane tests: compact → the new button exists and emits `searchSender` with the mailbox, the name is not a button; regular → unchanged. Re-run `contact.png` into this track's directory. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <ContactPane tests> tests/layout` and the Contact rendered test pass.\n\n- [ ] 6. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` into your branch if it moved (`git fetch origin && git merge origin/mobile/integration`). `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" in two sentences (the labelled done button; Contact rows, copy buttons and the find-mail control), state not history. Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: labelled Done in the reader; phone-sized Contact\", body with what changed per item and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\ncat > $R/p6-selection/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p6 track C: selection can be found and says its scope\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first. Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p6-selection/`.\n\nBackground (design critique, 2026-11-17): on the phone the only way into selection is a 500ms long-press on a row (the row checkboxes are `display: none` until selection mode, so screen-reader users have no per-row route in); \"Select all (18)\" hides that it means the 18 *loaded* rows; the \"Mark 1 done\" button is 40px high while its neighbours are 48px.\n\nCode map: `src/components/SelectionBar.vue` (compact template), `src/assets/mobile/list.css` (`.selection-bar`, `.selection-row-primary`, `.row-select`, around line 248 and 405), `src/components/InboxList.vue` (row checkbox `.row-select`, row tap/long-press handling), `src/composables/useLongPressSelection.ts`, `src/App.vue` (`selectedCount`, `<SelectionBar v-if=…>`, `inboxSplitsShown`), `src/components/mobile/MobileTopBar.vue`, `src/components/HeaderGlyph.vue`, the mailbox selection API (find `selectAllLoaded`, `toggleSelected` or similar in `src/composables/`).\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p6-selection origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Selection mode can exist with nothing selected. Add an explicit compact selection mode flag (e.g. `selectionMode` ref in App or the selection composable): true while any row is selected, and also after the new Select control (item 3) is pressed with nothing selected yet. While it is true in compact mode: row checkboxes are visible, tapping a row toggles its selection instead of opening it (reuse what already happens when `selectedCount > 0`), the split pill is hidden (extend the existing `selectedCount > 0` condition in `inboxSplitsShown`), and the SelectionBar shows. Leaving it: the bar's X, Escape/Android Back (the escape ladder already clears selection; make it also clear the empty mode), changing context, opening the reader, or acting on the selection (after a bulk action the mode ends as today). Regular layout unchanged. App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts`: enter mode with 0 selected → checkboxes visible, bar visible, split pill hidden, row tap selects not opens; X → mode ends; Android Back (`window.__emailOsAndroidBack()` as in `tests/layout/mobile-android-back.test.ts`) → mode ends and returns true. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 3. A visible Select control. In compact mode, when the context is a list that supports selection (inbox, saved split, done, starred, search results; not reader, drafts, reminders or pushed pages) and no selection mode is active, the top bar shows a 48×48 round button (same style as the compose button, placed immediately left of it) with a new `select` glyph in `HeaderGlyph.vue` (a 24px rounded square with a tick, 2px stroke, `currentColor`, matching the other glyphs' style), `aria-label=\"Select conversations\"`, `data-test=\"mobile-select\"`. Pressing it enters the empty selection mode. While selection mode is active the button is not shown (the bar's X exits). The long-press stays. Unit test for the glyph name; app tests: visible on Inbox, absent on Drafts and in the reader, enters the mode. Rendered assertion at 412×915 and 360×800: the button is 48×48, inside the top bar, does not overlap the title or the compose button. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout` and the rendered top-bar/list file pass.\n\n- [ ] 4. The bar with nothing selected, and its scope words. SelectionBar compact template: when `count` is 0, the primary row shows the X, the text \"Select conversations\" (in place of \"0 selected\"), and no primary action button (do not render a disabled \"Mark 0 done\"); the secondary row shows only the select-all button. When `count` > 0: the count text reads \"{count} of {loadedCount} loaded\" (keep the `data-test=\"selection-count\"` element containing the count, and keep the hidden scope caveat); the select-all button label reads \"Select {loadedCount} loaded\" (accessible name \"Select all {loadedCount} loaded conversations\"); when every loaded row is already selected the button is disabled. Remove the compact-only rule that hides `.selection-loaded-scope` if it now duplicates text, so scope is stated once. Regular layout unchanged. Unit tests in the SelectionBar tests for count 0, count 1 of 18, all selected. Check: `pnpm vitest run <SelectionBar tests> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 5. Targets. In `list.css` (compact): the primary action button (`[data-test=\"selection-archive\"]`, `[data-test=\"selection-unarchive\"]`) has `min-height: 48px` (it is 40px today, around line 405); the secondary buttons stay ≥ 48px; the secondary row may wrap to two lines rather than overflow when the text is long (\"Select 18 loaded\" plus Mark read / Mark unread) — no horizontal overflow at 360px. Rendered assertions in the selection rendered test at 412×915 and 360×800: every button in the bar ≥ 48px high; the bar is inside the viewport; no element of the bar overflows horizontally; the bar's bottom ≤ the nav pill's top. Re-run `selection.png` and `selection-with-notice.png`, and add `selection-empty.png` (mode entered with the Select button, nothing selected) into this track's directory. Check: the rendered file passes and the three screenshots exist.\n\n- [ ] 6. Per-row route for assistive tech. With no selection mode active, the row checkbox is `display: none` in compact mode, so it is unreachable. Keep it visually hidden but reachable instead: in compact mode outside selection mode, style `.row-select` as visually hidden (the standard 1px clip pattern used elsewhere in the repo; find `.visually-hidden`) rather than `display: none`, so a screen reader can find \"Select <subject>\" on each row; checking it enters selection mode with that row selected. Pointer users see no change. Unit/app test: outside selection mode, the row checkbox is in the accessibility tree (not `display: none`) and checking it selects the row and enters the mode. Check: `pnpm vitest run tests/layout <InboxList tests>`.\n\n- [ ] 7. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` into your branch (`git fetch origin && git merge origin/mobile/integration`; another track may have changed `list.css`, `InboxList.vue` and `App.vue`; keep both sides' behaviour and tests). `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" selection paragraph (Select control, empty mode, scope words, 48px targets), state not history. Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: visible Select and loaded-scope wording\", body with what changed per item and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write track B and C checklists"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch99y77BsAm1M3K9GqX2K","requestRef":"579e0825-9910-40a4-b8a5-319806100aae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea02bedb-a018-49d3-a759-b2ad70ee6a46","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:47:24.803Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
