{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"abf392a77d8fb4b5016e8c4e7c545606fef7b8b0c9515f3d5f0f75b4e93cd8ae","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The validate checkout already has the src-tauri/gen generated files in place, though they may be untracked, and git status reports nothing, so that's fine for now. Next I'll launch the reviewers.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Launching the three reviewers: GPT-6.2-SOL and GPT-6.2-Astra in the background, Opus 5.5 in the foreground."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AmNCCzXC1B5V3m2kSod7xm","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"Critique r3 A1 (GPT-6.2-SOL): list surfaces","role":"review","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6.2-sol","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"clientRequestId":"crit-r3-a1","task":"You are a senior product design director doing an independent design review (Assessment A of an \"Impeccable critique\") of a phone UI. Read `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/COMMON.md` first and follow it exactly (read-only repo, where to write, what to ignore). Do not request escalated permissions; run commands directly.\n\nYour screens: the **mail list surfaces**: inbox list and rows (`browser/inbox.png`, `browser/inbox-scrolled-end.png`), the navigation drawer (`drawer.png`), swipe actions (`swipe-done.png`, `swipe-done-armed.png`, `swipe-remind-armed.png`), selection (`selection.png`, `selection-empty.png`, `selection-with-notice.png`), notices (`inbox-undo-toast.png`, `inbox-after-undo-window.png`), the bottom navigation and split pill, the reminder picker sheet (`reminder-picker.png`), the command palette (`palette.png`), drafts (`drafts.png`), plus the Android screenshots `android/inbox.png`, `android/selection-empty.png`, `android/selection-one.png`, `android/inbox-undo-toast.png`, `android/inbox-after-undo-window.png`. Look at every one with your image tool; read the matching CSS (`src/assets/mobile/list.css`, `shell.css`, `notices.css`, `tokens.css`) and components (`InboxList.vue`, `SelectionBar.vue`, `ActionNotice.vue`, `mobile/MobileTopBar.vue`, `mobile/MobileDrawer.vue`, `useSwipeAction.ts`).\n\nEvaluate as a design director: design specificity (authored for this product vs category-interchangeable), hierarchy, IA, composition, typography, colour, states, copy, edge cases, thumb reach and touch targets, motion. Then:\n1. Design-specificity verdict (one paragraph).\n2. Nielsen's 10 heuristics, each scored 0–4 with a one-line key issue (4 = genuinely excellent; most real interfaces total 20–32). Score only for your screens.\n3. Cognitive load: the 8-item checklist (single focus; chunking ≤4 per group; grouping; visual hierarchy; one thing at a time; ≤4 visible options per decision; working memory; progressive disclosure); report failures and decision points with more than 4 visible options.\n4. Emotional journey: peak-end, valleys, reassurance at high-stakes moments (bulk mark done, swipe commit, undo window ending).\n5. 2–3 specific strengths.\n6. 3–5 priority issues, each tagged P0/P1/P2/P3, with What, Why it matters, a concrete Fix (selectors, values, copy), and evidence (screenshot name and/or file:line).\n7. Persona red flags for \"Alex\" (impatient power user), \"Casey\" (one-handed distracted phone user) and \"Sam\" (screen reader / low vision).\n8. Minor observations (bullets) and 2–3 provocative questions.\n\nBe direct and specific. Verify claims against the code before stating them; if something might be harness chrome rather than product, say so instead of counting it.\n\nWrite the full review to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/A1-list.md` and also return it as your final message. Do not delegate, do not edit the repository."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011AQTU4ymvkjeRH3QuyshsA","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"Critique r3 B (GPT-6.2-Astra): detector","role":"review","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6.2-astra","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"clientRequestId":"crit-r3-b","task":"You run Assessment B (deterministic detector + browser evidence) of an \"Impeccable critique\" of a phone UI. Read `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/COMMON.md` first and follow it (read-only repo, where to write). You do not do a subjective design review; you collect and triage detector evidence. Do not request escalated permissions; run commands directly, and keep any temporary files inside `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/`.\n\nTool: the Impeccable launcher at `/home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable`. Run it with cwd `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate`. Rendered scans need `IMPECCABLE_BROWSER=/tmp/chrome-rendered/chrome/linux-156.0.8078.80/chrome-linux64/chrome`. Run `.../impeccable detect --help` first for the exact flags (it supports `--viewport WxH`).\n\nSteps:\n1. Source scan: `impeccable detect --json src/components src/App.vue` (markup only). Exit 0 = clean, 2 = findings. Record counts per rule and file:line.\n2. Rendered scan of the phone layout. `dist/` was built from this commit; if it is missing or older than `src/`, run `pnpm build` (writes only `dist/`, allowed). Start `npx vite preview --port 4873 --strictPort` in the background so it survives your command (for example `nohup … &` inside a shell that then waits on a readiness check), record its PID, and scan `http://localhost:4873/` with `--viewport 412x915`. If the detector can only scan the landing state (the inbox), say so. Stop the preview server before you finish and confirm the port is closed.\n3. Do not attempt a live overlay or human-browser injection; report \"overlay not available: headless environment\".\n4. Triage every finding: true issue, false positive (with reason: off-screen or inert desktop-only markup; harness chrome such as the top account-tab strip and yellow \"Preview\" label; text that sits under the floating bottom bars only at the sampled scroll position), or advisory. Check each against `src/assets/mobile/` and the screenshots in `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/browser/`.\n\nReturn: CLI findings (counts, rule names, file locations), rendered findings (counts, rules, selectors, viewport), the triage table, and skipped/failed steps with the concrete reason and command output. Write it to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/B-detector.md` (raw JSON next to it) and return it as your final message. Do not delegate, do not edit the repository."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
