{"parentUuid":"72ae0982-1747-42e2-924c-e6067419c5a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9DeVPaHwH7c8GUoAF4v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012GG7ddRSjGcZALGGysgYw2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Critique r3 A2 (Opus 5.5)","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"You are a senior product design director doing an independent design review (Assessment A of an \"Impeccable critique\") of a phone UI. Read `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/COMMON.md` first and follow it exactly (read-only repo, where to write, what to ignore). Use the Read tool to view PNG images.\n\nYour screens: the **reader, editors and secondary pages**: reader (`browser/reader.png`, `reader-scrolled-end.png`, `reader-more-sheet.png`, `reader-message-sheet.png`, `reader-undo-toast.png`), new message and reply (`compose.png`, `compose-keyboard.png`, `reply.png`), search (`search.png`, `search-results.png`), reminders (`reminders.png`), settings (`settings.png`, `settings-note-open.png`), activity (`activity.png`), contact (`contact.png`), plus the Android screenshots `android/reader.png`, `android/contact.png`, `android/compose.png`, `android/settings.png`. Look at every one; read the matching CSS (`src/assets/mobile/reader.css`, `pages.css`, `shell.css`, `tokens.css`, compose CSS) and components (`ReaderView.vue`, `ContactPane.vue`, compose/reply components, `ReminderSettings.vue`, `ActionNotice.vue`).\n\nEvaluate as a design director: design specificity (authored for this product vs category-interchangeable), hierarchy, IA, composition, typography, colour, states, copy (the product voice is terse and factual and must never overstate what happened; drafts are local and never sent), edge cases, thumb reach and touch targets, keyboard-up behaviour. Note: the product owner deliberately decided that on the phone the editors close only through the X (no \"Save and close\" text button), with the fixed status phrase \"never sent\"; do not recommend reversing that decision, though you may comment on how well the X communicates.\n\nThen produce:\n1. Design-specificity verdict (one paragraph).\n2. Nielsen's 10 heuristics, each scored 0–4 with a one-line key issue (4 = genuinely excellent; most real interfaces total 20–32). Score only for your screens.\n3. Cognitive load: the 8-item checklist (single focus; chunking ≤4 per group; grouping; visual hierarchy; one thing at a time; ≤4 visible options per decision; working memory; progressive disclosure); report failures and decision points with more than 4 visible options.\n4. Emotional journey: peak-end, valleys, reassurance at high-stakes moments (leaving a draft, a failed save, mark done from the reader, changing a setting).\n5. 2–3 specific strengths.\n6. 3–5 priority issues, each tagged P0/P1/P2/P3, with What, Why it matters, a concrete Fix (selectors, values, copy), and evidence (screenshot name and/or file:line).\n7. Persona red flags for \"Jordan\" (first-timer), \"Casey\" (one-handed distracted phone user) and \"Riley\" (stress tester: long subjects, failures, interruptions).\n8. Minor observations (bullets) and 2–3 provocative questions.\n\nBe direct and specific. Verify claims against the code before stating them; if something might be harness chrome rather than product, say so instead of counting it.\n\nWrite the full review to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/critique-r3/A2-reader-pages.md` and return it in full as your final message. Do not edit the repository; do not spawn sub-agents."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4010,"cache_read_input_tokens":423787,"output_tokens":1344,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creat