{"parentUuid":"b3062ddc-42a7-4544-9aca-5167e3ecb9d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EGLDvYQ1rH9LYhnqrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Swipes are confirmed working in selection mode. Next I'm putting the report together, and I need to flag the tension between the owner's call that finished actions should end quietly and A1's request for a handoff. I'll also raise A2's idea of swapping the X for a down-chevron as a question, since it only partly respects the owner's decision. The first merged priority issue is that disabled reader controls look live, which A2 verified and which traces back to our round-2 styling.\n\nI'm drafting the report now: the priority list, the tension between the owner's \"end quietly\" choice and A1's handoff request, and a few items still left to sort out.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"output_tokens":3887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3887,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7184,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch9EGEe4Wajd7h6WDkJNA","requestRef":"95615a0b-f46e-4d4a-85ba-abc0f782ff44","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b99617cb-f677-4f8e-b127-521bbddb2fdb","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:10.113Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"b99617cb-f677-4f8e-b127-521bbddb2fdb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EGLDvYQ1rH9LYhnqrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that the disabled and enabled reader buttons share the muted icon color, that swipes still work in selection mode, and that a failed swipe-setting save leaves the tapped radio checked. I'm sending the combined report now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"output_tokens":3887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3887,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch9EGEe4Wajd7h6WDkJNA","requestRef":"95615a0b-f46e-4d4a-85ba-abc0f782ff44","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"45d6878d-5dab-4bfe-bab7-3e05670cc0fe","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:10.126Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"45d6878d-5dab-4bfe-bab7-3e05670cc0fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EGLDvYQ1rH9LYhnqrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NX7vtpizNYyKR2PPCxur3A","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"Method: three isolated sub-agents (A1: GPT-6.2-SOL, list surfaces · A2: Opus 5.5, reader, editors, pages · B: GPT-6.2-Astra, detector). A1 and A2 never saw B or each other. Commit ac939a3.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Receipts are exact; Undo shows no deadline; closing an editor with X confirms nothing |\n| 2 | Match with real world | 2 | \"Done\" reads like a status badge; ^/v read as scroll; \"loaded\", \"cached\" are product words |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back, Undo, Keep draft solid everywhere |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px vs 48px elsewhere; swipe settings and reminder settings handle failure differently |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes still act during selection mode; a fast fling commits before its label shows |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader buttons look live; disabled reasons only in hidden titles |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, Select, long-press, commands; Mark read is two taps deep in the reader |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; the search form sits over an unrelated Inbox list |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Failure copy and the Activity link are good; one settings failure leaves a wrong value showing |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; nothing teaches the gestures or \"loaded\" scope |\n\nEach half scored 25. **None of last round's priority issues came back:**\n- the lingering notice\n- the unlabelled Done\n- the hidden selection entry and its scope\n- Contact's targets\n- the swipe icon\n\nThe score stayed flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\n\n## Design specificity\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\"Local draft · never sent\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cached content only — incomplete…\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\"\n\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\n\n## Overall impression\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"output_tokens":3887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3887,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9391,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NX7vtpizNYyKR2PPCxur3A":{"message":"Method: three isolated sub-agents (A1: GPT-6.2-SOL, list surfaces · A2: Opus 5.5, reader, editors, pages · B: GPT-6.2-Astra, detector). A1 and A2 never saw B or each other. Commit ac939a3.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Receipts are exact; Undo shows no deadline; closing an editor with X confirms nothing |\n| 2 | Match with real world | 2 | \"Done\" reads like a status badge; ^/v read as scroll; \"loaded\", \"cached\" are product words |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back, Undo, Keep draft solid everywhere |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px vs 48px elsewhere; swipe settings and reminder settings handle failure differently |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes still act during selection mode; a fast fling commits before its label shows |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader buttons look live; disabled reasons only in hidden titles |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, Select, long-press, commands; Mark read is two taps deep in the reader |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; the search form sits over an unrelated Inbox list |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Failure copy and the Activity link are good; one settings failure leaves a wrong value showing |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; nothing teaches the gestures or \"loaded\" scope |\n\nEach half scored 25. **None of last round's priority issues came back:**\n- the lingering notice\n- the unlabelled Done\n- the hidden selection entry and its scope\n- Contact's targets\n- the swipe icon\n\nThe score stayed flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\n\n## Design specificity\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\"Local draft · never sent\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cached content only — incomplete…\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\"\n\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\n\n## Overall impression\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch9EGEe4Wajd7h6WDkJNA","requestRef":"95615a0b-f46e-4d4a-85ba-abc0f782ff44","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"82fb1085-4230-4e27-8f0e-e28e83034dad","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:19.518Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
