 flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\\n\\n## Design specificity\\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\\\"Local draft · never sent\\\", \\\"Confirmed\\\", \\\"Cached content only — incomplete…\\\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \\\"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\\\"\\n\\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\\n\\n## Overall impression\\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went.\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]},"uuid":"e00b6c67-6225-47e9-8ae6-e2f8565cd6b2","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:19.558Z","toolUseResult":"{\"sentMessage\":\"Method: three isolated sub-agents (A1: GPT-6.2-SOL, list surfaces · A2: Opus 5.5, reader, editors, pages · B: GPT-6.2-Astra, detector). A1 and A2 never saw B or each other. Commit ac939a3.\\n\\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\\n\\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Receipts are exact; Undo shows no deadline; closing an editor with X confirms nothing |\\n| 2 | Match with real world | 2 | \\\"Done\\\" reads like a status badge; ^/v read as scroll; \\\"loaded\\\", \\\"cached\\\" are product words |\\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back, Undo, Keep draft solid everywhere |\\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px vs 48px elsewhere; swipe settings and reminder settings handle failure differently |\\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes still act during selection mode; a fast fling commits before its label shows |\\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader buttons look live; disabled reasons only in hidden titles |\\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, Select, long-press, commands; Mark read is two taps deep in the reader |\\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; the search form sits over an unrelated Inbox list |\\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Failure copy and the Activity link are good; one settings failure leaves a wrong value showing |\\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; nothing teaches the gestures or \\\"loaded\\\" scope |\\n\\nEach half scored 25. **None of last round's priority issues came back:**\\n- the lingering notice\\n- the unlabelled Done\\n- the hidden selection entry and its scope\\n- Contact's targets\\n- the swipe icon\\n\\nThe score stayed flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\\n\\n## Design specificity\\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\\\"Local draft · never sent\\\", \\\"Confirmed\\\", \\\"Cached content only — incomplete…\\\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \\\"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\\\"\\n\\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\\n\\n## Overall impression\\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went.\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"T3 Code","version":"0.1.10"}},"structuredContent":{"sentMessage":"Method: three isolated sub-agents (A1: GPT-6.2-SOL, list surfaces · A2: Opus 5.5, reader, editors, pages · B: GPT-6.2-Astra, detector). A1 and A2 never saw B or each other. Commit ac939a3.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Receipts are exact; Undo shows no deadline; closing an editor with X confirms nothing |\n| 2 | Match with real world | 2 | \"Done\" reads like a status badge; ^/v read as scroll; \"loaded\", \"cached\" are product words |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back, Undo, Keep draft solid everywhere |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px vs 48px elsewhere; swipe settings and reminder settings handle failure differently |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes still act during selection mode; a fast fling commits before its label shows |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader buttons look live; disabled reasons only in hidden titles |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, Select, long-press, commands; Mark read is two taps deep in the reader |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; the search form sits over an unrelated Inbox list |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Failure copy and the Activity link are good; one settings failure leaves a wrong value showing |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; nothing teaches the gestures or \"loaded\" scope |\n\nEach half scored 25. **None of last round's priority issues came back:**\n- the lingering notice\n- the unlabelled Done\n- the hidden selection entry and its scope\n- Contact's targets\n- the swipe icon\n\nThe score stayed flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\n\n## Design specificity\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\"Local draft · never sent\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cached content only — incomplete…\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\"\n\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\n\n## Overall impression\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went.","message":"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"82fb1085-4230-4e27-8f0e-e28e83034dad","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"e00b6c67-6225-47e9-8ae6-e2f8565cd6b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EGLDvYQ1rH9LYhnqrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ByZa8HVzNuh8aW9tYsu9Fq","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"## What's working\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \"1 of 14 selected\" and \"Mark 1 done\" make the scope concrete (A1).\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \"Saved locally · never sent\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \"Keep draft\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\n\n## Priority issues\n\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\n- This is the \"dead controls that look actionable\" anti-reference.\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\n\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \"Could not save\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\"), next to that group.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\n  - A1 asks for \"Undo for Ns\" while it lasts.\n  - Then a few seconds of \"Moved to Done · Open Done\".\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\n  - A2 asks for a \"Draft kept · Open\" notice.\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\n- This pulls against your \"end quietly\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\n\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \"Search mail\" and move the example into Search syntax.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"output_tokens":3887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3887,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10674,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ByZa8HVzNuh8aW9tYsu9Fq":{"message":"## What's working\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \"1 of 14 selected\" and \"Mark 1 done\" make the scope concrete (A1).\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \"Saved locally · never sent\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \"Keep draft\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\n\n## Priority issues\n\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\n- This is the \"dead controls that look actionable\" anti-reference.\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\n\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \"Could not save\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\"), next to that group.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\n  - A1 asks for \"Undo for Ns\" while it lasts.\n  - Then a few seconds of \"Moved to Done · Open Done\".\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\n  - A2 asks for a \"Draft kept · Open\" notice.\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\n- This pulls against your \"end quietly\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\n\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \"Search mail\" and move the example into Search syntax.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`"}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Ch9EGEe4Wajd7h6WDkJNA","requestRef":"95615a0b-f46e-4d4a-85ba-abc0f782ff44","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fcea936-e5b1-41c2-8317-afe4bfe99a69","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:30.203Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"6fcea936-e5b1-41c2-8317-afe4bfe99a69","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"78913aa5-1136-493b-a758-3f044dcad330","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ByZa8HVzNuh8aW9tYsu9Fq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## What's working\\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \\\"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\\\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \\\"1 of 14 selected\\\" and \\\"Mark 1 done\\\" make the scope concrete (A1).\\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \\\"Saved locally · never sent\\\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \\\"Keep draft\\\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\\n\\n## Priority issues\\n\\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\\n- This is the \\\"dead controls that look actionable\\\" anti-reference.\\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\\n\\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \\\"Could not save\\\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\\\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\\\"), next to that group.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\\n  - A1 asks for \\\"Undo for Ns\\\" while it lasts.\\n  - Then a few seconds of \\\"Moved to Done · Open Done\\\".\\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\\n  - A2 asks for a \\\"Draft kept · Open\\\" notice.\\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\\n- This pulls against your \\\"end quietly\\\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\\n\\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \\\"weekly status\\\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \\\"Search mail\\\" and move the example into Search syntax.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]},"uuid":"3ce64b56-7eb1-4844-9c5d-04cb80c7359a","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:30.235Z","toolUseResult":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## What's working\\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \\\"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\\\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \\\"1 of 14 selected\\\" and \\\"Mark 1 done\\\" make the scope concrete (A1).\\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \\\"Saved locally · never sent\\\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \\\"Keep draft\\\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\\n\\n## Priority issues\\n\\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\\n- This is the \\\"dead controls that look actionable\\\" anti-reference.\\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\\n\\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \\\"Could not save\\\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\\\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\\\"), next to that group.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\\n  - A1 asks for \\\"Undo for Ns\\\" while it lasts.\\n  - Then a few seconds of \\\"Moved to Done · Open Done\\\".\\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\\n  - A2 asks for a \\\"Draft kept · Open\\\" notice.\\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\\n- This pulls against your \\\"end quietly\\\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\\n\\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \\\"weekly status\\\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \\\"Search mail\\\" and move the example into Search syntax.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"T3 Code","version":"0.1.10"}},"structuredContent":{"sentMessage":"## What's working\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \"1 of 14 selected\" and \"Mark 1 done\" make the scope concrete (A1).\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \"Saved locally · never sent\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \"Keep draft\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\n\n## Priority issues\n\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\n- This is the \"dead controls that look actionable\" anti-reference.\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\n\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \"Could not save\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\"), next to that group.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\n  - A1 asks for \"Undo for Ns\" while it lasts.\n  - Then a few seconds of \"Moved to Done · Open Done\".\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\n  - A2 asks for a \"Draft kept · Open\" notice.\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\n- This pulls against your \"end quietly\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\n\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \"Search mail\" and move the example into Search syntax.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`","message":"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6fcea936-e5b1-41c2-8317-afe4bfe99a69","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"3ce64b56-7eb1-4844-9c5d-04cb80c7359a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EGLDvYQ1rH9LYhnqrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K1tuzFPT7ELweFsRZQEE8z","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"## Persona red flags\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \"Mark done\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\n  - \"Copy text\" gives no visible confirmation.\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\n  - Reads the lavender \"Done\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\n  - Opened mail still says \"Unread\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \"Copy text\" only greys the row.\n\n## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \"one violet thing\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\n- The minute select has 60 options.\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\n- Reply quote shows \"Plain text only.…\".\n- \"Refresh reminders\" reads as body text, not a button.\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \"Schedule\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \"Unread\" word *be* the Mark read control?\n- Would a down-chevron say \"kept\" where X says \"gone\", without adding a word or a button?\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"output_tokens":3887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3887,"cache_read_input_tokens":453122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7942,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01K1tuzFPT7ELweFsRZQEE8z":{"message":"## Persona red flags\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \"Mark done\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\n  - \"Copy text\" gives no visible confirmation.\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\n  - Reads the lavender \"Done\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\n  - Opened mail still says \"Unread\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \"Copy text\" only greys the row.\n\n## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \"one violet thing\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\n- The minute select has 60 options.\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\n- Reply quote shows \"Plain text only.…\".\n- \"Refresh reminders\" reads as body text, not a button.\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \"Schedule\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \"Unread\" word *be* the Mark read control?\n- Would a down-chevron say \"kept\" where X says \"gone\", without adding a word or a button?\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?"}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Ch9EGEe4Wajd7h6WDkJNA","requestRef":"95615a0b-f46e-4d4a-85ba-abc0f782ff44","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e6ac36a0-5eec-4abf-81e5-16b9471d527c","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:38.152Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"parentUuid":"e6ac36a0-5eec-4abf-81e5-16b9471d527c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"78913aa5-1136-493b-a758-3f044dcad330","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1tuzFPT7ELweFsRZQEE8z","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## Persona red flags\\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \\\"Mark done\\\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\\n  - \\\"Copy text\\\" gives no visible confirmation.\\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\\n  - Reads the lavender \\\"Done\\\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\\n  - Opened mail still says \\\"Unread\\\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \\\"Copy text\\\" only greys the row.\\n\\n## Minor observations\\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \\\"one violet thing\\\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\\n- The minute select has 60 options.\\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\\n- Reply quote shows \\\"Plain text only.…\\\".\\n- \\\"Refresh reminders\\\" reads as body text, not a button.\\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \\\"Schedule\\\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\\n\\n## Questions to consider\\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \\\"Unread\\\" word *be* the Mark read control?\\n- Would a down-chevron say \\\"kept\\\" where X says \\\"gone\\\", without adding a word or a button?\\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]},"uuid":"65b73307-8142-49ff-bb04-e447725430ec","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:38.180Z","toolUseResult":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## Persona red flags\\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \\\"Mark done\\\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\\n  - \\\"Copy text\\\" gives no visible confirmation.\\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\\n  - Reads the lavender \\\"Done\\\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\\n  - Opened mail still says \\\"Unread\\\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \\\"Copy text\\\" only greys the row.\\n\\n## Minor observations\\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \\\"one violet thing\\\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\\n- The minute select has 60 options.\\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\\n- Reply quote shows \\\"Plain text only.…\\\".\\n- \\\"Refresh reminders\\\" reads as body text, not a button.\\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \\\"Schedule\\\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\\n\\n## Questions to consider\\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \\\"Unread\\\" word *be* the Mark read control?\\n- Would a down-chevron say \\\"kept\\\" where X says \\\"gone\\\", without adding a word or a button?\\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"T3 Code","version":"0.1.10"}},"structuredContent":{"sentMessage":"## Persona red flags\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \"Mark done\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\n  - \"Copy text\" gives no visible confirmation.\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\n  - Reads the lavender \"Done\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\n  - Opened mail still says \"Unread\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \"Copy text\" only greys the row.\n\n## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \"one violet thing\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\n- The minute select has 60 options.\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\n- Reply quote shows \"Plain text only.…\".\n- \"Refresh reminders\" reads as body text, not a button.\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \"Schedule\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \"Unread\" word *be* the Mark read control?\n- Would a down-chevron say \"kept\" where X says \"gone\", without adding a word or a button?\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?","message":"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e6ac36a0-5eec-4abf-81e5-16b9471d527c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"t3-code","cwd":"/home/exedev/email-os","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","version":"2.1.326","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cached-bubbling-meadow"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"744885abbe5e6d565cd5d877aa2bc4a6f2cd69b7601c51832619f5de69dd212f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Swipes are confirmed working in selection mode. Next I'm putting the report together, and I need to flag the tension between the owner's call that finished actions should end quietly and A1's request for a handoff. I'll also raise A2's idea of swapping the X for a down-chevron as a question, since it only partly respects the owner's decision. The first merged priority issue is that disabled reader controls look live, which A2 verified and which traces back to our round-2 styling.\n\nI'm drafting the report now: the priority list, the tension between the owner's \"end quietly\" choice and A1's handoff request, and a few items still left to sort out.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that the disabled and enabled reader buttons share the muted icon color, that swipes still work in selection mode, and that a failed swipe-setting save leaves the tapped radio checked. I'm sending the combined report now.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NX7vtpizNYyKR2PPCxur3A","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"Method: three isolated sub-agents (A1: GPT-6.2-SOL, list surfaces · A2: Opus 5.5, reader, editors, pages · B: GPT-6.2-Astra, detector). A1 and A2 never saw B or each other. Commit ac939a3.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Receipts are exact; Undo shows no deadline; closing an editor with X confirms nothing |\n| 2 | Match with real world | 2 | \"Done\" reads like a status badge; ^/v read as scroll; \"loaded\", \"cached\" are product words |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back, Undo, Keep draft solid everywhere |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px vs 48px elsewhere; swipe settings and reminder settings handle failure differently |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes still act during selection mode; a fast fling commits before its label shows |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader buttons look live; disabled reasons only in hidden titles |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, Select, long-press, commands; Mark read is two taps deep in the reader |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; the search form sits over an unrelated Inbox list |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Failure copy and the Activity link are good; one settings failure leaves a wrong value showing |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; nothing teaches the gestures or \"loaded\" scope |\n\nEach half scored 25. **None of last round's priority issues came back:**\n- the lingering notice\n- the unlabelled Done\n- the hidden selection entry and its scope\n- Contact's targets\n- the swipe icon\n\nThe score stayed flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\n\n## Design specificity\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\"Local draft · never sent\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cached content only — incomplete…\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\"\n\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\n\n## Overall impression\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ByZa8HVzNuh8aW9tYsu9Fq","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"## What's working\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \"1 of 14 selected\" and \"Mark 1 done\" make the scope concrete (A1).\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \"Saved locally · never sent\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \"Keep draft\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\n\n## Priority issues\n\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\n- This is the \"dead controls that look actionable\" anti-reference.\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\n\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \"Could not save\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\"), next to that group.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\n\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\n  - A1 asks for \"Undo for Ns\" while it lasts.\n  - Then a few seconds of \"Moved to Done · Open Done\".\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\n  - A2 asks for a \"Draft kept · Open\" notice.\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\n- This pulls against your \"end quietly\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\n\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \"Search mail\" and move the example into Search syntax.\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K1tuzFPT7ELweFsRZQEE8z","name":"mcp__t3-code__send_to_user","input":{"message":"## Persona red flags\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \"Mark done\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\n  - \"Copy text\" gives no visible confirmation.\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\n  - Reads the lavender \"Done\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\n  - Opened mail still says \"Unread\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \"Copy text\" only greys the row.\n\n## Minor observations\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \"one violet thing\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\n- The minute select has 60 options.\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\n- Reply quote shows \"Plain text only.…\".\n- \"Refresh reminders\" reads as body text, not a button.\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \"Schedule\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\n\n## Questions to consider\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \"Unread\" word *be* the Mark read control?\n- Would a down-chevron say \"kept\" where X says \"gone\", without adding a word or a button?\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","hash":"c8e902f3707953e01ce75427043f567d8298a6e48d5188aac5fe45d263775ee9","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NX7vtpizNYyKR2PPCxur3A","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"Method: three isolated sub-agents (A1: GPT-6.2-SOL, list surfaces · A2: Opus 5.5, reader, editors, pages · B: GPT-6.2-Astra, detector). A1 and A2 never saw B or each other. Commit ac939a3.\\n\\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\\n\\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Receipts are exact; Undo shows no deadline; closing an editor with X confirms nothing |\\n| 2 | Match with real world | 2 | \\\"Done\\\" reads like a status badge; ^/v read as scroll; \\\"loaded\\\", \\\"cached\\\" are product words |\\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back, Undo, Keep draft solid everywhere |\\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px vs 48px elsewhere; swipe settings and reminder settings handle failure differently |\\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes still act during selection mode; a fast fling commits before its label shows |\\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader buttons look live; disabled reasons only in hidden titles |\\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe, Select, long-press, commands; Mark read is two taps deep in the reader |\\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; the search form sits over an unrelated Inbox list |\\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Failure copy and the Activity link are good; one settings failure leaves a wrong value showing |\\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Good disclosures; nothing teaches the gestures or \\\"loaded\\\" scope |\\n\\nEach half scored 25. **None of last round's priority issues came back:**\\n- the lingering notice\\n- the unlabelled Done\\n- the hidden selection entry and its scope\\n- Contact's targets\\n- the swipe icon\\n\\nThe score stayed flat because the reviewers went deeper, and some of last round's own fixes created new findings.\\n\\n## Design specificity\\nBoth reviewers say the same thing: **authored voice, borrowed form.** The copy could only belong to this product (\\\"Local draft · never sent\\\", \\\"Confirmed\\\", \\\"Cached content only — incomplete…\\\"). The shapes are a generic dark mail app: round corner buttons, stacked bottom pills, Material-style sheets. Opus 5.5: the desktop's precision \\\"has not been translated into a phone idiom of equal precision; it has been replaced by a safe, generic one.\\\"\\n\\n**Detector (Astra):** same result as last run.\\n- Code scan: clean apart from one advisory (the 8px startup-card radius).\\n- Inbox at 412×915: 18 hits are one real issue, row previews at 1.25 line spacing below the 1.3 minimum. Neither design reviewer caught it.\\n- 4 false positives: text under the floating bars at that scroll position.\\n- No overlay (headless). Only the inbox could be scanned.\\n\\n## Overall impression\\nThe triage loop is trustworthy and the targets of last round's issues are fixed. What's left is precision at the edges: controls that look live but aren't, gestures that act when they shouldn't, and actions that end without saying where things went.\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ByZa8HVzNuh8aW9tYsu9Fq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## What's working\\n- **The outcome receipt is the product's thesis.** \\\"Mark done · ‹subject› / Confirmed / Undo\\\" names the conversation you already left, with a 48px Undo. Both reviewers called it the peak moment.\\n- **Selection now separates the set from focus.** The empty mode explains itself. \\\"1 of 14 selected\\\" and \\\"Mark 1 done\\\" make the scope concrete (A1).\\n- **Draft safety is complete.** \\\"Saved locally · never sent\\\", protected close, Retry before the fields, Discard → \\\"Keep draft\\\". The keyboard-up layout keeps everything reachable (A2).\\n\\n## Priority issues\\n\\n**[P1] Disabled reader buttons look exactly like live ones** (A2; confirmed).\\n- On the first conversation, the dead Previous chevron is identical to the live one.\\n- Cause: my round-2 rule `button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }`, and resting glyphs use the same `--icon-muted`. Reader Back is also 40px.\\n- This is the \\\"dead controls that look actionable\\\" anti-reference.\\n- *Fix:* live glyphs `--text-secondary`, disabled `--icon-muted` at 0.4 opacity; reader Back 48px.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable polish`\\n\\n**[P1] Swipes still act in selection mode, and a fling can beat its label** (A1; first part confirmed). `onRowPointerDown` starts a swipe even while selecting, so you can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected. A 64px fling commits; the label only appears at 128px.\\n- *Fix:* no swipes while selecting.\\n- *Fix:* one distance rule for arming and commit, at the larger of 128px or 35% of the row.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n**[P1] A failed swipe-setting save leaves the wrong option checked** (A2; confirmed). `SwipeActionSettings.vue` says \\\"Could not save\\\" but leaves the tapped radio checked while the old preference stays in effect. The reminder time on the same page restores correctly.\\n- *Fix:* restore the checked radio. Say which side failed (\\\"Could not save swipe right. Still: Remind me\\\"), next to that group.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable harden`\\n\\n**[P1] Endings are silent: the reviewers want a short receipt, which goes against your last choice.**\\n- *Mail actions (A1):* when Undo ends, the notice now vanishes and the thread is simply gone.\\n  - A1 asks for \\\"Undo for Ns\\\" while it lasts.\\n  - Then a few seconds of \\\"Moved to Done · Open Done\\\".\\n- *Editors (A2):* the X closes the editor with no sign the draft was kept.\\n  - A2 asks for a \\\"Draft kept · Open\\\" notice.\\n  - A2 also suggests silently dropping an untouched empty draft.\\n- This pulls against your \\\"end quietly\\\" choice; a short-lived, neutral receipt is the middle ground.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable clarify`\\n\\n**[P2] The search form sits on top of the Inbox list, which looks like results** (A2). The placeholder `from:ada \\\"weekly status\\\" -invoice` sits over Ada's weekly-status rows.\\n- *Fix:* hide the list until a search runs.\\n- *Fix:* use the placeholder \\\"Search mail\\\" and move the example into Search syntax.\\n- *Command:* `/impeccable distill`\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1tuzFPT7ELweFsRZQEE8z","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"sentMessage\":\"## Persona red flags\\n- **Alex (power user):** a fling commits before its verb shows. The palette's \\\"Mark done\\\" doesn't name the conversation it will act on.\\n- **Casey (one-handed):**\\n  - Menu, Select and the editor X all sit at the top.\\n  - In the reader, the Reply pill is 12px above Star and Remind.\\n  - \\\"Copy text\\\" gives no visible confirmation.\\n  - Coming back after 10 seconds, the thread is gone with no trace.\\n- **Sam (screen reader):**\\n  - Selection mode hides the read-state cue and its accessible label.\\n  - The paperclip on a selected row is about 2.75:1 contrast.\\n  - The checkbox outside selection mode is clipped but still focusable; needs a TalkBack pass.\\n- **Jordan (first-timer):**\\n  - Reads the lavender \\\"Done\\\" as a status and ^/v as scrolling.\\n  - Opened mail still says \\\"Unread\\\", and Mark read is hidden in More.\\n  - Takes the search placeholder for an applied query.\\n- **Riley (stress tester):** reader subjects are still cut at three lines with no ellipsis (raised last round too, not fixed). Toasts have no line limit. A failed \\\"Copy text\\\" only greys the row.\\n\\n## Minor observations\\n- Row previews use 1.25 line spacing (detector).\\n- Lavender appears 3–4 times on a reader screen; DESIGN.md's \\\"one violet thing\\\" rule needs either an exception or fewer uses.\\n- Settings radios are browser blue.\\n- The opened settings note is louder than its parent text.\\n- The minute select has 60 options.\\n- The browser More sheet puts a divider between every row (`Files and links` has no group).\\n- Reply quote shows \\\"Plain text only.…\\\".\\n- \\\"Refresh reminders\\\" reads as body text, not a button.\\n- Contact's recent rows have no dates.\\n- The drawer is still grouped by position (`index === 8`) and has no close button.\\n- The palette shows 9 commands at once.\\n- The reminder picker repeats the year, zone and offset on each date and lists dates out of order. \\\"Schedule\\\" stays disabled after typing a time until Enter is pressed (A1).\\n- The bottom of the list may still sit under a tall selection-plus-notice stack (A1, from the CSS).\\n\\n## Questions to consider\\n- If reading never marks read, should the reader's \\\"Unread\\\" word *be* the Mark read control?\\n- Would a down-chevron say \\\"kept\\\" where X says \\\"gone\\\", without adding a word or a button?\\n- Done already moves to the next conversation. Do Previous and Next earn two of the six slots in the phone's most valuable strip?\",\"message\":\"Shown to the user. Don't repeat it.\"}"}]}}
