{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","prNumber":84,"prUrl":"https://github.com/BbrSofiane/email-os/pull/84","prRepository":"BbrSofiane/email-os","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:43:38.275Z"}
{"parentUuid":"65b73307-8142-49ff-bb04-e447725430ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EK5i8LzsCxT9ZQfAmH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SufHknDCiq4rHLyiPxG11z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate && S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad; cat > $S/crit3-body.md <<'EOF'\nMethod: three isolated sub-agents (A1 GPT-6.2-SOL list · A2 Opus 5.5 reader/editors/pages · B GPT-6.2-Astra detector). Commit ac939a3.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Exact receipts; no Undo deadline; editor X confirms nothing |\n| 2 | Match system / real world | 2 | \"Done\" reads as status; ^/v read as scroll; loaded/cached vocabulary |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 3 | Back/Undo/Keep draft solid |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 2 | Reader Back 40px; swipe vs reminder settings failure handling differ |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 2 | Swipes act during selection mode; fling commits before label |\n| 6 | Recognition rather than recall | 2 | Disabled reader controls look live; reasons only in titles |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency | 3 | Swipe/Select/long-press/commands; Mark read two taps deep |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist | 3 | Quiet; search form over unrelated Inbox list |\n| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Good failure copy + Activity; swipe-setting failure shows wrong value |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 2 | Disclosures good; no gesture/scope teaching |\nHalves: A1 25, A2 25. Last round's five priority issues did not recur.\n\n## Design specificity\nAuthored voice, borrowed form (both reviewers). Detector: source clean except design-system-radius advisory (FixtureTransitionGate.vue:115); rendered inbox 412x915: tight-leading x18 (.row-preview line-height 1.25, list.css:79) true; text-occlusion x4 false positives. No overlay (headless).\n\n## Priority issues\n1. [P1] Disabled reader controls indistinguishable from enabled (reader.css:107-110 vs style.css:309 both --icon-muted); reader Back 40px (shell.css:308-315). polish.\n2. [P1] Swipes active during selection mode (InboxList.vue onRowPointerDown has no selecting guard); fling commits at 64px before 128px label. harden.\n3. [P1] Swipe setting save failure leaves tapped radio checked (SwipeActionSettings.vue:13-22). harden.\n4. [P1] Silent endings: Undo has no deadline cue and the settled notice vanishes with no handoff (A1); editor X gives no \"draft kept\" confirmation, empty drafts kept (A2). Tension with owner's \"end quietly\" choice. clarify.\n5. [P2] Search form shown over the Inbox list; example placeholder reads as an applied query (App.vue:2354). distill.\n\n## Persona red flags\nAlex: fling before verb; palette Mark done target unnamed. Casey: top-corner Menu/Select/X; Reply pill 12px above Star; no Copy text confirmation; silent disappearance. Sam: selection hides read-state cue; selected-row paperclip ~2.75:1; clipped checkbox focusable. Jordan: Done as status; Unread persists, Mark read in More; placeholder as query. Riley: reader subject clipped at 3 lines (reader.css:9-17, repeat); toast label unclamped; Copy text failure only greys the row.\n\n## Minor observations\nPreview leading 1.25; lavender 3-4x per reader screen; radios browser blue; settings note louder than parent; 60-option minute select; More sheet dividers (Files and links no group, App.vue:898); reply quote \"Plain text only.…\"; Refresh reminders reads as text; Contact recent rows no dates; drawer index===8, no close; palette 9 commands; reminder picker verbose/out of order, Schedule disabled until Enter; dock height not in scroll clearance (inferred).\n\n## Questions\nUnread word as the Mark read control? Down-chevron instead of X? Do Previous/Next earn two dock slots?\nEOF\nIMPECCABLE_CRITIQUE_META='{\"target\":\"phone layout key screens (src/assets/mobile)\",\"total_score\":25,\"max_score\":40,\"na_heuristics\":\"\",\"p0_count\":0,\"p1_count\":4}' /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable critique-storage write src/assets/mobile $S/crit3-body.md 2>&1 | tail -1; rm -f $S/crit3-body.md; /home/exedev/.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable critique-storage trend src/assets/mobile 5 2>&1 | grep -oE '\"total_score\": ?[0-9]+' | tr '\\n' ' '","description":"Persist round-3 critique snapshot and read trend"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7386,"cache_read_input_tokens":453665,"output_tokens":1837,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1837,"cache_read_input_tokens":453665,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":14288,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SufHknDCiq4rHLyiPxG11z":{"command":"cd /home/exedev/email-os-mobile-validate && S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-exedev-email-os/415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b/scratchpad; cat > $S/crit3-body.md <<'EOF'\nMethod: three isolated sub-agents (A1 GPT-6.2-SOL list · A2 Opus 5.5 reader/editors/pages · B GPT-6.2-Astra detector). Commit ac939a3.\n\n## Design Health Score: 25/40 (Acceptable)\n| # | Heuristic | Score | Key issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 3 | Exact receipts; no Undo deadline; editor X confirms nothing |\n| 2 | Match system / real world | 2 | \"Done\" reads as status; ^/v read as scroll; lo