{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","id":"efa02c3b-d695-4f87-82b3-629d5bbd2089","timestamp":"2026-11-18T06:03:00.474Z","version":"2.1.326","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"79e0fdfbf43898e250795693e770e3b9381ea13553ab3d06d07fc5408a31198c","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"5a5fb343-ce74-4e24-91ce-074f2cc991fc","keep":633,"tail":["54a9a6186bbdb93d3ba17ac267b311d6d932c9f20915f714dcd41b314d8ac8fd","bc236dcbc0711d1831f655f38067751055e0605e0e4ba3d473d0dfda6379c504"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",633,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",634,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f59d356b376f05caf22e00c8dba4767fdff553983f290b81d7c43abd488f905d"}
{"parentUuid":"adc8bdfd-f913-469b-8ca3-ee259542598d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9tPjM6QgRH9Wowhsb21","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both rounds are done. The changes from the second critique are built and merged. The third critique, by GPT-6.2-SOL, Opus 5.5 and GPT-6.2-Astra, scored 25/40 again; that report and its findings are in the messages above. PR #80 is still waiting for your review.\n\n**What the GPT-6.2-SOL threads built** (three PRs, all merged into `mobile/integration`):\n- **#87:**\n  - A finished action's notice now leaves when its Undo window ends. Failed or unknown outcomes stay on screen and get an \"Activity\" button.\n  - The swipe cue now follows the same rule as the commit, and the swipe icon follows the action set in Settings.\n- **#88:** the reader's done button shows \"Done\" / \"Not done\" next to its tick. Contact has 48px rows, always-visible copy buttons and a \"Find mail from sender\" action.\n- **#89:** a Select button in the top bar starts selection with nothing selected. The bar reads \"1 of 18 selected\" and \"Select 18 loaded\", with 48px buttons.\n\n**Checks on the merged branch (ac939a3):**\n- 2,042 unit tests pass, plus typecheck and build. 86 browser layout tests pass, 6 are skipped (screenshot and opt-in files), and CI passes.\n- On the emulator I confirmed each change above. Back clears a selection and stays in the app.\n\nI reviewed the threads' screenshots and sent back three fixes. \"Find mail from sender\" had a broken border. The selection count read \"1 of 17 loaded\". And one selection screenshot was a duplicate.\n\nOne thread stopped twice on permission prompts that I can't approve here; restarting its turn got it going.\n\n**Why the score didn't move:** none of the earlier issues came back. Each run's reviewers found finer problems, and one of them was caused by my own round-2 change.\n\n**Next round, based on your answers.** Endings stay silent, so that P1 drops out. That leaves four items, in this order:\n1. **`/impeccable distill`:** the search form stops sitting over the Inbox list. The list stays hidden until a search runs, and the placeholder becomes \"Search mail\", with the example moved into Search syntax.\n2. **`/impeccable polish`:** live and disabled reader buttons look different (live in `--text-secondary`; disabled in `--icon-muted` at reduced opacity), and the reader's Back button becomes 48px.\n3. **`/impeccable harden`:**\n   - Swipes are off while a selection is active.\n   - Arming and committing a swipe use one distance rule, so a fast fling can't act before its label shows.\n4. **`/impeccable harden`:** a failed swipe-setting save puts the radio back. The failure message names the swipe direction, sits beside its group, and says which option is still in effect.\n5. **`/impeccable polish`:** a final pass, then screenshots, the emulator check and a PR #80 update.\n\nYou can ask me to run these one at a time, all at once, or in any order you prefer. I'd split them across GPT-6.2-SOL threads as in this round. Item 1 touches different files from the rest, so it can run in parallel with them.\n\nRe-run `/impeccable critique` after fixes to see your score improve."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":553,"cache_read_input_tokens":465098,"output_tokens":1073,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":553,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":465098,"cache_creation_input_tokens":553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":553},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[