{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"415cd333-37f5-4cfe-be88-ad6fe867d94b","id":"cb7d82bf-d009-40a9-a71f-e7a296893531","timestamp":"2026-11-18T06:04:11.007Z","version":"2.1.326","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"79e0fdfbf43898e250795693e770e3b9381ea13553ab3d06d07fc5408a31198c","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"50e85fd7-9794-4324-b2ef-c66c257689fa","keep":637,"tail":["2059ae5536c279aa3cb6b0ec0443d512e37eb167d5c4b22f4c04a6bf70164255","012755dccf33b2be9d412bd626967d22ff3f629db54b906635426d353610b10e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",637,"content",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",638,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"e1dd0f8495baa04acec63fc7a3c086138f7f4c1004ccf6a1ee38b9c3d01757e6"}
{"parentUuid":"248ac1ad-01f9-45c4-a03f-0a20f22d6667","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9tUww2AuCVerNPiBoZR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0131K6ZoqrCk7TMeXFdnBbfV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review; mkdir -p $R/p7-search $R/p7-controls; sed -i 's/Read `\\/home\\/exedev\\/email-os-mobile-review\\/P6-RULES.md`/&/' $R/P6-RULES.md; cat >> $R/P6-RULES.md <<'EOF'\n\nPermissions: you run with full access. Never request escalated or sandbox-bypass permissions (nobody can approve them here and you will stall). Keep temporary files inside your worktree (e.g. under `.git/`), not in `/tmp`. Pass PR bodies inline or from a file inside the worktree.\nEOF\ncat > $R/p7-search/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p7 track D: the search form stops posing over the Inbox\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first (same rules apply to p7). Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p7-search/`.\n\nBackground (design critique 2026-11-17, owner's first priority): on the phone, opening Search shows the search form (`<form class=\"mail-search\">` in `src/App.vue`, around line 2354) above whatever list was current. In `search.png` that is the Inbox, with no caption, while the top bar says \"Search\" and the bottom nav marks Search current. The placeholder `from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice` sits over Ada's \"weekly status\" rows, so the Inbox reads as results of a query that was never run.\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p7-search origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Hide the underlying list while the form is open on a non-search context. In compact mode, when `searchVisible` is true and `mailbox.context.value !== 'search'`, the list below the form is not shown (not just covered): no rows, no month caption, no list empty state, no split pill (already hidden), no selection bar. Prefer a template condition or a class on the central column (e.g. `searching-form`) with a compact CSS rule in `pages.css` (`display: none` on the list scroller), whichever keeps the InboxList mounted state and scroll position intact for when the form closes (closing the form with Escape/Back must return to the same list at the same scroll position and focused row). When the context already is `search` (results shown) and the user reopens the form to edit the query, the results stay visible below the form as today. Regular layout unchanged. The space below the form shows only what the form already renders (suggestions / recent queries if any, the Search syntax disclosure). App-level tests in `tests/layout/mobile-app.test.ts`: open the form from Inbox → no conversation rows rendered/visible; close it → rows back and the previously focused row still focused; open the form from search results → results still visible. Rendered assertion in the pages/search rendered test at 412×915: with the form open from Inbox, no `.inbox-row` is visible (zero boxes or `display:none` ancestor). Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run tests/layout tests/search` and the rendered file pass.\n\n- [ ] 3. Plain placeholder; example inside the syntax help. In compact mode only, the input placeholder is `Search mail`. The example query `from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice` becomes the first line of the compact Search syntax list, written as \"Example: from:ada \"weekly status\" -invoice\" in `var(--text-secondary)` with the query part in the same monospace/code style the list already uses for operators (check how `#search-help` items render operators). Regular layout keeps today's placeholder and list. Unit test: compact placeholder is \"Search mail\" and the example line is the first item inside the compact disclosure; regular unchanged. Check: `pnpm vitest run tests/layout tests/search`.\n\n- [ ] 4. One left edge for the form. In compact mode the input's text start, the \"Cached mail only\" checkbox and the \"Search syntax\" summary chevron align on the page inset (20px start inset, the same as list rows): measure in a rendered assertion at 412×915 and 360×800 that the input's left padding edge, the checkbox's left edge and the summary's left edge are within 2px of each other and of the page inset; the Search button keeps at least 48×48. Re-run the screenshots into this track's directory (`search.png`, `search-results.png` at least). Check: the rendered file passes and both screenshots exist.\n\n- [ ] 5. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` if it moved. `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" search sentence(s) (state, not history). Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: search form stands alone\", body with what changed and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\ncat > $R/p7-controls/PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# p7 track E: live controls look live; swipes respect selection; settings never show an unsaved value\n\nRead `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/P6-RULES.md` first (same rules apply to p7). Screenshots go to `/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review/p7-controls/`.\n\nBackground (design critique 2026-11-17, all confirmed in code):\n- Disabled reader toolbar buttons look exactly like enabled ones: `src/assets/mobile/reader.css` sets `.mobile-reader-actions .reader-actions > button:disabled { opacity: 1; color: var(--icon-muted) }` and resting `.header-glyph` is also `var(--icon-muted)` (`style.css` around line 309); touch has no hover, so they never differ. The reader's Back button (`.mobile-back-host > .reader-back`, `shell.css` around 308–315) is 40×40 while other round buttons are 48×48.\n- Swipes still start while a selection is active: `onRowPointerDown` in `src/components/InboxList.vue` calls `swipeFor(row).pointerdown` with no `selecting` guard, so a swipe can mark a different conversation done while a set is selected.\n- A fast fling commits at 64px (velocity rule in `src/composables/useSwipeAction.ts`, shared `wouldCommit`), but the label only appears at 128px.\n- `src/components/SwipeActionSettings.vue`: when `saveSwipePreferences` fails it sets \"Could not save\" and returns, but the radio the user tapped stays checked (the `:checked` binding did not change, so Vue does not patch it) while the old preference stays in effect. `ReminderSettings.vue` on the same page restores the confirmed value correctly.\n\nNote: the owner decided that endings stay silent (no Undo countdown, no \"Draft kept\" notice). Do not add those.\n\n- [ ] 1. Branch: `git fetch origin && git switch -c mobile/p7-controls origin/mobile/integration`; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed. Check: `pnpm typecheck` passes.\n\n- [ ] 2. Live vs disabled in the reader toolbar (compact only). Enabled toolbar glyph buttons use `color: var(--text-secondary)`; disabled ones use `color: var(--icon-muted)` with `opacity: 0.4`. The labelled Done/Not done button keeps its accent colour when enabled and follows the disabled rule when disabled. Keep the existing `header-glyph-held` exemption (a held button during the sub-120ms conversation swap must not flash to disabled). Do the same for the reader Back button, and make it 48×48 with a 24px glyph like `.mobile-round-button`. Rendered assertions in the reader rendered test at 412×915: on the first conversation the Previous button is disabled and its computed opacity is ≤ 0.5 while Next (enabled) has opacity 1 and a different computed colour; the Back button is 48×48. Re-run `reader.png` into this track's directory. Check: the rendered file passes.\n\n- [ ] 3. No swipes while selecting. In `InboxList.vue` `onRowPointerDown`, do not start a swipe when `selecting.value` is true (the long-press/tap selection handling continues to work). If a swipe is in progress when selection starts (long-press fires), cancel it: reset its offset/armed/revealed state without committing. Unit tests: with selection active, a horizontal drag past the commit distance does not emit archive/remind and leaves the row in place; outside selection the same drag still commits. Check: `pnpm vitest run <InboxList tests> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 4. One distance for arming and committing. In `useSwipeAction.ts`, replace the velocity exception with a single distance rule used by both the armed cue and the release: `Math.max(128, rowWidth * 0.35)`. Remove the velocity-based commit entirely (a quick short flick no longer commits; a release below the threshold returns the row). Keep reduced-motion behaviour and the 160ms exit for committed done swipes. Update the unit tests (fast 80px drag: not armed, does not commit; slow drag past the threshold: armed and commits) and the rendered swipe test expectations if they relied on velocity. Re-run the swipe screenshots into this track's directory. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <useSwipeAction tests> tests/layout` and the swipe rendered test pass.\n\n- [ ] 5. Settings never show an unsaved swipe choice. In `SwipeActionSettings.vue`, on a failed save: restore the radio group to the confirmed value (e.g. switch the radios to a `v-model` on a local per-side ref that is reset to the confirmed preference on failure, or set the tapped input's `checked` back and force a re-render), and show the message in a `role=\"status\"` line directly under that side's legend, worded \"Could not save swipe {right|left}. Still: {current option label}.\" in `var(--danger)`. On success that side's line reads \"Saved\" (secondary colour) and the other side's line is cleared. Unit tests: simulate `saveSwipePreferences` returning false → the previously confirmed radio is checked again, the tapped one is not, the message names the side and the still-active option; success → \"Saved\" under that side only. Check: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm vitest run <the SwipeActionSettings / settings tests> tests/layout`.\n\n- [ ] 6. Final. Merge `origin/mobile/integration` if it moved (another track edits `App.vue` and `pages.css`; keep both sides). `pnpm typecheck`, full `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, the full rendered suite, the screenshots. Update `DESIGN.md` \"Compact layout (phone)\" (reader toolbar live/disabled states and 48px Back; swipes off during selection; single swipe distance; swipe settings failure behaviour), state not history. Open the pull request, title \"Mobile: honest controls in the reader, swipes and settings\", body with what changed per item and the test counts. Write the URL under this item.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write p7 checklists and add permission rule"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_read_input_tokens":466731,"output_tokens":3850,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":960,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3850,"cache_read_input_tokens":466731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":960},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":34047,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0131K6ZoqrCk7TMeXFdnBbfV":{"command":"R=/home/exedev/email-os-mobile-review; mkdir -p $R/p7-search $R/p7-controls; sed -i 's/Read `\\/home\\/exedev\\/email-os-mobile-review\\/P6-RULES.md`/&/' $R/P6-RULES.md; cat >> $R/P6-RULES.md <<'EOF'\n\nPermissions: you run with full access. Never request escalated or sandbox-bypass permissions (nobody can approve them here and you will stall). Keep temporary files inside your worktree (e.g. under `.git/`), not in `/tmp`. Pass PR bodies